2 CONT
2 CONT BONIFAZIO di Caretto, son of --- di Caretto & his wife --- (-after Feb 1285, bur Ponto Santa Maria).  Marchese di Caretto.  The testament of "Bonifacius marchio de Carreto", dated Feb 1285, elected burial at "ecclesiæ S. Mariæ de 
2 CONC Ponto", named "Vallierminus frater meus", made bequests to "Percivallio de Lavania cognato meo…Aloysiæ de Canellis domicellæ Caracossæ uxoris meæ…sororis prædicti D. Percevalli…Simoneta filia mea…pro ipsa maritanda…Alazina filia m
2 CONC ea…pro ea maritanda…Gullielmum Danielem, Ottobonum et Percivallium filios meos…in custodia…D. Percivalli eorum avunculi et prædictæ Caracossæ mater eorum…Leonem filium meum et alios filios meos naturales…Conradum et Oddonum…Leone…
2 CONC Manuelluxium…Aloysium" and bequeathed "castri et loci Bublii…quæ fuit quondam D. Oddi marchionis de Carretto avi mei" to "Friderico Simplici de Rocchetta et Henrico fratre suo atque…Jacobino filio comitis Bartolomei fratris prædic
2 CONC torum Friderici et Henrici"[1168]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' as her second husband, CARACOSA Fiesco, widow of BONIFAZIO Grimaldi, daughter of TEODORO Fiesco Conte di Lavagna & his wife Simone --- (-after Feb 1285).  The testament of "Bonifacius marchio de Carreto", dated Feb 1285, m
2 CONC ade bequests to "Percivallio de Lavania cognato meo…Aloysiæ de Canellis domicellæ Caracossæ uxoris meæ…sororis prædicti D. Percevalli…"[1169]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bonifazio & his wife had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *1.         GUGLIELMO DANIELO (-after Feb 1285).  The testament of "Bonifacius marchio de Carreto", dated Feb 1285, made bequests to "…Gullielmum Danielem, Ottobonum et Percivallium filios meos…in custodia…D. Percivalli eorum avun
2 CONC culi et prædictæ Caracossæ mater eorum…"[1170]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *2.         OTTOBUONO (-after Feb 1285).  The testament of "Bonifacius marchio de Carreto", dated Feb 1285, made bequests to "…Gullielmum Danielem, Ottobonum et Percivallium filios meos…in custodia…D. Percivalli eorum avunculi et 
2 CONC prædictæ Caracossæ mater eorum…"[1171]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *3.         PERCEVALLE (-after Feb 1285).  The testament of "Bonifacius marchio de Carreto", dated Feb 1285, made bequests to "…Gullielmum Danielem, Ottobonum et Percivallium filios meos…in custodia…D. Percivalli eorum avunculi et
2 CONC  prædictæ Caracossæ mater eorum…"[1172]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *4.         SIMONETA (-after Feb 1285).  The testament of "Bonifacius marchio de Carreto", dated Feb 1285, made bequests to "…Simoneta filia mea…pro ipsa maritanda…Alazina filia mea…pro ea maritanda…"[1173]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *5.         ALESSINA (-after Feb 1285).  The testament of "Bonifacius marchio de Carreto", dated Feb 1285, made bequests to "…Simoneta filia mea…pro ipsa maritanda…Alazina filia mea…pro ea maritanda…"[1174]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bonifazio had five illegitimate children by unknown mistresses: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *6.          LEO (-after Feb 1285).  The testament of "Bonifacius marchio de Carreto", dated Feb 1285, made bequests to "…Leonem filium meum et alios filios meos naturales…Conradum et Oddonum…Leone…Manuelluxium…Aloysium"[1175]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *7.          CORRADO (-after Feb 1285).  The testament of "Bonifacius marchio de Carreto", dated Feb 1285, made bequests to "…Leonem filium meum et alios filios meos naturales…Conradum et Oddonum…Leone…Manuelluxium…Aloysium"[1176]
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT *8.          OTTONE (-after Feb 1285).  The testament of "Bonifacius marchio de Carreto", dated Feb 1285, made bequests to "…Leonem filium meum et alios filios meos naturales…Conradum et Oddonum…Leone…Manuelluxium…Aloysium"[1177].
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT *9.          EMMANUELE (-after Feb 1285).  The testament of "Bonifacius marchio de Carreto", dated Feb 1285, made bequests to "…Leonem filium meum et alios filios meos naturales…Conradum et Oddonum…Leone…Manuelluxium…Aloysium"[117
2 CONC 8]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *10.       LUIGI (-after Feb 1285).  The testament of "Bonifacius marchio de Carreto", dated Feb 1285, made bequests to "…Leonem filium meum et alios filios meos naturales…Conradum et Oddonum…Leone…Manuelluxium…Aloysium"[1179]. 
