2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         '''BEATRICE di Monferrato''' .  The late 13th/14th century Vida of the poet Raimbaut de Vaqueiras describes Beatrice as sister of Bonifazio Marchese di Monferrato married to "Enric del Caret"[177].  However, Raimbaut de
2 CONC  Vaqueiras himself calls her "filha del marques" in the famous 'Carros', 'Truan, mala guerra', composed in [1200/01], which emphasises her youth[178].  The identity of her husband "Enric del Caret" has not been established, assumi
2 CONC ng that the marriages of Enrico [II] di Caretto are correct as shown below in this document.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' [ENRICO di Caretto, son of ---]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Beatrice''', married Enrico del Carretto, Marquis of Savona, as the second of his three wives;
2 CONT /!\ she is the ''Bel Cavalher (Fair Knight)'' of [https://www.geni.com/people/Rambaldo-di-Vaqueiras/6000000108007437822 Vaqueiras]'s songs, composed in the 1190s.
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boniface_I,_Marquis_of_Montferrat
2 CONT
2 CONT  - - - - - - - - - - - 
2 CONT
2 CONT /!\ ''{but her [https://www.geni.com/people/NN-di-Monferrato/6000000222396583971 aunt] would seem to be the best candidate }
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
