2 CONT Sir '''Robert II''' (died 15 February 1286),[7][1] son of William II and Joan, had by 1248 inherited his father's manor of Perching in the West Sussex parish of Fulking and in 1260 acquired two-thirds of the neighbouring manor of 
2 CONC Fulking, with the reversion of the other third. In 1264 he was licensed to enclose his manor house at Perching with a ditch and a stone wall, and to crenellate it, so marking the origin of Perching Castle. In 1281 he acquired furt
2 CONC her land in Perching and in 1284 was reported as holding the whole settlement.[22] In 1248 he also obtained a grant of free warren in his demesne lands of Addington and in 1270 licence to embattle his house there.[21] In 1267 he s
2 CONC erved as Sheriff of Surrey & Sussex and was Keeper of Guildford Castle. After 1265 he was granted lands at Berwick, East Sussex, taken from the rebel William Marmion, and was Keeper of Arundel Castle during the minority of its hei
2 CONC r in 1272. In 1274 he did service at the coronation of King Edward I. After his second marriage to a rich widow, he acquired more landholdings: Portslade in Sussex and Wendover in Buckinghamshire, both in 1270,[23] together with S
2 CONC tapleford in Hertfordshire, where in 1285 he held both manor and advowson.[24] He first married by August 1256 Joan, widow of Sir John Mohun (died 1253) and daughter of William de Ferrers, 5th Earl of Derby and his first wife Siby
2 CONC l Marshal. After her death before October 1267, he married Margaret, widow of Baldwin de Redvers, 7th Earl of Devon, and daughter of Count Thomas II of Savoy and his second wife Beatrice of Fieschi. Margaret was a first cousin of 
2 CONC Queen Eleanor of Provence and a grand-niece of Pope Innocent VI. She died shortly before 14 May 1292. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  His daughter and heiress, from his first marriage to Joan, was:
2 CONT *Isabel (born 25 March 1258 - died before 28 May 1323), who married Hugh, 1st Baron Bardolf.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Aguillon was born circa 1226 at Watton at Stone, Hertfordshire, England. He was Christened at Perching of Addington, Surrey, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aguillon of Addington, Surrey, England 
2 CONT
