1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beatrice_of_Viennois
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice was born in 1160 in Vienne, France, the second child of Géraud I of Mâcon (son of William III of Mâcon) and Maurette de Salins. She was descended from the House of Mâcon and had seven siblings.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Humbert III, Count of Savoy's third wife, Clementia of Zähringen, in 1175, Humbert was inconsolable and refused to remarry; however, he had no male heir. His advisers persuaded him to wed Beatrice the following 
2 CONC year.[1] Beatrice gave birth to Thomas, Count of Savoy in 1178.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice died in 1230 in Champagne-et-Fontaine, Aquitaine, France.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BURGUNDIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#BeatrixMacondied1230<br/>
2 CONT 6.         BEATRIX de Vienne (-8 Apr 1230).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to one of the unnamed sisters of "comitem Guilelmum Matisconensem sive Viennensem et Galterum de Salins et quemdam Gerardum et Stephan
2 CONC um Bisuntinensem electum" as mother of "comes Thomas de Sabaudia"[256].  The primary source which confirms her name has not been identified.  "Thomas…Mauriannensis comes et marchio Italiæ" confirmed the donations made by "pater me
2 CONC us…[et] domini comitis Humberti…abavi mei" to the canons of Saint-Jean de Maurienne, with the advice of "B. matris mee et…tutore meo Bonifacio marchione Montisferrati", by charter dated 12 Jun 1189[257].  The necrology of Hautecom
2 CONC be records the death of "Beatrix comitissa" 8 Apr 1230[258].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ([1175]) as his fourth wife, HUMBERT III Comte de Maurienne et de Savoie, son of AMEDEE III Comte de Maurienne et de Savoie & his wife Mathilde d'Albon [Viennois] (Avigliana 4 Aug 1136-Chambéry 4 Mar 1189, bur Abbaye de Ha
2 CONC utecombe).   
2 CONT
