2 CONT After his father's death in 1209, Ramón Berenguer IV, Count of Provence and Forcalquier, was imprisoned in the castle of Monzón, in Aragon, until he was able to escape in 1219 and claim his inheritance. He was a powerful and energ
2 CONC etic ruler who added Forcalquier to his domain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Giovanni Villani in his Nuova Cronica had this to say about Raymond: "Count Raymond was a lord of gentle lineage, and kin to them of the house of Aragon, and to the family of the count of Toulouse. By inheritance Provence, this si
2 CONC de of the Rhone, was his; a wise and courteous lord was he, and of noble state and virtuous, and in his time did honorable deeds, and to his court came all gentle persons of Provence and of France and of Catalonia, by reason of hi
2 CONC s courtesy and noble estate, and he made many Provençal coblas and canzoni of great worth."
2 CONT
2 CONT See http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramon_Berenguer_IV,_Count_of_Provence for more information.
