2 CONT GUILLAUME de Grandson (-[1386]).  The 29 Mar 1340 testament of Louis [II] de Savoie Comte de Vaud names his nephew Otto de Grandson, Guillaume his brother and his sisters[814].  "Ysabella de Scabellione domina Novicastri relicta…d
2 CONC omini Ludovici de Sabaudia domini Vaudi" granted rights in her lands to "consanguineorum nostrorum Guilliermi de Grandissono et Ioannis dominorum Albone" by charter dated 13 Jun 1352[815].  Seigneur de Sainte-Croix [Vaud], de Cudr
2 CONC efin, de Grandcour et Aubonne [Vaud][816].  Amédée VI Comte de Savoie granted the seigneurie d’Aubonne to Guillaume de Grandson Seigneur de Sainte-Croix in 1365[817].  Rodolphe [IV] Comte de Gruyére sold his rights to the seigneur
2 CONC ie d’Aubonne to Guillaume de Grandson Seigneur de Sainte-Croix in 1370 for 2000 florins[818].  Guillaume de Grandson Seigneur de Sainte-Croix et d’Aubonne donated property to Lance convent, for the souls of “lui, de son père, de s
2 CONC a mère, de sa sœur dame de la Tour, de son...oncle de bonne mémoire Othon seigneur de Grandson et de dame Jehanne de Vienne son épouse décédée” by charter dated 23 Jan 1372[819].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m JEANNE de Vienne, daughter of JEAN de Vienne & his wife [Catherine de Jonvelle] (-before 23 Jan 1372).  Coudriet & Châtelet name “une fille...Jeanne qui épousa Guillaume de Granson-Sainte-Croix” as the child of Jean de Vienne an
2 CONC d his wife Catherine[820].  Père Anselme names her “dame de Vaugrenan” and her husband “Guillaume de Grançon surnommé le Grand”[821].  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not been identified.  Guillaum
2 CONC e de Grandson Seigneur de Sainte-Croix et d’Aubonne donated property to Lance convent, for the souls of “...de dame Jehanne de Vienne son épouse décédée” by charter dated 23 Jan 1372[822].  Guillaume & his wife had three children:
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         OTHON de Grandson (-Bourg 7 Aug 1397).  Seigneur de Sainte-Croix.  Accused of involvement in the death of Amédée VII Comte de Savoie in 1391, his properties were confiscated[823].  Bonne de Bourbon regent of Savoy confi
2 CONC scated Aubonne from Othon de Grandson in 1393 and enfeoffed Rodolphe de Gruyère Seigneur de Vaugrenant with the seigneurie for 14000 gold florins 4 Nov 1393[824].  He was killed by Gérard d’Estavayer in a trial by combat[825].  m 
2 CONC (1365) JEANNE Alamandi, daughter of HUMBERT Alamandi Seigneur d’Aubonne & his wife Agnes de Joinville-Gex (-after 2 Oct 1404).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         GUILLAUME de Grandson (-[late Aug] 1381).  m as her first husband, JEANNE de Saint-Dizier Dame de Roche-sur-Marne et de la Fauche, daughter of HENRI de Saint-Dizier Seigneur de Roche-sur-Marne & his wife Marguerite de J
2 CONC oinville Dame de la Fauche (-after 18 Aug 1408).  Documents dated Sep 1381 record that “Messire Renaut de Mello et sa femme, auparavant femme de Messire Hue de Grand” claimed against “Messire Eudes de Savoisy et Marguerite de Dong
2 CONC eux sa femme fille de feu Messire Oger de Dongeux Seigneur de la Fauche, et Madame Ieanne de S. Disier fille de ladite Marguerite et de feu Henry de Saint Disier son premier mary...ores veuve de feu Guillaume de Grançon”, noting t
2 CONC hat her [Jeanne’s] father died 1376 “environ Noel” and that her husband had died “il n y a pas trois sepmaines”[826].  She married secondly (before 14 Mar 1388) Jacques de Vergy.  She married thirdly (1398) Gaucher Seigneur de Sav
2 CONC oisy.  She married fourthly (before 13 Aug 1401) Ferry de Chardoigne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)         THOMAS de Grandson .  Perchet records that “Thomas chevalier...se fixa en Angleterre” but does not cite the source which confirms this information[827]. 
2 CONT =---------------------------=
