2 CONT  Emperor Friedrich II had one illegitimate daughter by Mistress (4):
2 CONT
2 CONT 11.       CATERINA da Marano ([1216/18]-after 1272).  The Annales Placentini Gibellini record the marriage in 1247 of "imperator filiam suam" and "Iacomino de Careto"[736].  The Thomas Tusci Gesta Imperatorum et Pontificum refers 
2 CONC to the wife of "Ubertino marchioni de Carreto" as full sister of "Hentius"[737].  The primary source which confirms her first marriage has not yet been identified.   The testament of “Henricus...rex Sardinie”, dated 16 Mar 1272, b
2 CONC equeathed property to “dominam nostram Catharinam de Marrano...sororem nostram...domini Federigi Romanorum imperatoris filiam”[738].  
2 CONT
