2 CONT i)          LAZARINO (-end May 1393).   A charter dated 20 Mar 1385 records a dispute between the commune of Genoa and “dominos Lazarinum et Karolum marchiones de Carreto natos quondam domini Georgiii...et vice Georgini nepotis ip
2 CONC sorum nati quondam domini Enriceti...et...dominum Manuelem marchionem de Cravexana filium quondam domini Frederici et domum Iohannem de Saluciis marchionem de Cravexana...dominos Georginum Guiraldum Cristoforum et Iacobum marchion
2 CONC es de Ceva...dominus Guillelmus marchio Ceve miles filius domini Georgini procurator...dominorum Manuelis et Antonii marchionum de Carreto” concerning their fiefs, and a settlement agreed by “dominis Manuele de Carreto quondam dom
2 CONC ini Enrici et Anthonio filio quondam domini Alarami de Carreto nepote dicti domini Manuelis...cum filiis et heredibus quondam Enriceti marchionis de Carreto fratris ipsorum dominorum Lazarini et Carolli...cum dominis Manuel marchi
2 CONC one de Cravexana quondam domini Frederici et Iohanne de Saluciis marchione Cravexane” and by “dominus Carolus de Carreto ex marchionibus Saone...et...Lazarinum de Carreto marchionem Saone fratrem suum...”, by charter dated 13 Jan 
2 CONC 1385[1244].  Marchese di Noli e Finale: “Dominorum Manuelis quondam domini Enrici et Antonii filii quondam domini Alerami marchionum de Carreto...marchiones Savone et Cravexane”, implementing an arbitration dated 16 Apr 1385, exch
2 CONC anged “dimidia marchionatiis Cravexane” for “medietatem...castrorum Finarii” with “dominum Manuelem quondam domini Frederici marchionis de Cravexana” by charter dated 19 Apr 1385[1245], and transferred the interest in Finali to “d
2 CONC ominis Lazarino et Carolo marchionibus de Carreto” by charter dated 20 Apr 1385[1246].  “Dominum Lazarinum marchioniem de Carreto” bought his share in “castri...Finarii” from “dominum Karolum...frat[rem suum]” by charter dated 13 
2 CONC Apr 1390[1247].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' MARIETTA, daughter of ---.  A charter dated 24 May 1395 reviews longstanding disputes relating to “Castrumfranchum” between the commune of Genoa, including with “dominam Marietam uxorem quondam dicti domini Lazarini ac dom
2 CONC inum Lazarinum natum ipsius et dicti quondam domini Lazarini, nec non dominum Georginum natum quondam domini Enrici marchionis de Carreto”, and reproduces a document dated 7 Aug 1394 (“domina Marieta de Carreto uxor quondam...mili
2 CONC tis domini Lazarini de Carreto marchionis Saone tutrix testamentaria Nicolai Antonii et Lodisii filiorum [ipsius]”)[1248]. -         MARCHESI di NOLI e FINALE. 
