2 CONT 6.         GUY de la Tour (-24 Feb 1250, bur Lyon Dominican church).  His parentage is confirmed by the following document: the testament of “Siboud seigneur de Beauvoir[-de-Marc]”, dated 23 Jul 1242, ordered the restoration of he
2 CONC r dowry to “son épouse S., à la décision de Guy archidiacre de Lyon et de son frère A[lbert] seigneur de la Tour”[2161].  '''Archdeacon of Lyon'''.  “Hugo...Claromontanus episcopus et Humbertus dominus Bellijoci, et Arbertus domin
2 CONC us de Turre, et Guido archidiaconus Lugdunensis, et Arbertus de Turre, et Hugo senescalcus Lugdunensis fratres” agreed an alliance under a charter dated Sep 1246[2162].  The testament of “G. de Turre archidiaconus Lugdunensis”, da
2 CONC ted 24 Feb 1249 (O.S.), chose burial “in domo Fratrum Predicatorum Lugdunensium...juxta matrem meam”, bequeathed property to “Hugonem senescalcum Lugdunensem...Humberti nepoti meo...frater suus...nepotem meum Albertum...”[2163].  
2 CONC The necrology of Lyon records the death 24 Feb 1249 (O.S.) of “Guy de la Tour archidiacre de...Lyon”[2164].
