1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkbresse.htm#HumbertIVMontlueldied1289
2 CONT
2 CONT HUMBERT de Montluel, son of PIERRE [I] Seigneur de Montluel & his wife --- (-after Apr 1289).  Seigneur de Montluel.  Humbert Seigneur de Montluel confirmed donations to l’Île Barbe made by “Humbert jadis seigneur de Montluel et s
2 CONC on Pierre jadis seigneur de Montluel, aïeul et père dudit seigneur de Montluel” by charter dated Apr 1256[367].  A charter dated Jan 1266 records the agreement between “Guidonem dominum Castillionis en Chotaigny” and “Humbertum do
2 CONC minum Montis Lupelli fratrum” to divide the inheritance from “Petri domini Montis Luppelli eorum patris”[368].  “Humbertus dominus Montislupelli” granted privileges to Montluel, with the consent of “...domini nostri...Humberti dom
2 CONC ini de Turre et de Cologniaco...Guidonis de Montelupello domini de Castellione in Chautagnia...fratris [nostri]...domine Alasie domine Montislupelli uxoris nostre”, by charter dated Mar 1276[369].  An inscription in the church of 
2 CONC Montluel St Barthélemy records the church’s foundation in 1289 by “dominum Humbertum dominum Montislupelli et...dominam Alaysiam de Turre eius uxorem”[370].  “Guido de Montelupello domicellus dominus Coloniaci et Margareta eius ux
2 CONC or” granted privileges relating to “castrum suum seu villam de Coloniaco” by charter dated Apr 1289, witnessed by “Humbertus dominus de Toire et de Vilars, et Humbertus dominus Montislupelli et Stephanus de Coloniaco dominus d’And
2 CONC elost”[371]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ALIX de la Tour-du-Pin, daughter ALBERT [III] Seigneur de la Tour-du-Pin & his wife Beatrix de Coligny (-after 1289).  Her parentage is indicated by the presence of her brother Humbert in the Apr 1274 charter of her daught
2 CONC er Catherine (see below).  “Humbertus dominus Montislupelli” granted privileges to Montluel, with the consent of “...Guidonis de Montelupello domini de Castellione in Chautagnia...fratris [nostri]...domine Alasie domine Montislupe
2 CONC lli uxoris nostre”, by charter dated Mar 1276[372].  An inscription in the church of Montluel St Barthélemy records the church’s foundation in 1289 by “dominum Humbertum dominum Montislupelli et...dominam Alaysiam de Turre eius ux
2 CONC orem”[373]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Humbert [II] & his wife had three children: 
