1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matteo_I_Visconti   '' (ITA more info) [18 languages available] ''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Matteo I Visconti''' (1250–1322) was the second of the Milanese Visconti family to govern Milan.[1] Matteo was born to Teobaldo Visconti and Anastasia Pirovano.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1287, Matteo's uncle [https://www.geni.com/people/arcivescovo-Ottone-Visconti-signore-di-Milano/6000000008498629717 Ottone Visconti, archbishop and first lord of Milan], nominated him as ''capitano del popolo'' of Milan. Follow
2 CONC ing his uncle's death in 1295, he succeeded him as lord of Milan. Matteo was appointed numerous times as Imperial Vicar over the whole of Lombardy, while expanding, with the assistance of his sons, his sphere of influence to Piedm
2 CONC ont, Emilia, Bologna, and Genoa. Caught between the Papal and Imperial power struggle over northern Italy, Matteo would renounce his imperial title for "General Lord of the Milanese People". Found guilty on the charge of necromanc
2 CONC y, excommunicated, and facing a crusade, Matteo resigned his position and died months later. He was succeeded by his son Galeazzo I.
2 CONT
2 CONT #	[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matteo_I_Visconti#Life Life]  
2 CONT #	[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matteo_I_Visconti#Conflict_with_the_Church Conflict with the Church] 
2 CONT #	[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matteo_I_Visconti#Family Family]
2 CONT
