1 NOTE Manfred (c. 1231-66), king of Sicily, where he was born a natural son of the Emperor Frederick II. He reigned from 1258 until his death. He was excommunicated (1259) by Pope Alexander IV, but with his Saracens overran Tuscany, and
2 CONC  won the battle of Monte Aperto (1260). He subsequently met Charles of Anjou in battle and was killed. [World Wide Illustrated Encyclopedia, 1935]
