2 CONC Jewish books. Such legislation against the Talmud, not uncommon in the history of Christendom, was due to medieval courts' concerns that its production and circulation might weaken the faith of Christian individuals and threaten t
2 CONC he Christian basis of society, the protection of which was the duty of any Christian monarch
