1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Margaret (Plantagenet) of England, Queen Consort of Scotland=
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of''' Eleanor of Provence''' and '''Henry III, King of England'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret was married on 26 December 1251, at York Minster, to King '''Alexander III of Scotland''', with whom she had three children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Margaret, Princess of Scotland''' (1260/61–1283), who married Eirik II of Norway
2 CONT *''' Alexander, Prince of Scotland''' (21 January 1263 Jedburgh – 28 January 1283 Lindores Abbey); buried in Dunfermline Abbey
2 CONT *''' David of Scotland''' (20 March 1272 – June 1281 Stirling Castle); buried in Dunfermline Abbey
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret was unhappy in her married life as Queen Consort of Scotland. Her feeling of mistreatment  caused political tension between England and Scotland (Echols & Williams, p. 305).
2 CONT
