2 CONC tford, 2nd Earl Gloucester and Maud de Lacy, on 7 October 1272 at Chapel of Ruislip, Ruislip, Middlesex, England; No issue.1,3,4,5,6 Sir Edmund, 2nd Earl of Cornwall, Sheriff of Cornwall & Rutland and Margaret de Clare were divorc
2 CONC ed on 14 February 1294; Separated so she could "live in chastity."2,3,6 Sir Edmund, 2nd Earl of Cornwall, Sheriff of Cornwall & Rutland died circa 25 September 1300 at Abbey of Ashridge, Buckinghamshire, England.1,2,3,4,6 He was b
