1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1233 Pope Gregory IX took Hartmann IV in his protection in recognition of his efforts to exterminate the heretics. '''Hartman IV initially administered the Kyburg possessions together with his nephew Hartmann V 
2 CONC and founded the Dominican convent Töss near Winterthur in 1234 and the Cistercian monastery Fraubrunnen (Canton Bern) in 1246. The two Hartmanns are also responsible for the founding of the cities of Aarau, Mellingen, Zug and Frau
2 CONC enfeld.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.deutsche-biographie.de/sfz26212.html?language=en
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWABIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#HartmannVKyburgdied1263
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         '''HARTMANN''' [V] (-3 Sep 1263, bur Wettingen).  Graf von Kiburg.  Seigneur de Fribourg.  The Community of "Uriburt" promised to observe the donation by "Conte Hartmano di Kibourg" with the consent of "Conte Hartmano G
2 CONC iuniore" to "Dama Margarita Moglie del detto Conte H. Seniore" by charter dated 1241[861].  The necrology of Wettingen records the death "III Non Sep 1263" of "Hermannus com iunior de Kiburg et Anna uxor eius"[862].  The index of 
2 CONC benefactors of Wettingen records the death in 1263 of "Hartmannus com de Kiburg iunior…benefactor" and his burial "apud sacellum beatæ Mariæ Virginis"[863].  The necrology of Fraubrunnen records the death "IV Non Sep" of "Graf Har
2 CONC tman der jünger"[864].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly (before 9 Feb 1248, divorced before 28 Jan 1251, remarried?) ANNA von Rapperswil, daughter of RUDOLF Graf von Rapperswil & his wife --- (-30 May 1253).  Pope Innocent IV granted dispensation to “nobili viro Artiman
2 CONC no nato...L. comitis de Froburc” [Hartmann von Frohburg] to marry “Annam filiam nobilis viri --- comitis de Rapreswiler”, who had been divorced from “H. iunior comes de Kiburch tertia te linea consanguinitatis” because he had prev
2 CONC iously contracted to marry “matertera ipsius A[nne] sponsalia”, dated 28 Jan 1251[865].  The following documents suggest that the difficulty which provided the basis for the couple’s divorce was resolved and that the validity of t
2 CONC he marriage was later recognised by the church.  The necrology of Wettingen records the death "III Kal Jun" of "domina Anna de Kiburg", recalled in the later entry "III Non Sep 1263" of "Hermannus com iunior de Kiburg et Anna uxor
2 CONC  eius"[866].  “Hartmannus junior comes de Kiburc” founded an anniversary for “recenti morte...Annæ comitissæ” at Wettingen by charter dated 31 May 1253, witnessed by “H. patruus noster de Kiburc, R. socer noster de Rapertwiler...”
2 CONC [867].  “Hartmannus comes iunior de Kiburc” renounced rights over property in favour of Kloster Wettingen, for the souls of “bone memorie...uxoris nostre Anne comitisse” and in the hope of a long life for “filii nostri Wernheri co
2 CONC mitis”, by charter dated 4 Jun 1253[868].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (contract 27 Jan 1254) ELISABETH de Chalon, daughter of HUGUES de Chalons Seigneur de Salins Comte Palatin de Bourgogne & his wife Alix von Andechs-Merano Ctss Palatine de Bourgogne (-9 Jul 1275).  “Hartmannus jun
2 CONC ior comes de Kibourc” confirmed agreement to the dowry for his marriage to “Hugo comes Burgundie palatinus et...A...uxor eius...Elisabeth filie eorumdem primogenite uxoris nostre” by charter dated 27 Jan 1254[869].  She became a C
2 CONC larissan nun at Freiburg.  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Graf Hartmann [V] & his first wife had one child: 
2 CONT    Graf Hartmann [V] & his second wife had two children:   
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
