2 CONT b)         MARGUERITE de Beaujeu (1346-1402).  The contract of marriage between "Dominum Jacobum de Sabaudia Principem Achayæ" and "Domicellam Margaritam de Bellojoco" is dated 16 Jul 1362, and names "Dominus Antonius dominus Bell
2 CONC ijoci frater dictæ domicellæ…bonæ memoriæ Dom. Eduardi et Dom. Mariæ de Til Dom. quondam Bellijoci patris et matris dictorum Dom. Antonii Dom. nunc Bellijoci et dictæ domicellæ Margaritæ"[746].  A dispensation for the marriage bet
2 CONC ween "Giacomo di Savoia Principe d'Acaja" and "Margarita figlia del fu Edoardo Signore di Beaujeu" was granted by "Amedeo di Savoia Vescovo di Moriena Subdelegato Apostolico" 18 Jul 1362[747].  Her marriage was agreed as a conditi
2 CONC on of the treaty of 2 Jul 1362 which settled the dispute between her future husband and Amédée VI Comte de Savoie.  Dame de Berzay.  The testament of "Dominus Jacobus de Sabaudia Princeps Achayæ filius et hæres…Domini Philippi de 
2 CONC Sabaudia Principis Achayæ quondam" dated 16 May 1366 bequeaths the dowry under the contract of marriage of "Dominæ Margaretæ de Bellojoco eius conjugi"[748].  She conspired to exclude her step-son from the succession in Piemonte, 
2 CONC in favour of her own sons[749].  After the suppression of the rebellion of her stepson, she was obliged to resign the guardianship of her infant sons in 1369 in return for an annual pension of 3,000 florins, and was interned in a 
2 CONC Franciscan convent[750].  The testament of "Margarite de Beaujeu Princesse de la Morée, relicte de…Jaques de Sauoye Prince de la Morée" dated 21 Oct 1388 chooses her burial "en l’Eglise des Freres Meneurs de Pinerol…auec ques mon…
2 CONC Seigneur et Mary Monsieur Jaques de Sauoye jadis Prince de la Morée" and names as her heirs "mes…fils Amies de Sauoye Prince de la Morée…et Loys de Sauoye mon…fils" and, in default of male descendants, "mon oncle Monsieur Jean sei
2 CONC gneur de Til"[751].  Dame de Berzay.  
