2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         JEAN [III] de la Chambre ([after 1352?]-25 Aug 1418).  Vicomte de Maurienne.  He was named in a charter dated 6 Sep 1372 “sous la curatelle de sa mère Agnès de Savoie”[1057].  His testament is dated 12 Mar 1412[1058].  
2 CONC He died 25 Aug 1418[1059].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly ([1370/75?]) JEANNE de Chalon, daughter of JEAN de Chalon Seigneur d’Arlay & his wife Marguerite de Lorraine ([1356/60]-after 12 Mar 1412).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not been
2 CONC  identified.  She succeeded her father as Dame d'Auberive.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly RICHARDE de Roussillon, daughter of [GERARD de Roussillon & his wife Marguerite de Miribel].  Foras records her marriage, noting her parentage “selon Guichenon” (who reverses the order of her husband’s marriages)[
2 CONC 1060].  The primary source which confirms this information has not been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean [III] & his first wife had one child: 
