2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria of Brabant
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria of Brabant (13 May 1254, Leuven – January 10, 1321, Murel), Queen consort of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a daughter of Henry III, Duke of Brabant and Adelaide of Burgundy, daughter of Hugh IV, Duke of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria became the second wife of Philip III of France on 21 August 1274 at Vincennes. She was crowned at Ste-Chapelle on 24 June 1275. She was the mother of Louis d'Evreux, Marguerite (wife of Edward I of England), and Blanche, wif
2 CONC e of Rudolph I of Bohemia. Due to her influence Philip became involved in the affairs of the Angevins and in hostilities with the Kingdom of Aragon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis (May 1276 – May 19, 1319), Count of Évreux
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche (1278 – March 19, 1305, Vienna), married Rudolf III of Austria on May 25, 1300
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret (1282 – February 14, 1317), married Edward I of England
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the death of her husband the King in 5 October 1285, she withdrew to a convent near Meulan. She died there 36 years later, and was buried in the Cordeliers convent in Paris.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie of Brabant (French: Marie de Brabant; 13 May 1254 – 10 January 1321) was Queen consort of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie was born in Leuven, Brabant. She was a daughter of Henry III, Duke of Brabant, and Adelaide of Burgundy, daughter of Hugh IV, Duke of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents [hide]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Family
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Children
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 Death
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 Ancestors
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 See also
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie's paternal grandparents were Henry II, Duke of Brabant, and his wife Marie of Hohenstaufen. Her maternal grandparents were Hugh IV, Duke of Burgundy, and his first wife Yolande of Dreux. Marie's siblings included Henry IV, D
2 CONC uke of Brabant, and John I, Duke of Brabant.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie married on 24 June 1275, to Philip III of France. This was Philip's second marriage, after the death of his first wife, Isabella of Aragon. Isabella had already given birth to three surviving sons: Louis, Philip and Charles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip was under the strong influence of his mother, the dowager Queen of France, Margaret of Provence and his minion, surgeon and chamberlain (Chambellan) Pierre de La Broce (or Pierre de Brosse). Not being French, Marie stood ou
2 CONC t at the French court.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1276, Philip's son and heir, Louis died, under suspicious circumstances. Marie was suspected of ordering him to be poisoned. La Brosse, who was also suspected, was imprisoned and later executed for the murder. Margaret suspecte
2 CONC d Marie of ordering the death of Louis and Philip did seem to agree more with his mother than his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Philip III in 1285, Marie lost her political influence, and dedicated her life to her three children. Her stepson, Philip was crowned king of France, as Philip IV, on 6 January 1286 in Reims. Marie lived right t
2 CONC hrough Philip IV's reign and she had outlived all three children.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie and Philip had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Louis (May 1276 – 19 May 1319), Count of Évreux
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Blanche (1278 – 19 March 1305, Vienna), married Rudolf III of Austria on 25 May 1300
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.Margaret, married Edward I of England
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Death
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie died in 1321, aged sixty one, in the monastery at Les Mureaux, near Meulan, where she had withdrawn to in 1316. Marie wasn't buried in royal necropolis of Basilica of Saint-Denis, but in the Cordeliers Convent, in Paris. Des
2 CONC troyed in a fire in 1580, the church was rebuilt in the following years.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Ancestors
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria's ancestors in three generations Marie of Brabant Father:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry III, Duke of Brabant Paternal Grandfather:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry II, Duke of Brabant Paternal Great-grandfather:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry I, Duke of Brabant 
2 CONT
2 CONT Paternal Great-grandmother:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mathilde of Flanders 
2 CONT
2 CONT Paternal Grandmother:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie of Hohenstaufen Paternal Great-grandfather:
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip of Swabia 
2 CONT
2 CONT Paternal Great-grandmother:
2 CONT
2 CONT Irene Angelina 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother:
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelaide of Burgundy Maternal Grandfather:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh IV, Duke of Burgundy Maternal Great-grandfather:
2 CONT
2 CONT Eudes III, Duke of Burgundy 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maternal Great-grandmother:
2 CONT
2 CONT Theresa of Portugal 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maternal Grandmother:
2 CONT
2 CONT Yolanda of Dreux Maternal Great-grandfather:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert III of Dreux 
2 CONT
