1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://translate.google.com/translate?hl=en&sl=fr&u=http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaucher_V_de_Ch%25C3%25A2tillon&ei=XTa_TJiHIIeqsAOGlaGXDA&sa=X&oi=translate&ct=result&resnum=2&ved=0CCAQ7gEwAQ&prev=/search%3Fq%3DGau
2 CONC cher%2Bde%2BCh%25C3%25A2tillon%26hl%3Den%26rlz%3D1I7DKUS_en%26prmd%3Divm
2 CONT
2 CONT Progeny 
2 CONT
2 CONT V Gaucher de Châtillon married three times: 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1276 , with Isabella de Dreux ( 1264 - 1300 ) princess of royal blood of France, daughter of Robert I ( 1217 - 1264 ), Lord of Beu, Vicomte de Chateaudun , himself the son of Robert III of Dreux and descending of Louis VI . His
2 CONC  mother, Isabel de Villebéon lady is Bagneux La Fosse & La Chapelle-Gauthier , in Brie , is the descendant among others by the ancestors of most of its early kings of France. Hence five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT -VI Gaucher de Chatillon ( one thousand two hundred eighty-one - in 1325 ), Lord of Tours and Sompuis (51), Earl of Porcéan Effigy VI alleged Gaucher de Chatillon, Count of Porcien
2 CONT
2 CONT -Jean II de Chatillon ( 1283 - 1363 ), Lord of La Ferté-en-Ponthieu, Gandelus and Marigny, Grand cooks of France and Grand Master of France . 
2 CONT
2 CONT -Jeanne de Châtillon ( 1 285 - 1 354 ), married to Walter V of Brienne , conte di Lecce (1296-15 March 1311), Comte de Brienne (1296-15 March 1311), Duke of Athens (October 5, 1308 to March 15, 1311 ). 
2 CONT
2 CONT -Hugues de Chatillon ( in 1287 - 1 336 ), Lord of Pontarcy, of Auzoy, Rozoy in Thiérache and Recquignies.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Marie de Châtillon, who married Guichard of Beaujeu. 
2 CONT
2 CONT - Isabeau de Chatillon, Abbess of Notre-Dame de Soissons .
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------
