1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkbresse.htm#HumbertIVThoiredied1336B
2 CONT
2 CONT HUMBERT [IV] de Thoire et Villars, son of HUMBERT [III] Seigneur de Thoire et Villars & his second wife Marguerite --- (-28 Nov 1336).  Humbert [IV]’s birth date is estimated from the following: Humbert Seigneur de Thoire emancipa
2 CONC ted his son in Jul 1291 and granted him properties including “Villars, Chastelard...Montreal...Arbent”, reserving the usufruct for life[526].  The Chronicle of Chassagne abbey records that the abbey settled disputes with “Humberto
2 CONC  de Thoire et Humberto filio eius, comite Gebennensi” concerning “justitia de Chassagnia et pro pedagio portus de Loya” in 1270[527].  Given his likely birth date, this entry may be misdated.  Seigneur de Thoire et Villars.  “Humb
2 CONC ert sire de Thoire et de Villars” sold revenue and harvest from “la paroisse de Chatelard” to the chapter of Lyon Saint-Just by charter dated 7 Jun 1303[528].  “Humbert sire de Thoire et de Villars” acknowledged holding “les châte
2 CONC au, ville et mandement de Trévoux” from the church of Lyon by charter dated 10 Aug 1304[529].  “Humbert seigneur de Thoire et de Villars” sold revenue and harvest from “les manses de la Fleurière, de Neyret, de la Chabauderie, de 
2 CONC la Conforterie, des Blanchières” to “Barthélemy Constantin bourgeois d’Anse”, with the consent of “Eléonore femme dudit Humbert”, by charter dated 14 Aug 1310[530]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (contract Lyon 30 Jun 1291) ELEONORE de Beaujeu, daughter of LOUIS [I] Seigneur de Beaujeu & his wife Eléonore de Savoie (-10 Sep 1344).  A charter dated 30 Jun 1291 records an arbitral sentence between “Louis sire de Beaujeu” a
2 CONC nd “Humbert sire de Thoire et de Villars” requiring the latter to grant “Chatillon-la-Palud le fief qu’il tient...du sire de Beaujeu” and the former to grant “sa fille Eléonore en mariage à Humbert fils émancipé du sire de Villars
2 CONC ”, who granted “le château du Chatelard” as her dower[531].  “Humbert seigneur de Thoire et de Villars” sold revenue and harvest from “les manses de la Fleurière, de Neyret, de la Chabauderie, de la Conforterie, des Blanchières” t
2 CONC o “Barthélemy Constantin bourgeois d’Anse”, with the consent of “Eléonore femme dudit Humbert”, by charter dated 14 Aug 1310[532]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Humbert [IV] & his wife had seven children:  
