2 CONT Ermesinde, Countess of Luxembourg From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Ermesinde of Luxembourg (also known as Ermesinde of Namur) (1186 - February 12, 1247) was the Countess of Luxembourg, Laroche and Durbuy between 1197 and 1247. She was the only child of Henry IV, Count of Luxembourg and Namur, and
2 CONC  his second wife Agnes of Guelders. Prior to her birth, her aging father Henry IV had designated Baldwin V, Count of Hainaut as his likely successor. However, when Ermesinde was born in 1186 and Henry IV named her as his heir, a w
2 CONC ar of succession inevitably took place. At its end, it was decided that Baldwin would have Namur, Ermesinde would have Durbuy and La Roche, and that Luxembourg would revert to the Holy Roman Empire (Emperor Henry VI then gave the 
2 CONC fief to his brother Otto of Burgundy). Ermesinde was initially betrothed to Henry II of Champagne, but the engagement was cancelled in 1189. Instead her first husband was Theobald I of Bar (1158-1214). He successfully negotiated w
2 CONC ith Otto I, Count of Burgundy for the latter's renunciation of Luxembourg, thus making Theobald and Ermesinde the Count and Countess of Luxembourg. When Theobald died in 1214, Ermesinde married Waleran III of Limburg (1180-1226), 
2 CONC who would rule as the Count of Luxembourg. In 1223 Ermesinde and Waleran pressed their claim to Namur against Margrave Philip II, but were ultimately unsuccessful. After Walram's death, Ermesinde ruled Luxembourg alone for two dec
2 CONC ades. She proved to be an effective administrator, granting charters of freedom to several towns and increasing the prosperity of her country. [edit]Children
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Ermesinde and her first husband Theobald I of Bar were: Renaud (died before 1214), Seigneur of Briey Elisabeth (d.1262), married Valéran of Limburg, Lord of Monschau Marguerite (d?), first married Hugh III, Count o
2 CONC f Vaudémont(d.1243); later married Henry of Bois, regent of Vaudémont. The children of Ermesinde and Waleran III of Limburg were: Henry V of Luxembourg (1216 - 1281), Count of Luxembourg Gérard I of Durbuy, Count of Durbuy (d. 127
2 CONC 6) Catherine of Limburg (d.1255), wife of Matthias II, Duke of Lorraine [edit]External links
2 CONT
