1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walram_III_van_Limburg
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waleran_III,_Duke_of_Limburg
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00026504&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Waleran III or Walram III (1180 – 2 July 1226) was initially '''lord of Montjoie''', then '''count of Luxembourg''' from 1214. He became '''count of Arlon''' and '''duke of Limburg''' on his father's death in 1221. He was the son 
2 CONC of Henry III of Limburg and Sophia of Saarbrucken.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a younger son, he did not expect to inherit. He carried on an adventurous youth and took part in the Third Crusade in 1192. In 1208, the imperial candidate Philip of Swabia died and Waleran, his erstwhile supporter, turned to h
2 CONC is opponent, Otto of Brunswick. In 1212, he accompanied his first cousin Henry I, Duke of Brabant, to Liège, then in a war with Guelders. Waleran's first wife, Cunigunda, a daughter of Frederick I, Duke of Lorraine, died in 1214 a
2 CONC nd in May he married Ermesinda of Luxembourg*, and became count there. Ermesinda claimed Namur and so Waleran added a crown to his coat of arms to symbolise this claim.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1221, he inherited Limburg and added a second tail to the rampant lion on his arms. This symbolised his holding of two great fiefs. In 1223, he again tried to take Namur from the Margrave Philip II. He failed and signed a peace
2 CONC  treaty on 13 February in Dinant. He then took part in various imperial diets and accompanied the Emperor Frederick II into Italy. Returning from there, he died in Rolduc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Information from the Wikipedia entry: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waleran_III,_Duke_of_Limburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical information about the Duchy of Limburg: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duchy_of_Limburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical information about the House Ardennes-Verdun: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ardennes-Verdun_dynasty
2 CONT
2 CONT Further Historical and Genealogical Discussion: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LIMBURG.htm 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT In Dutch, list of the Hertog van Limburg: http://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lijst_van_hertogen_van_Limburg
2 CONT
2 CONT German Wikipedia entry: http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walram_III._%28Limburg%29
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT **Discrepancy regarding parentage discussed here in the German Wikipedia entry for Heinrich I. (Limburg):
2 CONT
2 CONT http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heinrich_I._%28Limburg%29
2 CONT
2 CONT Apparently, there is a question as to whether Heinrich I. (Limburg) was married once or twice. 
2 CONT --------------------
