1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Frederick II, Duke of Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT By his 1188 marriage to Agnes of Bar (d.19 June 1226), he received the lands of Amance, Longwy, and Stenay. He entered into a war with his father-in-law, Theobald I of Bar, and was defeated in 1208, being captured and imprisoned f
2 CONC or seven months.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT By his marriage to the daughter of the count of Bar and Laurette de Looz, he had:
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald (d.1220), his successor in Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthias (d.1251), his brother, successor in Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT Reginald (d.1274), count of Blieskastel
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice, countess of Ormes, married firstly Werner (d.1228), count of Kirbourg, and secondly, in 1229, Walter, lord of Vignory
2 CONT
2 CONT Lauretta, married Simon III, Count of Saarbrücken, in 1226
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob (d.1260), bishop of Metz
