2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/151979819/marguerite_de_champagne
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NAVARRE.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT King Teobaldo I & his third wife had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         '''MARGUERITE de Champagne, Infanta doña MARGARETA de Navarra''' ([1240]-3 Oct 1307, bur église des Précheresses, Nancy).  The marriage contract between “Ferris dux de Lorraine et marchis” and “Thiebaut...Roy de Navarre
2 CONC  et de Champaigne et de Brie conte palatin et...Marguerite sa femme...Marguerite la fille à dict Roy” is dated 10 Jul 1255[650].  She renounced her rights over the county of Champagne shortly after her marriage, renewing the decla
2 CONC ration 20 Mar 1273[651].  The testament of “Ferris duc de Lorregne et marchis”, dated 1297, bequeathes property to “Marguerite ma femme...Ferri mon fils de Plommieres...Jean mon fils de Toul...mon anée fille Isabéez...Thibaut me f
2 CONC ils...Catherine ma fille...”[652].  She founded the convent of the Clarissans at Neufchâteau in 1297.  m (contract 6 Jun 1249, 10 Jul 1255) FERRY III Duke of Lorraine, son of MATHIEU II Duke of Lorraine & his wife Catherine van Li
2 CONC mburg (early 1240-31 Dec 1302, bur Beaupré Abbey). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT === Family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LORRAINE.htm#FerryIIIdied1302B
2 CONT
2 CONT FERRY de Lorraine, son of MATHIEU II Duke of Lorraine & his wife Catherine de Limbourg (early 1240-31 Dec 1303, bur Beaupré Abbey).  Mathieu II Duke of Lorraine donated “l’usage du ban de Viéville” to Sainte-Marie-au-Bois-lès-Prén
2 CONC y, with the conse of “Catherine sa femme et de Ferry son fils”, by charter dated 31 May 1250[266]. …
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Ferry III & his wife had [eight] children:  … 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederick_III,_Duke_of_Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick III (French: Ferry) (1240 – 31 December 1302) was the Duke of Lorraine from 1251 to his death. He was the only son and successor of Matthias II and Catherine of Limburg.  He was not yet thirteen years of age when his fat
2 CONC her died, so his mother assumed the regency for a few years. In 1255, he married '''Margaret''', the daughter of King Theobald I of Navarre and '''Margaret of Bourbon'''.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT By his marriage to Margaret,[1] he had the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Theobald (1263–1312), his successor in Lorraine
2 CONT # Matthias (died 1282), lord of Beauregard
2 CONT # Frederick (died 1299), bishop of Orléans (1297–1299)
2 CONT # Frederick (died c. 1320), lord of Plombiéres, Romont, and Brémoncourt
2 CONT # Gerard (known 1317)
2 CONT # Isabelle (died 1335), married (1287) Louis III, Duke of Lower Bavaria; then Lord Henry of Sully; and then (1306) Count Henry III of Vaudémont [fr] (died 1348)
2 CONT # Catherine, lady of Romont, married (1290) Conrad II (died 1350), count of Fribourg
2 CONT # Agnes, married John II (died 1302), sire of Harcourt
2 CONT # Margaret, married Eberhard I, Count of Württemberg
2 CONT
