2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkvaud.htm#HumbertAlamandiMAgnesJoinvilleGex
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         HUMBERT Alamandi (-after 22 Mar 1352).  The testament of “Guillaume Allemand chevalier seigneur de Valbonnais”, dated 27 Apr 1332, named “sa [premièr] femme Agnès de Villars, de leur fils Hugues, de sa mère Eléonore de 
2 CONC Roussillon, de ses filles Béatrix et Jeanne, de sa seconde femme Sibylle de la Palud”, and appointed “des curateurs à son fils Humbert”[581].  His parentage is confirmed by the charter dated 20 Aug 1370 under which his son-in-law 
2 CONC "Rodulphus comes Gruerie" sold the succession in the seigneuries d’Aubonne et de Coppet, inherited from "dne Agnetis de Villar, quondam dne Albone, et dni Humberti Alamandi, eius filii"[582].  Seigneur d’Aubonne.  The testament of
2 CONC  “Humbert Allemand seigneur d’Aubonne”, dated 22 Mar 1352 or 11 Apr 1353, bequeathed property to “son oncle Artaud prieur de Rommond”[583].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' AGNES de Joinville, daughter of GUILLAUME de Joinville Seigneur de Gex & his wife Jeanne de Savoie (-after 2 May 1349).  Humbert & his wife had three children:  
