1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00535094&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Rodolphe IV, comte de Gruyère, was the eldest son and successor of Pierre IV, comte de Gruyère, and Catherine de La Tour. He married twice. With his first wife Marguerite Alleman, daughter of Humbert Alleman, seigneur d'
2 CONC Aubonne, and Agnès de Joinville, he had a son Rodolphe who would have progeny. There appears to be no recorded progeny from his second marriage, to Marguerite de Grandson. Both Rodolphe's wives were related to the house of Savoy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT It was said of Rodolphe that he displayed in his long rule no quality worthy of his generous and high spirited father Pierre, and no trace of the conciliatory wisdom or devoted piety of his mother. Calculating in his marriages, he
2 CONC  was unjust and even dishonest with his people, whom he forced to pay twice over for their exemptions and privileges. Continuing to dishonestly withhold the signed and purchased acknowledgement of their new privileges from his sub
2 CONC jects, he was surprised alone at night in the castle by a brave peasant, who forced the paper from his unwilling hands and threw it out of the window to a waiting accomplice. Left in charge of the Savoy troops who had driven the i
2 CONC nvading Visconti from the Valais, and entrusted with the guardianship of the châteaux and prisoners won by Savoy arms, he extracted large sums for his services, although those services amounted to a complete surprise and defeat at
2 CONC  the hands of the inhabitants of the Valais; except for the heroic defence of the subjects he had so oppressed, he would himself have died in the attack. From the benefits of the peace which was ultimately established in the Valai
2 CONC s, these same loyal subjects were excluded. How greatly Rodolphe was lacking in the noble and humanitarian qualities which had generally characterised the counts of Gruyère, was shown in his dealings with his young relative Othon 
2 CONC III de Grandson, son of Guillaume 'le Grand' de Grandson, seigneur de Sainte-Croix, de Grandcour, Cudrefin, the brother of his second wife Marguerite de Grandson. Othon had been a comrade of Rodolphe's brother Jean de Gruyère in h
2 CONC is French campaigns and in their long captivity in Spain following their capture at the Spanish victory over John de Hastings, earl of Pembroke, at the Battle of La Rochelle on 22 June 1372. Othon was later doubly related to Rodol
2 CONC phe, as brother-in-law of his first wife Marguerite Alleman, and as nephew of his second wife Marguerite de Grandson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The tragic hero of an unjust drama of prosecution which divided into opposing camps the nobles of Romand Switzerland, Othon de Grandson was falsely accused of complicity in the poisoning of Amadeo VII 'the Red', comte de Savoie, i
2 CONC n 1391. Although declared innocent by a royal French tribunal, he was again implacably accused by his rival in love, a Count Estavayer, on his return to his estates. Calling God to witness that his accuser lied, he consented to de
2 CONC fend and prove his innocence in a trial of arms. In the presence of the count of Savoy and of his council and assembled knights, he was mortally wounded by his opponent. No effort was made by Rodolphe to defend his relative, while
2 CONC  his son Rodolphe was not only an unprotesting witness to Othon's undeserved fate, but the purchaser with his father's assistance of the confiscated Grandson estates. Again, although selling the newly acquired châteaux of Oron and
2 CONC  Palézieux to increase their revenues, the two Rodolphes, in total disregard of the rights of the new owners, attempted to retake them by force of arms, and except for the immediate intervention of the count of Savoy, they would h
2 CONC ave plunged the newly pacified country into a general war. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Rodolphe died about 1403, leaving his county heavily indebted. As his son Rodolphe had predeceased him he was succeeded by his grandson Antoine.
