1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alice of Saluzzo, Countess of Arundel (died 25 September 1292)[1] also known as Alessia di Saluzzo, was a Savoyard noblewoman and an English countess. She was daughter of Thomas I of Saluzzo, and the wife of Richar
2 CONC d Fitzalan, 1st Earl of Arundel. She assumed the title of Countess of Arundel in 1289.
2 CONT Family
2 CONT Alice was born on an unknown date in Saluzzo (present-day Province of Cuneo, Piedmont); the second-eldest daughter of Thomas I, 4th Margrave of Saluzzo, and Luigia di Ceva, daughter of Giorgio, Marquis of Ceva.[1] Alice had fiftee
2 CONC n siblings. Her father was a very wealthy and cultured nobleman under whose rule Saluzzo achieved a prosperity, freedom and greatness it had never known previously.[citation needed] She was niece of Alasia of Saluzzo, who in 1247 
2 CONC had married an English nobleman, Edmund de Lacy, Baron of Pontefract, and was a more distant kinswoman of Eleanor of Provence, queen consort of Henry III of England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alice_of_Saluzzo,_Countess_of_Arundel
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She is a Direct Descendant of Charlemagne.'''
2 CONT This is her lineage:
2 CONT
2 CONT Charlemagne
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis I, The Pious
2 CONT
2 CONT Giséle of Cysoing 
2 CONT
2 CONT Berengar I, emperor of the Romans
2 CONT
2 CONT Gisela of Friuli 
2 CONT
2 CONT Berengar II of Ivrea, king of Italy 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adalbert II, king of Italy
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto Guillaume I, comte de Bourgogne et de Mâcon 
2 CONT
2 CONT Reginald I of Ivrea, count palatine of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT William I "the Great" count of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT Gisèle (Gille) de Bourgogne
2 CONT
2 CONT William V Aleramici, "the Old" marquess of Montserrat
2 CONT
2 CONT Alasia Aleramici, del Monferrato [descendant by both parents]
2 CONT
2 CONT María di Saluzzo
2 CONT
2 CONT Aloisia di Saluzzo (di Ceva)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Medlands: [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MONFERRATO,%20SALUZZO,%20SAVONA.htm#Luigiadied1291 "Monferrat, Saluzzo, Savona"]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/people/Guglielmo-II-marchese-di-Ceva/6000000006727915839 Guglielmo] [II] (-after 25 Nov 1228). ''The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.''  Marchese di Ceva,  "''Dominus
2 CONC  Willelmus, D. Manuellus, D. Leo, D. Bonefacius et D. Georgius fratres omnes Marchiones de Ceva''" exchanged property with Giacopo Bishop of Asti by charter dated Sep 1222[885].  "''Otto marchio de Careto et Oddonus eius nepos mar
2 CONC chiones de Vasto et Guielmus marchio de Ceva et Manuellus eius frater suo et fratrum suorum…Raymundus marchio de Busca…et fratrum suorum et Gratapalea…et Henrici di Careto soceri sui''…" made an alliance with Asti against Alexandr
2 CONC ia and Alba by charter dated 25 Nov 1228[886].   <br> '''m''' --- di Saluzzo, daughter of MANFREDO II Marchese di Saluzzo & his wife Alasia di Monferrato. ''The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet 
2 CONC been identified.'' <br> Guglielmo [II] & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT ** i) '''ALOISIA di Ceva''' (?–[22 Aug 1291/1293], bur Revello Santa Maria).   <br> A continuation of the ''Chronica Jacobi de Aquis'' names "''Loysa figlola dil Marchese di Ceva''" as the wife of "Thomaso", son of "Manfredo"[859]
2 CONC .  <br> A charter dated 31 Mar 1282 names "''Thome marchionis Salutiarum et Aluyisia eius uxoris''"[860].  <br> ''Aloisia comitissa Salutiarum uxor Thomæ I marchionis Salutiarum''" consented to donations by "''eundem marchionem eo
2 CONC rum filio Mainfredo''" on the occasion of the latter´s marriage to "''Beatrice filia quondam Mainfredi regis Siciliæ''" by charter dated 1286[861].   <br> "''Marchese Tomaso di Saluzzo e Marchesa Alosia padre e madre di detto Manf
2 CONC redo''" consented to the marriage between "''Manfredo figlio primogenito del Marchese Tomaso di Saluzzo''" and "''Beatrice figlia del fù Re Manfredo, sorella della Regina Costanza d'Aragona e Sicilia''" by contract dated 3 Jul 128
2 CONC 6[862]. <br> "''Thomas marchio Salutiarum atque…Aluysia de Ceva eius uxor et Salutiarum marchionissa''" donated property to "''monasterii beati Marie de Revello''" by charter dated 25 Jun 1291[863].  <br> '''m''' TOMASO I Marchese
2 CONC  di Saluzzo, son of MANFREDO III Marchese di Saluzzo & his wife Béatrix de Savoie (-3 Dec 1296). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ====References 
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/150859462/aloisia-di_saluzzo
2 CONT
