2 CONT Albert en est le baron l'an 1161, croisé de 1190 à 92 et est père d'Albert II, de Berlion, de Hugues évêque de Clermont (1227-† 1249 à la croisade), et de Guy, archevêque de Vienne3
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Dictionnaire historique, chronologique, géographique, généalogique, héraldique, juridique, politique et botanographique du Dauphiné, Par Guy Allard, Hyacinthe Gariel, Publié par impr. E. Allier, 1864, Notes sur l'article: 
2 CONC [VOL. 3], p.690.
2 CONT
2 CONT =---------------------------=
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkvien.htm#_Toc31798808
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          ALBERT [I] de la Tour (-after 1184).  "Arbertus de Turre et Galo consobrinus meus nec non et Willelmus de Thiel" donated “pascua Cizerini” to Ecouges by charter dated 1154[2102].  "Dom. comes Albionensium, Guigo…dalphi
2 CONC nus", acting with his council of advisers "Arberti de Turre…" and with the advice of "Willelmi de Clariaco Romanensis ecclesie sacristie", gave permission to the inhabitants of Romans to build a wall around their town, by charter 
2 CONC dated 1161[2103].  "Albertus de Turre…" witnessed the charter dated 1184 under which records that "Hugo Divionensis dux" married "filiam comitis Dalphini viduam Taillefer filii comitis Sancti Egidii" and agreed rights over la Plai
2 CONC ne with the bishop of Grenoble[2104].  Père Anselme records that Albert de la Tour witnessed charters of Hugues III Duke of Burgundy (dated 1184)[2105].  "Dominus Arbertus de Turre" donated property to Léoncel, with "filii eius Ar
2 CONC bertus et Berlio", by undated charter[2106].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ---.  The name of Albert’s wife is not known.  Albert [I] & his wife had [five or more] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *(a)       ALBERT [II] de la Tour (-1229 or after).  "Dominus Arbertus de Turre" donated property to Léoncel, with "filii eius Arbertus et Berlio", by undated charter[2107]. -         see below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *(b)       BERLION de la Tour (-murdered [10 Jun 1249/13 Feb 1250]).  "Dominus Arbertus de Turre" donated property to Léoncel, with "filii eius Arbertus et Berlio", by undated charter[2108]. -         SEIGNEURS de VINAY. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *(c)       JACELME de la Tour (-after 22 Oct 1252).  “Noble Berlion de la Tour” granted “[le] village de Quinsonas dans le mandement de la Tour” to “son frère Jacelme de la Tour” by charter dated 1244[2109].  Canon of Romans.
2 CONT
2 CONT =-------------------------------=
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkvien.htm#BerlionTourdied1249
2 CONT
2 CONT BERLION de la Tour, son of ALBERT [I] de la Tour & his wife --- (-murdered [10 Jun 1249/13 Feb 1250]).  "Dominus Arbertus de Turre" donated property to Léoncel, with "filii eius Arbertus et Berlio", by undated charter[2178].  "Fil
2 CONC ii Alberti Domini de Turre Albertus et Berlio" confirmed donations to the Chartreuse de Portes by their father and by "pater eius Giroldus de Turre" by charter dated 1200[2179].  “Noble Berlion de la Tour” granted “[le] village de
2 CONC  Quinsonas dans le mandement de la Tour” to “son frère Jacelme de la Tour” by charter dated 1244[2180].  Seigneur de Vinay.  “Beryllio de la Tour seigneur de Vinay” sold his possessions in la Motte-Saint-Antoine to Dauphin Guigues
2 CONC  by charter dated 10 Jun 1249[2181]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ALASIE de Montluel, daughter of HUMBERT [I] Seigneur de Montluel & his wife ---.  The testament of "Humbertus dominus Montislupelli", dated 1 Aug 1236, appoints as his heirs "Alasiam filiam meam…Helizabeth filiam meam…Marg
2 CONC aretam filiam meam…Matthiam filiam meam" and provides dowries for each of them[2182].  Guichenon says that Alasie married "Berlioni de Turre militi, Alberti domini de Turre-Pini flio, apud Delphinates", without citing the correspo
2 CONC nding source[2183].  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Berlion [I] & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT ==More Information==
