1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Curator's Note: Cawley places this Guy as the son of Albert II. However, benoit Gonod's history of the Bishops of Clermont states the Hugues was succeeded as Bishop by his nephew Gui de La Tour, named by Gonod as t
2 CONC he son of Gui de la Tour who donated an old chateau in Clermont to the church in 1273 which was made into a church and consecrated in 1284 (the building later served as the Departmente Archives). Therefore, I have placed him as Gu
2 CONC y's son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Benoît Gonod, ''Chronologie des évêques de Clermont et des principaux événements de l'histoire ecclésiastique de l‛Auvergne'' (Thibaud-Landriaot,1833) p. 35-36. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkvien.htm#_ftnref2149
2 CONT
2 CONT d)         GUY de la Tour-du-Pin (-1286).  "Hugo de Turre, abbas Claromontensis, et Guido frater eiusdem, canonicus Claromontensis" noted a donation to Cluny by charter dated 13 Oct 1238, which names “dominum Albertum de Turre pat
2 CONC rem nostrum, et Albertum filium eius fratrem nostrum…”[2150].  Bishop of Clermont .  The epitaph of "Guido de Turre 37 episcopus Arverniæ" records his death in 1286[2151]. 
