1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Pierre IV, son of Aymon, first of the T. to bear the title of baron of Niedergesteln, was bailiff of Vaud (1291) in the service of Savoy. He incited the nobles to revolt against the bishop of Sion, Boniface de Chal
2 CONC lant, but reconciled with the latter in 1299, after the defeat at the Sustmatten (also called Seufzermatten) near Leuk (1296).
2 CONT
2 CONT Fibicher, Arthur: "Tour, de la (barons)", in: Historical Dictionary of Switzerland (DHS) , version of 04.12.2012, translated from German. Online: https://hls-dhs-dss.ch/fr/articles/019784/2012-12-04/, consulted on 08.06.2021.
