2 CONT m secondly (before 9 Aug 1202) '''BERTA''' di Clavesana heiress of Mambarasco e Cortemiglia, daughter of BONIFAZIO Marchese di Clavesana & his wife -.  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by the charter dated 9 Aug 1202 which
2 CONC  records that Bonifazio Marchese di Monferrato promised "Guilelmo filio suo" to ratify the peace agreement with Alexandria and Asti and with "socero suo domino Bonefacio de Cravexana…"[193].  1224. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Marchese Guglielmo VI & his second wife had [six] children:
2 CONT * 1.         BONIFAZIO (-[22 Sep 1253/10 Dec 1255]).  His parentage is confirmed by the charter dated 30 Dec 1230 under which "Dominus Bonefacius marchio de Monte ferrato filius condam domini Villelmi marchionis" granted exemption
2 CONC s to Staffarda[194].  He succeeded his father in 1225 as BONIFAZIO II Marchese di Monferrato.  -        see below. 
2 CONT * 2.         ODDONE (-1251).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   Cardinal deacon 1237.  Pontifical legate to Denmark and London [1237].  Bishop of Porto. 
2 CONT * 3.         DEMETRIO .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   1224. 
2 CONT * 4.         BEATRICE di Monferrato ([1204/10][195]-after Mar 1276). … m (21 Nov 1219) as his third wife, ANDRE de Bourgogne Comte de Gap et d'Embrun, son of HUGUES III Duke of Burgundy [Capet] & his second wife Béatrix de Viennoi
2 CONC s (1184-14 Mar 1237, bur Grenoble, église collégiale de Saint-André).  He succeeded his mother in 1228 as Comte d'Albon, Dauphin. 
2 CONT * 5.         ALASIA (-Kirenia castle 1233 before Apr, bur Nicosia Santa Sofia).  She is named "Aalais" by William of Tyre (Continuator), who names her husband and specifies that she was "fille dou marquis de Monferrare"[199].  …  
2 CONC m (May 1229) as his first wife, HENRI I King of Cyprus, son of HUGUES I King of Cyprus & his wife Alix of Jerusalem Ctss of Jaffa (3 Mar 1217-18 Jan 1253). 
2 CONT * 6.         [ELENA .  Niece and heiress of Demetrio King of Thessaloniki.  Baudouin II Emperor of Constantinople confirmed her rights over Thessaloniki 5 Feb 1240, confirmed in 1244 by the Pope.  m (before 1240) as his first wife
2 CONC , GUGLIELMO da Verona Lord of Eubœa, son of GIBERTO da Verona Lord of Eubœa & his wife --- (-killed in battle Demetrias [1268]).]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT William VI, Marquess of Montferrat
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages and children
2 CONT
2 CONT During his infancy, William was betrothed to Sophie, daughter of Frederick I, Holy Roman Emperor. The marriage took place in 1187, when William was fourteen years old, and Sophie twenty-five; nevertheless, this union ended soon: S
2 CONC ophie died shortly after in that year.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 9 August 1202 William married Berta, daughter of the Marquess Bonifacio di Clavesana, Count of Cortemiglia. They had at least three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Boniface II , Marquess of Montferrat (b. ca 1203).
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice (b. ca 1210 - d. 1274), Lady of Saint-Bonnet in her own right. She married three times:
2 CONT
2 CONT On 15 November 1219, Guigues VI of Viennois
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1252, Guy II, Lord of Bauge
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierre de la Roue
2 CONT
2 CONT Alix (b. ca. 1215 - d. 1232), married in May 1229 Henry I of Lusignan, King of Cyprus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto of Montferrat, (d. 1251), who became Bishop of Porto, and Cardinal in 1227, may have been a son of William VI; whether he was legitimate or not is uncertain.
