2 CONT -----
2 CONT Anna of Hungary
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna of Hungary (c. 1260 - 1281) was a daughter of Stephen V of Hungary and Elizabeth the Cuman, who was daughter of Kuthen, a chief of the Cuman tribe. Her mother had been a pagan before her marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 8 November 1273, Anna of Hungary married Andronikos II Palaiologos. He was the eldest surviving son of Michael VIII Palaiologos and Theodora Doukaina Vatatzina. He was co-emperor with his father since September, 1261.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to George Pachymeres, the couple had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael IX Palaiologos (17 April 1277 - 12 October 1320).
2 CONT
2 CONT Constantine Palaiologos, despotes. (c. 1278 - 1335). Married firstly Eudokia, a daughter of Theodore Mouzalon and a woman of the Kantakouzenos family. Married secondly Eudokia Neokaisareitissa. He also had a mistress, Kathara, who
2 CONC  was in the service of his second wife. Constantine was forced to become a monk by his nephew Andronikos III Palaiologos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eudokia Palaiologina. Only legitimate daughter of Constantine and Eudokia Neokaisareitissa. John VI Kantakouzenos records her marriage to Demetrios Tsamplakos, "Megas stratopedarchos".
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael Katharos. Illegitimate son of Constantine and Kathara. A favorite of his paternal grandfather Andronikos II in the later years of his reign.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna died before her husband became senior emperor in 1282. However every Palaiologos emperor to the Fall of Constantinople in 1453 descended from her through her son Michael.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.genealogieonline.nl/en/west-europese-adel/I49464.php
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Arpad 1258-1285 m. 1275 Andronic II Paleologos van Byzantyum (1259-1332)
