1 NOTE     ES 11:22;PED OF AUGUSTINE H. AYERS
1 NOTE Graaf van Valois (Karel I), kon. v. Aragon, gr. v. Barcelona, cte
2 CONT d'Alencon de Chartres, tit. keizere van Constantinopel etc.
1 NOTE Reðcoit le titre de comte de Valois lorsqu'il a 14 ans (1284). La mãeme annâee il reðcoit du pape l'investiture des deux royaumes de Valence et d'Aragon et du comtâe de Barcelone car ce dernier, Martin IV, vient de prononcer la dâ
2 CONC echâeance de Pierre d'Aragon qui s'est brouillâe avec le Saint-Siáege.
1 NOTE He was the founder of the Anjou dynasty in Hungary.  Charles was crowned 
2 CONT king of Hungary on the death of Andrew III in 1301, but was deposed by 
2 CONT Wenceslas II of Bohemia later that year. He was elected king again by the 
2 CONT Hungarian nobles in 1308 and was formally invested in 1309. Charles levied 
2 CONT direct taxes to support his army, encouraged trade and mercantile 
2 CONT expansion of cities, and increased the territory of Hungary, thus making 
2 CONT Hungary a major power. He was succeeded by his son Louis I.
1 NOTE COUNT OF VALOIS
1 NOTE EARL OF VALOYS
1 NOTE he was also Count of Valois
1 NOTE Margaret was Charles 1. marriage. See Europaeische Stammtafeln Bund II Tafel 16. *Les seize quartiers des reines et imperatrices de Frances* by Jacques Saillot. *The Plantagenet Ancestry* by W.H. Turton. *Genealogisches Handbuch d
2 CONC es Adels*, Fuerstliche Haeuser. *Gens Nostra*, magazine Dutch genealogical society. *Cashiers de St. Louis*.
2 CONT comte de Valois (1284-1325), roi titulaire d'Aragon og de Valence (1284-1290), comte d'Anjou (Charles III, 1290-1325), comte du Maine (Charles III, 1290-1313, 1315), comte d'Alenτon og du Perche (1293-1325), comte de Chartres (129
2 CONC 3), empereur titulaire de Constantinople (1301-1308)
2 CONT (Charles de Valois)
