1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philip_II,_Prince_of_Taranto 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Philip II of Taranto''' (1329 – 25 November 1374) of the Angevin house, was Prince of Achaea and Taranto, and titular Emperor of Constantinople (as Philip III) from 1364 to his death in 1374.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Philip I of Taranto and Catherine of Valois. Upon the execution of his cousin Charles, Duke of Durazzo, in 1348, he succeeded as King of Albania. Shortly after, his older brother Louis married their first cousin,
2 CONC  Joanna I of Naples, and became king. In April 1355, Philip married Joanna's younger sister, Maria of Calabria.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1364, Philip succeeded as titular Emperor of Constantinople, and Prince of Achaea and Taranto on the death of his oldest brother, Robert.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria died in 1366. On 20 October 1370, Philip married yet another Angevin, Elizabeth of Slavonia, former heir presumptive to the throne of Hungary. In 1373, he resigned his rights to the Principality of Achaea to his cousin and f
2 CONC ormer sister-in-law Joanna. He died on 25 November 1374 in Taranto.
2 CONT
2 CONT All his children had died young. His heir was his sister's son James of Baux, Duke of Andria.
2 CONT
