1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simon_II,_Duke_of_Lorraine (FR more info)
2 CONT =Simon II, Duke of Lorraine=
2 CONT '''Simon II''' (1140 – 4 January 1207) was the Duke of Lorraine from 1176 to 1205. 
2 CONT *He was the son and successor of '''Matthias I''' and '''Judith''', daughter of Frederick II, Duke of Swabia.
2 CONT *His mother wished for her second son, Frederick, to succeed and so Simon was forced to convene an assembly of the nobles to confirm his succession. *He was in turn forced to recognise certain feudal privileges and create the Esta
2 CONC tes of Lorraine, a form of parliament. 
2 CONT *He also gave Bitche as an appanage to Frederick who was not satisfied and revolted against Simon. The war lasted three years until the Treaty of Ribemont, whereby Simon retained the southern, francophone, half of the duchy and Fr
2 CONC ederick took the northern, germanophone, portion.
2 CONT *He married '''Ida''' (died 1227), daughter of Gerard I, count of Mâcon and Vienne, and Maurette of Salins. 
2 CONT *They had no children. He designated his nephew, Frederick, son of Frederick, as his successor and ceded, in 1202, the suzerainty over the county of Vaudémont to Count Theobald I of Bar. Simon abdicated and retired to a monastery 
2 CONC in 1205. He died two years later. 
2 CONT *He had no descendants and was succeeded by his brother.
