2 CONT 1.         ALIX [Elise] de Savoie ([1123/25]-).  Her origin is alluded to in the Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines which names "pater Wichardi [de Belloico] senior Humbertus" as "nepos ex sorore comitis Sabaudie", although s
2 CONC he is not named in this source[207].  Her birth date range is estimated based on the birth of her second son in 1142, as shown in Europäische Stammtafeln[208]. Dame de Châteauneuf-en-Valromey, de Virieu-le-Grand, et de Cordon-en-B
2 CONC ugey[209].  "Amedeus comes et marchio" confirmed donations to Saint-Sulpice en Bugey, for the soul of "filii mei Humberti", by charter dated to [1148], which also names "uxore mea Matildi", confirmed by "Aalasia comitissa de Bello
2 CONC  Joco…cum filio meo Guichardo"[210].  
2 CONT
