2 CONT '''Edmund de Lacy, Earl of Lincoln''' (c. 1230–1258) was an important landholder in Northern England, with a strategic manor at Stanbury which was important for east–west communication, and as Lord of the Honour of Pontefract he p
2 CONC ossessed Pontefract Castle....
