2 CONT 5.         Infanta doña VIOLANTE de Aragon (1273-Termini 19 Aug 1302, bur Marseille église des Frères mineurs).  The Historia Sicula of Bartolomeo di Neocastro names "Alfonsus, Elisabeth regina Portugalli…Rex Iacobus, Dominus Frid
2 CONC ericus, domina Violanta et dominus Petrus" as the children of "Petro regi Aragonum" and his wife[562].  The Crónica de San Juan de la Peña records that Jaime II King of Aragon arranged the marriage of "su hermana Doña Violant" and
2 CONC  "Rubert fillo del rey Carlos"[563].  m (Rome Mar 1297) as his first wife, ROBERT of Sicily, son of CHARLES II King of Naples & Sicily [Anjou-Capet] & his wife Maria of Hungary (Royal Palace of the Torre de San Erasmo, near Capua 
2 CONC 1278-Château-Neuf, Naples 16/20 Jan 1343/4, bur Naples Santa Chiara).  Named in 1297 as heir to Sicily by Pope Boniface VIII.  Appointed perpetual Vicar-General in the island of Sicily by his father 24 Jun 1299.  Principe di Saler
2 CONC no 5 May 1304.  Comte de Piémont 17 Feb 1309.  He succeeded his father in 1309 as ROBERT I "le Bon" King of Sicily. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.         Infante don PEDRO de Aragón ([1275]-Tordehumos 30 Aug 1296).  The Chronicle of Ramon Muntaner names "Alfonse, Jacques, Frédéric et Pierre" as the four sons of "le seigneur infant Pierre" and "la fille de Mainfroi roi de
2 CONC  Sicile…Constance"[564].  The Historia Sicula of Bartolomeo di Neocastro names "Alfonsus, Elisabeth regina Portugalli…Rex Iacobus, Dominus Fridericus, domina Violanta et dominus Petrus" as the children of "Petro regi Aragonum" and
2 CONC  his wife[565].  The Chronicle of Ramon Muntaner records the death of "l´infant Pierre…ainsi que Raimond d´Anglesola" at the siege of León and their burial in adjacent graves in Aragon[566].  m (28 Aug 1291) GUILLELMA de Béarn, da
2 CONC ughter of GASTON [VII] de Moncada Vicomte de Béarn & his first wife Mathe [Amata] de Marsan [Mastas] Ctss de Bigorre ([1245/55]-1309).  The Chronicle of Ramon Muntaner records the marriage of "l´infant Pierre" and "madame Guillelm
2 CONC ine de Muncada, fille de Gaston de Béarn", dated to 1295[567].  She had previously been betrothed to Alfonso Manuel, and later to the latter's first cousin the future Sancho IV King of Castile.  Pedro had two illegitimate children
2 CONC  by unknown mistresses: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         ALFONSO de Aragón (-[2 Apr 1321/12 Mar 1325]).  Cingolani cites a document of King Jaime II dated 2 Apr 1321 which names “Alfonso et Ferdinando filiis nobilis Petri quondam fratris nostri”, suggesting that he died befor
2 CONC e the 12 Mar 1325 cited below under his brother in which Alfonso is not named[568]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         FERNANDO de Aragón (-after 12 Mar 1325).  Cingolani cites a document of King Jaime II dated 2 Apr 1321 which names “Alfonso et Ferdinando filiis nobilis Petri quondam fratris nostri”[569].  Cingolani cites another docum
2 CONC ent of King Jaime II dated 12 Mar 1325 which names “Ferferrandello, filiio nobilis Petri de Aragonia, quondam ffratris nostri”[570]. 
