2 CONT 7.          ALFONSO Pérez de Aragón ([1255/56]-after 1269).  Cingolani records his parentage, noting that he was recorded Jan 1269 as “escudero” which suggests his birth [1255/56] and in turn suggests that Juana was therefore his 
2 CONC mother[571].  King Jaime I granted revenue from “un horno que poseía en Xàtiva” to “Alfonso Petri, nepoti nostro” by charter dated 21 May 1268[572].  same person as...?  ALFONSO Pérez (-after 1286).  Cingolani suggests that he cou
2 CONC ld be the same person named “entre los nobles aragoneses en una convocatoria de Cortes de 1286”, but commenting that “la distancia temporal entre 1269 y 1286...no permite estar seguros”[573]. 
