2 CONT 8.          TERESA Pérez de Aragón (before 1260-after 27 Oct 1285).  Zurita names “el Rey...Doña Teresa Perez su hija” as the wife of “D. Artal de Alagon”[574].  Bofarull names “Da Inés Zapata” as mother of the king’s illegitimate
2 CONC  children “…la hija…Da Teresa y casó con D. Garcia Romeu que murió sin sucesion”, adding that Teresa “casó segunda vez con Artal de Alagon, y viuda de este pasó á terceras nupcias, segun Zurita, con D. Pedro Lopez de Oteiza” (no s
2 CONC ources cited)[575].  Cingolani corrects her parentage, recording that Juana was her mother, and suggests her birth “algún tiempo antes de 1260” given the date of death of her first husband[576].  A document dated 27 Oct 1285 recor
2 CONC ds payments, guaranteed from income from Lérida, to “dompne Iohanne, matri dompne Taresie Petri, uxor nobilis Artaldi de Alagone”[577].  The primary source which confirms her third marriage has not been identified.  m firstly GARC
2 CONC ÍA Romeu [III], son of GARCÍA Romeu [II] & his first wife --- (-before 2 Jan 1275).  Ricohombre de Aragón.  m secondly ([1278/79?]) ARTAL de Alagón Señor de Sástago y Pina, son of BLASCO de Alagón & his wife Jusiana Jiménez de Ent
2 CONC ença y de Luesia (-1295).  m thirdly (after 1295) PEDRO López de Oteiza, son of ---.    
