2 CONT 10.       PEDRO de Aragón (-after 1314).  The Nobiliario of Pedro Conde de Barcelos names "D. Pedro de Aragon" as the son of "el Rey D. Pedro" and "D. Ines Zapata"[579].  Bofarull names “Da Inés Zapata” as mother of the king’s ill
2 CONC egitimate children “D. Fernando señor de Albarracín, D. Pedro que casó en Portugal con Da Constanza Mendez Pelita, y D. Sancho castellan de Amposta : la hija…Da Teresa y casó con D. Garcia Romeu que murió sin sucesion” (no sources
2 CONC  cited)[580].  Salazar y Castro records the testament of Isabel Queen of Portugal, dated 1314, in which she bequeathed money to “Don Pedro, mi hermano, y à su hijo, qualquiera de ellos, que quedàre por mi muerte”[581].  m (Portuga
2 CONC l) CONSTANZA Mendez Pelita de Silva, daughter of SUERO Mendez de Silva & his wife María Annes Brochardo.  The Nobiliario of Pedro Conde de Barcelos records that "D. Pedro de Aragon", son of "el Rey D. Pedro" and "D. Ines Zapata", 
2 CONC married "D. Constança Mendez Petite"[582].  Pedro & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         PEDRO de Aragón .  The Nobiliario of Pedro Conde de Barcelos names "D. Pedro de Aragon, D. Fernando que fue asaz bueno, i casó" as the sons of "D. Pedro de Aragon" and his wife "D. Constança Mendez Petite"[583]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         FERNANDO de Aragón .  The Nobiliario of Pedro Conde de Barcelos names "D. Pedro de Aragon, D. Fernando que fue asaz bueno, i casó" as the sons of "D. Pedro de Aragon" and his wife "D. Constança Mendez Petite"[584].  m M
2 CONC ARÍA Núñez, daughter of NUÑO Fernández Cogominho & his wife Margarita de Albarnaz.  Salazar y Acha does not record Fernando’s marriage, although he says that he died “sin hijos”[585].  The primary source which confirms the informa
2 CONC tion has not been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT c)          CONSTANZA de Aragón .  The Nobiliario of Pedro Conde de Barcelos names "D. Constança. D. Teresa Alonso" as the daughters of "D. Pedro de Aragon" and his wife "D. Constança Mendez Petite"[586].  m GONZALO Annes Pimentel
2 CONC , son of ---. 
