2 CONT 12.       BEATRIZ de Aragón (-Portugal before 16 Nov 1316, bur Coimbra Santa Clara).  Bofarull names “una Señora llamada doña María” as mother of the king’s illegitimate children “D. Jaime Perez, D. Juan y Da Beatriz que casó con 
2 CONC D. Ramon de Cardona” (no sources cited)[589].  Cingolani corrects her parentage, recording that Inés Zapata was her mother citing a document which records “Beatricem, filia dicti domini regis Petri et Agnetis Çapate”[590].  Zurita
2 CONC  records that “don Ramon de Cardona” married “doña Beatriz de Aragon hija del Rey don Pedro”[591].  King Jaime II named “nobilis Beatrix, dorore nostra, uxoris quondam Raymundi de Cardona” in a document dated 16 Nov 1316 noting hi
2 CONC s worry about her children having been informed of her death[592].  Ferrer Mallol records her place of burial[593].  m RAMÓN de Cardona, son of --- (-Catalonia [1338]).  
