2 CONT 13.       JAIME Pérez de Aragón ([1265?]-after 9 Feb 1296).  Bofarull names “una Señora llamada doña María” as mother of the king’s illegitimate children “D. Jaime Perez, D. Juan y Da Beatriz que casó con D. Ramon de Cardona” (no 
2 CONC sources cited)[594].  Zurita records that “el Rey” granted “la ciudad de Segorbe” to “Don Jayme Perez su hijo natural” and married him to “Doña Sancha Fernandez hija de Don Hernando Diaz” in Nov 1279[595].  Señor de Segorbe.  Cing
2 CONC olani records the testament of Jaime Pérez de Aragón, dated 20 May 1285, which chose burial “en Poblet”, bequeathed property to his mother, his “amita, la infanta Sancha”, and “las dos hijas de la hermana de su madre, Suave”[596].
2 CONC   A charter dated 9 Feb 1296 requested listed Catalonian nobles to help Fernando IV King of Castile, including “…Jacobo Petri, domino Segorbe…”[597].  m (Nov 1279) SANCHA Fernández, daughter of FERNANDO Díaz & his wife ---.  Zurit
2 CONC a records that “el Rey” granted “la ciudad de Segorbe” to “Don Jayme Perez su hijo natural” and married him to “Doña Sancha Fernandez hija de Don Hernando Diaz” in Nov 1279[598].  Jaime & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         CONSTANZA de Aragón (after 20 May 1285-before 9 Apr 1313).  Constanza was not named in her father’s 20 May 1285 testament, cited above, so must have been born later.  Cariñena records that “don Artal de Luna…acrecentó m
2 CONC ucho el estado” by his first marriage (which he dates to “año 1309”) with “doña Constanza, hija de don Jayme Pérez, señor de Segorve, hijo del rey de Aragón…” with whom he had “la ciudad de Segorve y la villa y castillo de Trasmoz
2 CONC ”[599].  Zurita records the marriage in Mar 1299 of “Artal de Luna hijo de Don Lope” and “D. Jayme Perez señor de Segorbe y Doña Sancha Fernandez Diaz su muger...Doña Costança hija”[600].  Señora de Segorbe.  She is named as decea
2 CONC sed in the following document: Cariñena records that “don Artal de Luna, como tutor de Artalico de Luna, su hijo, y de doña Constanza, su muger difunta” swore homage 9 Apr 1313 “al rey por los feudos de la ciudad de Segorve y por 
2 CONC el castillo y villa de Trasmoz”[601].  m (Mar 1299) as his first wife, ARTAL [II] de Luna Señor de Luna, son of LOPE Ferrench de Luna & his wife Eva Jiménez de Urrea (-Sardinia [1323], bur Santa María de Veruela).
