2 CONT 15.       JUAN Benet, from Daroca (-1315).  Cingolani suggests the future king’s relationship with “una mujer llamada Muñina, de Daroca. Posiblemente...en los primeros años 1270”, noting a claim in late 1304 made by “Juan Benet de
2 CONC  Daroca” that he was the king’s son and the resulting inquiry dated 22 Feb 1306 by “el Justicia de Aragón, Jimeno Pérez de Salanova”[603].  Cingolani records that King Jaime II recognised Juan, gave him “un cargo eclesiástico”, an
2 CONC d paid for “las ceremonías fúnebres cuando murió en 1315”[604]. 
