2 CONT 16.       MELIADÚS (Messina [late 1283/early 1284]-after 21 Apr 1347).  Cingolani records the king’s relationship with “una anónima mujer siciliana...entre septiembre de 1282 y mayo de 1283...cuando el rey Pedro estuve en Sicilia”
2 CONC , noting that in early 1325 “un llamado Meliadús” came from Siciliy and presented himself in Barcelona to King Jaime II who “acepta la validez de las pruebas...y se le dirige como hermano”, although he “no obtuvo nada de su medio 
2 CONC hermano” and returned to Sicily where he was recorded “entre los prisoneros de la batalla de Lípari en 1339”[605].  Sciascia records “Macalda Scaletta, moglie del capitano [di Messina] Alaimo da Lentini” as the mother of Meliadús 
2 CONC whose career she discusses, including his last mention dated 21 Apr 1347[606].  m SIBILA de Queralt, daughter of BERNAT de Queralt & his wife Gerolda ---.  Sciascia records her parentage and marriage[607].  Meliadús & his wife had
2 CONC  one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         GIOVANNA (-Messina Aug 1347).  Sciascia records her parentage, as a nun “nel monasterio reale di S. Chiara di Messina”, and a document of Pope Clement VI recording her last sacraments dated Aug 1347[608]. 
