2 CONT 17.       SANCHO Pérez de Aragón ([Mar/May] 1284-[20 Sep 1334/end 1335]).  Cingolani records a document dated 15 Dec 1292, in which King Jaime II ordered payments to “dompna María Pérez de lo Gronyo, mater Sancii, filii...domini r
2 CONC egis Petri, clare memorie patris nostri”, and dates King Pedro’s presence in Logroño “entre el 10 de junio y finales del mes de agosto de 1283” and Sancho’s birth “entre marzo y mayo de 1284”[609].  Cingolani records a document da
2 CONC ted 1305, in which King Jaime II appointed “nobilem Sancium de Aragonia, fratrem” in a mission against the Byzantines, Sancho’s service in Sicily for King Federico III, his marriage there “antes de 1326, con Macalda, hija de Vinci
2 CONC gerra Pallizi”, his testament dated 20 Sep 1334, and the record of his being deceased “en los últimos meses de 1335”[610].  m (before 1326, in Sicily) MACALDA, daughter of VINCIGERRA Pallizi & his wife ---.  Cingolani records her 
2 CONC parentage and marriage, as noted above.  Sancho & his wife had two children: 
