2 CONT * '''RICHARD de Clare''', son of GILBERT de Clare Earl of Gloucester and Hereford & his wife Isabel Marshal of Pembroke (4 Aug 1222-Ashenfield in Waltham, near Canterbury 15 Jul 1262, bur Tonbridge, transferred 28 Jul 1262 to Tewk
2 CONC esbury)....'''m''' secondly (25 Jan 1238 or before) [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm#MaudLacydied1287 '''MATILDA de Lacy'''], daughter of JOHN de Lacy Earl of Lincoln & his second wife Margaret 
2 CONC de Quincy (-[1287/10 Mar 1289]).....'''Earl Richard & his second wife had seven children:'''
2 CONT ** 1. '''ISABEL''' (1240-murdered before 1271). The Annals of Tewkesbury record the birth in May 1240 of “''filia…Isabel''” to “''Ricardo de Clare''”[1954]. The ''Chronica de Fundatoribus et Fundatione'' of Tewkesbury Abbey names 
2 CONC “''Isabella primogenita, Margareta et Roysea''” as the three daughters of “''Ricardus de Clare secundus filius et hæres…Gilberti et Isabellæ''” and his wife “''Matildem…filiam comitis Lincolniæ''”[1955]. The Annals of Tewkesbury r
2 CONC ecord the marriage in Jun 1258 “''apud Leouns''” of “''Isabel filia Ricardi de Clare primogenita''” and “''domino Marchio de Ponte Ferato''”, recording that “''Willelmus de Bekeford monachus Theokesberiæ''” went with her[1956]. Th
2 CONC e ''Chronica Jacobi de Aquis'', dated to 1334, records that "''Marchio Guliermus''" married "''filiam regis Angliæ''" and that he killed her "''et dicitur sine caussa ex sola et levi suspicione''"[1957]. 
2 CONT ** '''m''' (Lyon Jun 1258) as his second wife, [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MONFERRATO,%20SALUZZO,%20SAVONA.htm#GuglielmoVIIdied1292 '''GUGLIELMO VII Marchese di Monferrato'''], son of BONIFAZIO II Marchese di Monferrato & hi
2 CONC s wife Marguerite de Savoie (–in prison Alessandria 8 Feb 1292).
2 CONT
2 CONT >https://thepeerage.com/p61486.htm#i614854
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud de Lacy, Countess of Lincoln
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud de Lacy, Countess of Lincoln (1223 – 1287) was the daughter of John de Lacy, Earl of Lincoln (1192-1240) and Margaret de Quincy (1208-1266). She married Richard de Clare, 6th Earl of Hertford. Their known children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Isabel de Clare (1240-1270), who married William of Montferrat;
2 CONT 2) Gilbert de Clare, 7th Earl of Hertford;
2 CONT 3) Thomas de Clare (1245-1287);
2 CONT 4) Bogo de Clare (1248-1294);
2 CONT 5) Margaret de Clare (1249-1313), who married Edmund, Earl of Cornwall;
2 CONT 6) Rohese de Clare (1252-after 1299), who married Roger de Mowbray; and
2 CONT 7) Eglentina de Clare, who died in infancy in 1257.
2 CONT
2 CONT William VII, Marquess of Montferrat
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT William was the eldest son of Boniface II and Margaret of Savoy. He was named his father's heir in a testament of 1253, the year of his father's passing and his succession. He remained under his mother's regency until 1257. Upon a
2 CONC ttaining his majority, he married Isabella, daughter Richard de Clare, in 1258. William's mother was a first cousin of Eleanor of Provence, queen consort of England, and it was through the latter's influence that the marriage was 
2 CONC arranged.
