2 CONT 6.             CHARLES de France (Creil, Oise 18 Jun 1294-Château du Bois de Vincennes 1 Feb 1328, bur église de l'Abbaye royale de Saint-Denis).  Comte de La Marche 1314.  He succeeded his brother in 1322 as CHARLES IV "le Bel" K
2 CONC ing of France, CARLOS I King of Navarre.  He was consecrated at Notre-Dame de Reims 21 Feb 1322.  The necrology of Sainte-Chapelle records the death "Kal Feb" of "Karoli Francie et Navarre regis"[436].  m firstly (before Apr 1308,
2 CONC  repudiated 7 Sep 1322) BLANCHE de Bourgogne, daughter of OTTO de Chalon Comte de Bourgogne & his wife Mahaut Ctss d’Artois (1296-Abbaye de Maubuisson Apr 1326).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has no
2 CONC t yet been identified.  She was accused and convicted of adultery, imprisoned at Château-Gaillard 26 Aug 1319-21 May 1321, then repudiated by Charles on the grounds of consanguinity.  She became a nun at the Abbaye de Maubuisson a
