1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joan, Countess of Blois
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from Joanne of Châtillon)
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan of Châtillon (died 1292), was countess of Blois from 1280 to 1292, and lady of Avesnes.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of John I and Alix of Brittany. Her maternal grandparents were John I, Duke of Brittany and Blanche of Navarre.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1263, Joanne married Pierre of Alençon, son of Louis IX of France and Marguerite of Provence. They had 2 children who died young. Pierre died in 1283.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan, Countess of Blois
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from Joanne of Châtillon)
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan of Châtillon (died 1292), was countess of Blois from 1280 to 1292, and lady of Avesnes.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of John I and Alix of Brittany. Her maternal grandparents were John I, Duke of Brittany and Blanche of Navarre.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1263, Joanne married Pierre of Alençon, son of Louis IX of France and Marguerite of Provence. They had 2 children who died young. Pierre died in 1283.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan received the County of Chartres from her father during his life; she later sold these lands to Philip IV of France in 1291. She ceded the lordship of Avesnes to her cousin Hugh before her death. When she died in 1292 the othe
2 CONC r titles were left to him, too.
