2 CONT 16.      ['''BLANCHE''' (-young).  A manuscript, maybe of Welsh origin and which names Henry VI at the end so can presumably be dated to his reign, names “...Beatrix quæ moritur puella, Blanchia quæ moritur puella” at the end of a
2 CONC  list of children of King Edward I[815].  Inaccuracies are noted elsewhere in this document, so its historical value is difficult to assess.  The existence of these daughters Beatrix and Blanche has not been corroborated in other 
2 CONC primary source documents.] 
