1 NOTE DIED YOUNG; HENRY III GAVE ORDERS FOR THE PROVISION OF A "GOOD AND FAIR CLOTH
2 CONT OF GOLD" TO COVER HER TOMB
1 NOTE Known as Joan of Acre from her place of birth.
1 NOTE KNOWN AS "JOAN OF ACRES"; COUNTESS OF GLOUCESTER; WHILE STILL AN INFANT SHE WAS
2 CONT BETROTHED TO HARTMAN, SON OF RUDOLPH OF HAPSBURG - 1ST WEDDING DATE SET FOR
2 CONT SPRING OF 1276, BUT POSTPONED BECAUSE OF WARFARE BETWEEN RUDOLPH AND COUNT OF
2 CONT SAVOY (OF WHICH THE DOWAGER QUEEN DISAPPROVED) - 2ND DATE FIXED FOR 4/1279 BUT
2 CONT WAS ALSO POSTPONED - HARTMAN DROWNED ON SUNDAY BEFORE CHRISTMAS 1282
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-2782
1 NOTE
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  Joan was also Countess of Gloucester and Hertford.  Her father had arranged for her to be married to Amadeus of Savoy, but she had already secretly married to Ralph Monthermer, Earl Gloucester & Hertford, a member of the Kings
2 CONC  household. Unknown GEDCOM info: MH:N132 Unknown GEDCOM info: ABB75B45-74D6-462E-9D2F-F0556B3C25F7
