2 CONT ====Medlands: [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLAND,%20Kings%201066-1603.htm#Margaretdied1318Or1333 England, Kings 1066-1603]
2 CONT * 11. '''BERENGARIA''' (Kennington Palace, Surrey 1 May [1276 or 1277]-young). The Continuator of Florence of Worcester records the birth in 1276 of "''filiam…Berengariam" to "Alienor regina''"[818]. The Annals of Winchester recor
2 CONC d the birth “''Kal Mai…apud Kenyngtone''” in 1276 of “''Alianora regina domino Edwardi regi Angliæ…filiam…---''”[819].  The Chronicle of John de Oxenedes records that “''Alianora regina''” gave birth to “''filiam...Berengarium''”,
2 CONC  dated to 1276 from the context[820]. '''If the birth of Margaret is correctly recorded in 1275 [sic] as shown above, Berengaria must have been born prematurely if born in 1276.  An alternative possibility is that the year was inc
2 CONC orrectly recorded and should have been 1277.'''
