2 CONT Alexander III 'the Glorius', King of Scotland1
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #102227, b. 4 September 1241, d. 19 March 1286
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander III 'the Glorius', King of Scotland was born on 4 September 1241 at Roxburgh, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Alexander II 'the Peaceful', King of Scotland and Mary de Coucy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, firstly, Margaret of England, Princess of England, daughter of Henry III, King of England and Eleanor of Provence, on 26 December 1251 at York Minster, York, Yorkshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Yolande de Dreux, daughter of Robert IV de Dreux, Comte de Dreux and Beatrix de Montfort, Comtesse de Montfort, on 1 November 1285 at Jedburgh Abbey, Roxburghshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also reported to have been married on 14 October 1285. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 19 March 1286 at age 44 at Kinghorne, Fife, Scotland, when his horse plunged over a cliff.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was buried at Dunfermline Abbey, Dunfermline, Fife, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander III 'the Glorius', King of Scotland succeeded to the title of King Alexander III of Scotland on 8 July 1249.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was crowned King of Scotland on 13 July 1249 at Scone Abbey, Scone, Perthshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He has an extensive biographical entry in the Dictionary of National Dictionary.4
2 CONT
