1 NOTE KNOWN AS "DE BRETAGNE"; DUKE OF BRITTANY; 7TH EARL OF RICHMOND; KNIGHTED IN
2 CONT LONDON BY HENRY III 12/13/1260; ACCOMPANIED FATHER IN 1270 AT SEIGE OF TUNIS;
2 CONT PRESENT AT EDWARD'S (HIS BROTHER-IN-LAW) CORONATION 8/19/1274; TOOK PART IN
2 CONT FRENCH INVASION OF ARAGON IN 1285; CREATED A PAPAL DUKE IN 1288, AND WENT TO
2 CONT LYONS IN 1305 FOR THE CORONATION OF POPE CLEMENT V (DURING PROCESSION THERE ON
2 CONT 11/14/1305, A WALL COLLAPSED AND HE WAS MORTALLY INJURED)
