1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marie de Bretagne (1268 - 1339)
2 CONT
2 CONT MARIE de Bretagne (1268-5 May 1339, bur Abbaye de Cercamp).  Heiress of Clermont.  Dame d'Elincourt et d'Arleux 1317.  m (22 Jul 1292) GUY [III] de Châtillon Comte de Saint-Pol, son of GUY [II] de Châtillon Comte de Saint-Pol & hi
2 CONC s wife Beatrix de Brabant (-6 Apr 1317).  
2 CONT
2 CONT parents:  JEAN de Bretagne, son of JEAN I Duke of Brittany & his wife Infanta doña Blanca de Navarra [Champagne] and  BEATRIX of England, daughter of HENRY III King of England & his wife Eléonore de Provence.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRITTANY.htm#MarieBretagnedied1339
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie of Brittany
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Not to be confused with Mary of Brittany
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie of Brittany (1268-1339) was the daughter of John II, Duke of Brittany and Beatrice of England. She is also known as Marie de Dreux
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Her maternal grandparents were Henry III of England and Eleanor of Provence, Henry was a son of King John of England. John was son of Henry II of England and his wife Eleanor of Aquitaine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her sister was Blanche of Brittany, wife to Philip of Artois and mother of Margaret of Artois, Robert III of Artois and Jeanne of Artois. Margaret was mother of Jeanne d'Évreux, Queen of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Guy IV, Count of Saint-Pol in 1292, their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT John of Châtillon (d. 1344), Count of Saint Pol
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacques of Châtillon (d.s.p. 1365), Lord of Ancre
2 CONT
2 CONT Mahaut of Chatillon (1293–1358), married Charles of Valois
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrix of Châtillon, married in 1315 Jean de Dampierre, Lord of Crevecoeur
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabeau of Châtillon (d. May 19, 1360), married in May 1311 Guillaume I de Coucy, Lord of Coucy
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie of Châtillon, married Aymer de Valence, 2nd Earl of Pembroke
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor of Châtillon, married Jean III Malet, Lord of Granville
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne of Châtillon, married Miles de Noyers, Lord of Maisy
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Descendents
2 CONT
2 CONT Through her daughter Mahaut, Marie is the maternal grandmother of Marie of Valois, Isabella of Valois who became Duchess of Bourbon and was the mother of Louis II, Duke of Bourbon and Joanna of Bourbon who became Queen of France. 
2 CONC Mahaut's other daughter was Blanche of Valois, who married Charles IV, Holy Roman Emperor and was the mother of Katharine of Bohemia.
