2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Berthold IV (died 12 August 1204) was the Count of Andechs (from 1172) and first Duke of Merania, that is, the seacoast of Dalmatia and Istria, of the House of Andechs. He was the son of Berthold I of Istria and Hedwig of Wittelsb
2 CONC ach.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1175, he was raised to the margraviate of Istria and then years later (1185) made the duke of the region called "Merania" after the Adriatic Sea (mare is Latin for "sea"). Merania encompassed the same area as the old margraviat
2 CONC e, but its ruler now gained much prestige from his new title.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1186, he accompanied the Emperor Henry VI to the Kingdom of Sicily. In 1189, he led the third division of the imperial army and was its standard-bearer on the Third Crusade. In 1195, he appeared as the advocate of Tegernsee Abb
2 CONC ey. After Henry's death in 1197, he sided with the claimant Philip of Swabia. At this juncture, the duke of Merania was at the height of his power and influence. He possessed lands from Franconia to the Adriatic.
2 CONT
2 CONT Berthold died in 1204 and was buried in Diessen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Berthold married Agnes of Rochlitz, and they had the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Otto I, who succeeded his father
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Ekbert, bishop of Bamberg
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Henry, margrave of Istria
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Hedwig, married Henry I the Bearded, duke of Silesia
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Gertrude, married Andrew II of Hungary
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Agnes, married Philip II of France
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Berthold, patriarch of Aquileia
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Mathilde, abbess of Klitzingen
2 CONT
2 CONT An unnamed daughter married into the Nemanjic family of Serbia
2 CONT
