1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://thepeerage.com/p10521.htm#i105210 '''thepeerage.com''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne III, Countess of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan of Burgundy (2 May 1308 – 1349), also known as Jeanne de Bourgogne or Jeanne de France was the eldest daughter of King Philip V of France and Joanna II of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married in 1318 to Eudes IV, Duke of Burgundy, as part of a settlement between the two men regarding the French succession (Eudes had previously supported the right of his niece - and Jeanne's cousin - Joan to inherit the 
2 CONC French throne); Jeanne thus became Duchess-consort of Burgundy. She became Countess of Burgundy and Artois in her own right in 1330, following the death of her mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne bore six children. With the exception of Philip, all were stillborn or died in infancy. Philip predeceased her; her titles therefore passed to her grandson, Philip I of Burgundy upon her death in 1349.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Died young.
