1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Geoffrey I of Villehardouin (French: Geoffroi Ier de Villehardouin) (c. 1169–c. 1229) was a French knight from the County of Champagne who joined the Fourth Crusade. He participated in the conquest of the Peloponne
2 CONC se and became the second prince of Achaea and Andravida (1209/1210–c. 1229).
2 CONT
2 CONT Under his reign, the principality became the direct vassal of the Latin Empire of Constantinople. He extended the borders of his principality, but the closing years of his rule were marked by his conflict with the church.
