2 CONT RICCARDO Orsini, son of MAIO [Orsini] Count of Kefalonia & his wife Anna Komnene Angelina (-murdered 1304 before 7 Apr).  Count of Kefalonia [1264].  He became the indirect vassal of Charles I King of Sicily [Anjou-Capet] when the
2 CONC  latter signed the first Treaty of Viterbo 23 May 1267 with Guillaume II Prince of Achaia who accepted Angevin suzerainty[641].  Conte di Gravina 1284/91.  Vicar General of Corfu 1286/89.  He was appointed bailli of Achaia by Isab
2 CONC elle Pss of Achaia in 1297[642].   The Livre de la Conqueste de la Morée records that “li contes Richard” was killed “à Clarence par un sien chevalier…messire Lion”[643]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly ---.  The name of Riccardo's first wife is not known.   ''(six children)''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (1299) as her second husband, MARGUERITE de Villehardouin Lady of Matagriphon (Akova) and Katochi, widow of ISNARD de Sabran, daughter of GUILLAUME de Villehardouin Prince of Achaia & his [third] wife Anna Komneno
2 CONC dukaina of Epirus (-Feb 1315).  The Livre de la Conqueste de la Morée records that “li contes Richart” married “la dame de Mathe-Griphon, la suer de la princesse Ysabeau”[644].  She died in prison. 
