1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matilda_of_Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda (Mechtilde) of Savoy (1390–1438) was a daughter of Amadeo, Prince of Achaea (also known as Amadeus of Piedmont or Amadeus of Savoy) and Catherine of Geneva. She was the second wife of the Elector Palatine Louis III, whom s
2 CONC he married on 30 November 1417.
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda had the following five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mathilde (7 March 1419 – 1 October 1482), married:
2 CONT in 1434 to Count Louis I of Württemberg
2 CONT in 1452 to Duke Albrecht VI of Austria
2 CONT Louis IV, Elector Palatine (1 January 1424 – 13 August 1449)
2 CONT Frederick I, Elector Palatine (1 August 1425 – 12 December 1476)
2 CONT Rupprecht (27 February 1427 – 26 July 1480), Prince-elector archbishop of Cologne
2 CONT Margarete (ca. 1428 – 23 November 1466), a nun at Liebenau monastery
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT - https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathilde_de_Savoie_(1390-1438)_
