1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''AMAURY [III] de Craon ([1280]-26 Jan 1333, bur Angers Cordeliers).  Seigneur de Craon.'''
2 CONT s/o MAURICE [V] Seigneur de Craon & Mathilde Berthout van Mechelen 
2 CONT x (contract 24 Aug 1300) ISABELLE de Sainte-Maure ([1290]-15 Dec 1310, bur Angers Cordeliers)
2 CONT *MAURICE [VII] de Craon ([1304]-8 Aug 1330, bur Angers Cordeliers).  Seigneur de Sainte-Maure et de Marcillac. 
2 CONT xx (contract Oct 1312) BEATRIX de Roucy (-7 Nov 1328, bur Angers Cordeliers)
2 CONT *AMAURY de Craon (-7 May 1334, bur Angers Cordeliers)
2 CONT * ISABELLE de Craon (-25 Feb 1334, bur Angers Cordeliers)
2 CONT *BEATRIX de Craon (-after 3 Aug 1382).
2 CONT *PIERRE de Craon (-19 Nov 1376, bur Angers Cordeliers)
2 CONT * GUILLAUME de Craon (after 15 Apr 1318-8 Jun 1387, bur Châteaudun, Abbaye des Cordeliers).
2 CONT *JEAN de Craon (-Paris 11 Apr 1374, bur Paris Cordeliers) Bishop of Le Mans 1348.  Archbishop of Reims *SIMON de Craon (after May 1322-26 Jan 1333, bur Angers Cordeliers). 
2 CONT *MARGUERITE de Craon (after May 1322-26 Aug 1336).  Nun at Longchamp. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/anjounob.htm#MarieCraonMGuyLaval
2 CONT ----
2 CONT AMAURY [III] de Craon, son of MAURICE [V] Seigneur de Craon & his wife Mathilde Berthout van Mechelen ([1280]-26 Jan 1333, bur Angers Cordeliers).  Seigneur de Craon.  “Ysabellis de Lezigniaco domina de Bellovidere supra mare, Pic
2 CONC taviensis dyœcesis” declared to “nepoti suo Almaurrico de Creone” that she had often heard from “dominum Gauffridum de Ranconio quondam maritum meum”, from whose successors he had inherited “in castro et castellania de Marcilhiaco
2 CONC ”, that these properties were fiefs of the bishop of Angoulême, by charter dated 16 Aug 1304[330].  “Almarricus de Credonio miles, dominus de Marcilhiaco” gave homage to the bishop of Angoulême for his rights in Marcillac, “racion
2 CONC e Hysabellis uxoris nostræ filiæ quondam domini Guillelmi de Sancta Maura olim domini de Marcilhiaco”, by charter dated 16 Apr 1309[331].  The testament of "Amauri seignour de Craon et de Sablé", dated 1 Mar 1311 (O.S.), requests 
2 CONC the performance of the testamentary dispositions of “noustre...père et le madame Ysabeau de La Marche noustre...aiole et le noustre...compeigne”, entrusted money to “monssour Regnaut de Précigné [...noustre...cousin]...à porter po
2 CONC ur nous en la terre d’oustre mer”, and bequeathed property to “noz seurs...Johenne...noustre seur la dame de Cliceon”[332].  A manuscript of the Cordeliers d’Angers lists members of the Craon family buried "dans la chapelle Saint-
2 CONC Jean", including “Monsieur Almaury sire de Craon...filz de monsieur Morice sire de Craon et de madame Mahault de Maslines” who died 27 Jan 1332 (O.S.)[333]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly (contract 24 Aug 1300) ISABELLE de Sainte-Maure, daughter of GUILLAUME [V] Seigneur de Sainte-Maure & his wife Alix de Thouars ([1290]-15 Dec 1310, bur Angers Cordeliers).  The marriage contract between "Amaury seigneur 
2 CONC de Craon et de Sableill vallet" and "madame Agnès de Ponz dame de Maroylle [jadis fame monsour Guillaume seignour de Seincte More] [error?] et Alliz jadis fame Guillaume de Seincte More vallet...Ysabeau de Seincte More fille do di
2 CONC t Guillaume de Seincte More et de ladite Aalliz" is dated 24 Aug 1300[334].  “Almarricus de Credonio miles, dominus de Marcilhiaco” gave homage to the bishop of Angoulême for his rights in Marcillac, “racione Hysabellis uxoris nos
2 CONC træ filiæ quondam domini Guillelmi de Sancta Maura olim domini de Marcilhiaco”, by charter dated 16 Apr 1309[335].  A manuscript of the Cordeliers d’Angers lists members of the Craon family buried "dans la chapelle Saint-Jean", in
2 CONC cluding “Madame Ysabel de Saincte-Maure dame de Craon première femme de messire Amory sire de Craon” who died 15 Dec 1310[336]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly (contract Oct 1312) BEATRIX de Roucy, daughter of JEAN [IV] Comte de Roucy Seigneur de Pierrepont & his wife Jeanne de Dreux (-7 Nov 1328, bur Angers Cordeliers).  Philippe IV King of France ratified the marriage contra
2 CONC ct between “Amauri seigneur de Craon” and "Jehan conte de Roucy...damoiselle Béatrix seur dudit comte" by charter dated Oct 1312[337].  Heiress of la Suze, inherited from her mother[338].  The testament of “Jehanne de Dreux comtes
2 CONC se de Roucy et dame de Puisoye”, dated 1 Oct 1324, bequeathed property to “ma fille de Chastiauvillain [...Marie]...ma fille de Craon [...Beatrix]...ma fille de Rouci la Comtesse...ma fille Beatrix fille Jehan mon fil“[339].  A ma
2 CONC nuscript of the Cordeliers d’Angers lists members of the Craon family buried "dans la chapelle Saint-Jean", including “Madame Béatrix de Roucy dame de Craon et seconde femme de monsi
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/anjounob.htm#MarieCraonMGuyLaval
2 CONT
