1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''from http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgdatuy.htm#GuillaumeVergydied1409 v4.2 Updated 04 November 2018
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean & his first wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''GUILLAUME de Vergy''' (-killed in battle Nikopolis [28] Sep 1396).  Seigneur de Port-sur-Saône.  Seigneur de Montenot, de iure uxoris: “Jehan de Vergy sires de Fonuens” and “Brun sires de la Haute-Ribaupierre” agreed the divisi
2 CONC on of properties between the three daughters of the latter, comprising the succession of “Jeanne de Blammont jadis dame de la Haute-Ribeaupierre leur mere et de...Marguerite de Blammont dame de Puteleinges leur tante”, under which
2 CONC  “Ysabel de Ribaupierre femme de...Guillaume de Vergey fils dudit monseigneur de Fonuens” received “la forteresse et chastel de Montenot...”, by charter dated 17 Mar 1381 (O.S.?)[135].  “Jean de Vergy seigneur de Fouvent, Guillaum
2 CONC e son fils, et Isabelle sa femme fille de Brun de Ribeaupierre” relinquished their claim to Faucogney in favour of the duke of Burgundy by charter dated 1394[136].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m (Betrothed 20 Mar 1378, before 17 Mar 1382) ISABELLE von Rappoltstein, daughter of BRUNO Herr von Rappoltstein [Haute-Ribeaupierre] & his first wife Jeanne de Blâmont.  A charter dated 20 Mar 1377 (O.S.?) records an agreement be
2 CONC tween “Brun seigneur de la Hauteribaupierre, Jean de Vergy seigneur de Fonuanz et seneschaulx de Bourgongne, messire Jehan de Chastel chevaliers” and “Brocars fils feu...Brocart seigneur de Fenestranges et de Pouruacre...Alixend s
2 CONC a femme fille dudit messire Brun et damoiselles Juhannette et Ysabel filles d’iceluy messire Brun”, noting that Bruno had been excluded from government and guardians appointed for his daughters “ladite Jeannette ledit messire Jean
2 CONC  de Chastel et à ladite Ysabel ledit messire Jean de Vergy”, for the marriage between “Guillaume de Vergey fils desdits messire Jean de Vergy et madame Jeanne de Chalon” and “damoiselle Ysabel fille desdits messire Brun et madame 
2 CONC Jeanne [de Blammont] sa femme et seur germaine desdites Ellesen [Alixend] et Jeannete”[137].  Dame de Montenot: “Jehan de Vergy sires de Fonuens” and “Brun sires de la Haute-Ribaupierre” agreed the division of properties between t
2 CONC he three daughters of the latter, comprising the succession of “Jeanne de Blammont jadis dame de la Haute-Ribeaupierre leur mere et de...Marguerite de Blammont dame de Puteleinges leur tante”, under which “Ysabel de Ribaupierre fe
2 CONC mme de...Guillaume de Vergey fils dudit monseigneur de Fonuens” received “la forteresse et chastel de Montenot...”, by charter dated 17 Mar 1381 (O.S.?)[138].  “Jean de Vergy seigneur de Fouvent, Guillaume son fils, et Isabelle sa
2 CONC  femme fille de Brun de Ribeaupierre” relinquished their claim to Faucogney in favour of the duke of Burgundy by charter dated 1394[139].  A document dated 18 Aug 1408 records a claim made by “Ioannam de Altarapinepetra dominam de
2 CONC  Migneariis relictam defuncti Folmerii de Guerolezek scutiferi et Ysabellim de Altarapinepetra dominam de Portu eius sororem relictam defuncti Guillelmi de Vergeio quondam militis, se gerentes heredes...defuncti Edouardi quondam d
2 CONC omini...de Vangione-rivo” against “Reginam” reciting that “defunctus Stephanus de Cabilone miles...dominus...de Vangione rivo et...eius matrimonio”, had “Ioannam de Cabilone eius filiam” who married “defuncto Guillelmo de Domnapet
2 CONC ra milite domino S. Desiderii et filio defuncti Iohannis de Domnapetra domini quondam S. Desiderii” and had “plures liberi...Iohannes...dominus...de Vangione-rivo et S. Desiderii...et Ysabellis...domina...de Vruilla et de Montenot
2 CONC ”, that “dictus...Ioannes” married “Alipdi de Auffemonte filia...quondam Marescalli Franciæ...de Nigella” by whom he had “Ioannes de S. Desiderio...magnus Coquus Franciæ ac dominus...de Vangione-rivo et de S. Desiderio” who marrie
2 CONC d “Maria de Barro” and had “dictum Eduardum” who died Aug 1401, that “defunctus quondam Guillelmus de Domnapetra miles ex sua uxore...de Asperomonte” had “duos liberos...Ioannem [incorrect, see 1317 charter] et Gaufredum”, the lat
2 CONC ter being father of “Henricum...dominus de Rupe” who was father of “Ioanna uxor...Ferrici [de Chardoigne]”[140].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillaume & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)       JEAN de Vergy (-19 Apr 1460, bur Theulay).<br/>
2 CONT (b)       GUILLEMETTE de Vergy .<br/>
2 CONT (c)       JEANNE de Vergy (-after 24 Jul 1439).<br/>
2 CONT (d)       MARGUERITE de Vergy .
2 CONT
