1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gauthier Aunay,  or Aulnay (circa 1288/1291 - Pontoise, April 19, 1314 ) was a Norman knight. He is famous for having been, from 1312, the lover of Margaret de Bourgogne , daughter of King Philip the Fair of France
2 CONC  , which earned him, and his brother, who was also accused of adultery,  a particularly cruel execution.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Gauthier V Aunay (died c. 1325 AD. 1318 / ) , Lord of Moucy -le- Neuf du Mesnil and Grand Moulin, he was married to Agnes de Montmorency, granddaughter Mathieu de Montmorency III , whose posterity : Philip II " Gal ( l) ois
2 CONC  " ( died before 1392, and posterity ) , Peter, John and Margaret Aunay ( or Aulnay ) .
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a Knight of the Count of Poitiers, second son of Philip the Fair . Convicted of adultery in the case of the Tour de Nesle,, he and his brother were  denounced by Isabelle , Queen of England (daughter of Philip the Fair ) , 
2 CONC who hated her sister Blanche. Interrogated under torture despite his rank, he  confessed to a 3 year affair,  and was sentenced for the crime of treason ( adultery would have  cast doubt on the legitimacy of royal issue) and impri
2 CONC soned at Pontoise with his brother Gauthier d' Aulnay particularly atrocious conditions.
2 CONT
2 CONT The "two young and bonny Knights " were broken on the wheel , skinned alive , emasculated , épendus lead sulfur boiling, then decapitated, dragged through streets, and hanged on the gallows there rotting for weeks. Their gender , 
2 CONC instruments of crime, thrown to the dogs . "Never will any body will suffer as much "  refers the chronique3 . Chateaubriand, in Historical Studies , reports the following verses : That they were alive ecorchiezPuis fu lor kind co
2 CONC péeAux dogs and beasts pier. He writes further: "They were skinned alive , dragged in Maubuisson newly mown meadow , mutilated, and hanged on a gibbet under the arms ."
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the contemporary chronicle 4:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Therefore , a kind of atoning death and ignominious a package so infamous punishment, they were at the sight of all Vivans skinned while in public . They are cut and manly genitals, and cut off their heads , they were dragged to 
2 CONC the public gallows where , stripped of their skin, they were hung by the shoulders and the joints of the arm. " Source: http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gauthier_d'Aunay
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://racineshistoire.free.fr/LGN/PDF/Aulnay.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://books.google.com/books?id=mAgDwx4pS0QC&pg=PA277&lpg=PA277&dq=robert+d'aulnay&source=bl&ots=WSupP7io0l&sig=dpaxBp825-chQR1gJtClP114wlA&hl=en&sa=X&ei=wy9SUpmAGIS88wS-noGIDw&ved=0CFMQ6AEwBDgy#v=onepage&q=robert%20d'aul
2 CONC nay&f=false
