1 NOTE
2 CONT 1.  Louis X, The Headstrong of France, was also Count of Champagne and King of Navarre 1305-1316. Unknown GEDCOM info: MH:N141 Unknown GEDCOM info: D5DDF96E-BBBC-4D25-838C-F10473952353
1 NOTE Louis X, called The Headstrong (1289-1316), king of France (1314-16), the 
2 CONT son of Philip IV. Influenced by his uncle, Charles de Valois (1270-1325), 
2 CONT he was preoccupied for much of his short reign with unrest among his 
2 CONT nobles, to whom he granted charters confirming their privileges, and with 
2 CONT an indecisive campaign against Flanders that he led in 1315. Louis's 
2 CONT posthumous son, John I, died five days old, and the succession went to 
2 CONT Louis's brother, Philip V.
1 NOTE Il fait face áa des râevoltes, notamment celles des Seigneurs qu'il calme par des concessions et le jugement d'Enguerrand de Marigny.
2 CONT Il se procure de l'argent en vendant des chartes d'affranchissement aux serfs et en dâepouillant les Juifs et les Lombards.
1 NOTE KNOWN AS "THE QUARRELSOME"; KING OF FRANCE 1314-1316 (ACCEDED 11/29/1314, AND
2 CONT CONSECRATED AT RHEIMS 8/29/1315); DIED OF A PULMONARY INFECTION
1 NOTE Ruled France 1314-1316. [GADD.GED]
