1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Frederick of Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick of Lorraine (1371 – October 25, 1415 in the battle of Agincourt) was Count of Vaudemont.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Duke John I of Lorraine and younger brother of Charles II. In 1393, Frederick married Margaret the heiress of Vaudemont and Joinville, and became Count of these lands in her right. He founded the House of Vaudemo
2 CONC nt, a junior branch of the Duchy of Lorraine.
2 CONT
2 CONT His children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Antoine, who succeeded as Count of Vaudemont,
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabelle, who married Philipp I of Nassau-Weilburg, and
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret, who married Thibault II of Blamont.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dynastic problems in the senior side made his great-grandson René of Vaudemont Duke of Lorraine in 1473.
