1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Isabelle de Saint-Pol de Valois (1313 - 1383)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella of Valois, Duchess of Bourbon
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella of Valois (1313 – August 26, 1388). Was a daughter of Charles of Valois and his third wife Mahaut of Chatillon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Her paternal grandparents were Philip IV of France and Isabella of Aragon. Her maternal grandparents were Guy IV, Count of Saint-Pol and Marie of Brittany. She was a sister of Blanche of Valois, who married Charles IV, Holy Roman 
2 CONC Emperor, Blanche's daughter was Katharine of Bohemia, Blanche died in 1348 at the age of 31. Isabella's other sister was Marie of Valois who married Charles, Duke of Calabria in 1323, Marie was the mother of Joan I of Naples. Isab
2 CONC ella had a brother called Louis, he became Count of Chartres but he died at the tender age of ten, Isabella, her mother and sisters were very upset. When her father died in 1325 all his titles went to Isabella's older half sibling
2 CONC s by his first marriage to Marguerite of Anjou and Maine. We know Isabella was born in 1313 but it is unknown what her exact birthday was.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Marriage and husband's death
2 CONT
2 CONT On 25 January 1326 she married Peter I, Duke of Bourbon, son of Louis I, Duke of Bourbon. Peter and Isabella had only one son, Louis and seven daughters. Her husband sadly died at the Battle of Poitiers in 1356, Isabella never rem
2 CONC arried. After her husbands death Isabella's son Louis became the Duke of Bourbon, in 1356 Isabella arranged for her daughter Jeanne to marry Charles V of France, at the time he was the Dauphin of France so Jeanne became Dauphine.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Name	Birth	Death	Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis II, Duke of Bourbon	1337	1410	Became Duke of Bourbon in 1356, married Anna of Auvergne, had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Joanna of Bourbon	1338	1378	Married Charles V of France, had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanca of Bourbon	1339	1361	Married Peter of Castile, she was murdered by him in 1361 and had no issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Bonne of Bourbon	1341	1402	Married Amadeus VI of Savoy, had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine of Bourbon	1342	1427	Married John VI, Count of Harcourt
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of Bourbon	1344	1416	Married Arnaud Amanieu, Lord of Albret, had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabelle of Bourbon	1345	1345	Died young
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary of Bourbon	1347	1401	Prioress of Poissy
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella outlived her eldest two daughters. Her husband suffered from madness, so this was passed on to the couples children. Jeanne and Louis were the only two of the seven children to suffer from madness. Nobody thought that Jea
2 CONC nne suffered from insanity until she had a nervous breakdown shortly after the birth of her seventh child Louis I de Valois, Duke of Orléans. Isabella's grandson Charles VI of France is well known for suffering from the mental dis
2 CONC order. In 1361 Isabella's daughter Blanca was murdered on the orders of her husband Pedro because he had fallen in love with Maria de Padilla, Blanca was either shot by a crossbowman or she was poisoned, Isabella was very upset to
2 CONC  hear of the death of her second eldest daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter I, Duke of Bourbon
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT On 25 January 1326 he married Isabella of Valois, daughter of Charles, Count of Valois and his third wife Mahaut of Chatillon. Peter and Isabella had only one son, Louis, and seven daughters. These were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne (1338–1378), married King Charles V of France
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche (1339–1361, Medina-Sidonia), married King Pedro of Castile in 1353 in Valladolid, poisoned by her husband
2 CONT
2 CONT Bonne (1341 – January 19, 1402, Château de Mâcon), married Amadeus VI, Count of Savoy in 1355 in Paris
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine (1342–1427, Paris), married John VI, Count of Harcourt
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret (1344–1416), married Arnaud Amanieu, Viscount of Tartas
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabelle (b. 1345)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (1347–1401, Poissy), Prioress of Poissy
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles of Valois
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Finally, in 1308, he married Mahaut of Chatillon (1293–1358), daughter of Guy III of Châtillon, Count of Saint Pol. They had also four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie of Valois (1309–1332). Married Charles, Duke of Calabria and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella de Valois (1313 – August 26, 1388). She married Peter I, Duke of Bourbon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche of Valois (1317–1348). She married Charles IV, Holy Roman Emperor. Sometimes called "Marguerite".
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis, Count of Chartres (1318–1328)
