2 CONT '''Successor'''	John I
2 CONT '''Born	1337'''
2 CONT '''Died	1410 (aged 73)'''
2 CONT '''Montluçon'''
2 CONT '''Spouse	Anne of Auvergne'''
2 CONT '''Issue'''	John I, Duke of Bourbon
2 CONT House	Bourbon
2 CONT '''Father'''	Peter I, Duke of Bourbon
2 CONT '''Mother'''	Isabella de Valois
2 CONT ________
2 CONT PIERRE de Bourbon, son of LOUIS I "le Boiteux" Duc de Bourbon & his wife Marie de Hainaut [Avesnes] ([1311]-killed in battle Poitiers 19 Sep 1356, bur Paris, église des Jacobins).  He succeeded his father in 1342 as PIERRE I Duc d
2 CONC e Bourbon, Comte de Clermont et de la Marche.  Governor General of Languedoc 8 Aug 1345. 
2 CONT m (Vincennes 5 Oct 1322) ISABELLE de Valois, daughter of CHARLES de France Comte de Valois & his third wife Mathilde de Châtillon Ctss de Saint-Pol (-Paris 26 Jul 1383, bur Paris, église des Frères mineurs).  The Chronique Parisie
2 CONC nne records the marriage “le mardi devant la feste saint Denys, v jours au moys d´Octobre au Boys de Vinciennes“ 1322 of “le filz à Louys conte de Clermont” and “la fille Charlez le conte de Valoiz”[247].  She became a nun at the 
2 CONC convent des Cordeliers du Faubourg Saint-Marceau, Paris.  The testament of "Ysabeau de Valoys duchesse de Bourbon", dated 25 Jan 1379 (O.S.), appointed "notre...filz Loys duc de Bourbon" as her main executor[248]. 
2 CONT Pierre & his wife had seven children: 
2 CONT '''1.         LOUIS de Bourbon (4 Aug 1337-Château de Montluçon 19 Aug 1410, bur Priory of Souvigny).  He succeeded his father in 1356 as LOUIS II "le Bon" Duc de Bourbon, Comte de Clermont.  A charter dated 18 May 1370 refers to 
2 CONC Louis Duc d´Anjou as "curateur de Mgr Jean de Forez", and records the authorisation by Charles V King of France of the transfer of the former´s rights in the county of Forez to Louis II Duc de Bourbon, husband of Comte Jean´s niec
2 CONC e Anne de Clermont[249].  Comte de Forez et de Roannais 15 May 1372, by right of his wife.  The testament of "Ysabeau de Valoys duchesse de Bourbon", dated 25 Jan 1379 (O.S.), appointed "notre...filz Loys duc de Bourbon" as her ma
2 CONC in executor[250].  The testament of "Louis duc de Bourbonnais comte de Clermont et de Forez", dated to [Apr 1390], appoints “son fils Jean” as his heir “sous la tutelle de sa femme, et à défaut de celle-ci sous la tutelle du duc d
2 CONC e Bourgogne, en considération du mariage projeté entre sondit fils et la fille du duc de Bourgogne”[251].  Head of the Council of Charles VI King of France.  Baron de Beaujeu et de Dombes 23 Jun 1400, by donation of Edouard Seigne
2 CONC ur de Beaujeu.  In return for his son inheriting the Duchy of Auvergne from his father-in-law Jean Duc de Berry, Duc Louis II agreed that the duchy of Bourbon and County of Clermont would revert to the French crown in case of exti
2 CONC nction of his male line.  This change in status of the patrimony of the Bourbon family into a simple apanage was especially significant in view of the previous transmission of the old seigneurie de Bourbon through the female line 
2 CONC on two occasions.  The testament of "Louis duc de Bourbon", dated 24 Jan 1409 (N.S.), chose burial at Souvigny priory, appointed “son fils Jean” as his heir, required that “si le même Jean a second fils” he should receive “en apan
2 CONC age la seigneurie de Beaujolais”, provided dowry for “sa fille Isabelle”, and appointed as executors “la duchesse sa femme, le duc de Berry, le comte de la Marche, le sire d’Albret”[252].  m (contract Montbrison 4 Jul 1368, in per
2 CONC son Ardes Jan 1370, Papal dispensation 15 Sep 1370) ANNE de Clermont Dame de Mercœur, daughter and heiress''' of BERAUD [II] Comte de Clermont [en Auvergne], Dauphin d'Auvergne & his first wife Jeanne de Forez dame d'Ussel (1358-C
2 CONC hâteau de Cleppé en Forez 22 Sep 1417, bur Priory of Souvigny).  Ctss de Forez.  "Domina Johanna de Borbonio, relicta…Guidonis comitis Forensis, comitissa Forensis" donated her rights in the county of Forez to "dominam Annam Dalph
2 CONC ine duchissam Borbonii, filiam suam et…dominum Ludovicem ducem Borbonii eius nepotem, conjuges" by charter dated 5 Jul 1382[253].  '''Louis Duc de Bourbon transferred his rights in the county of Forez to his wife by charter dated 
2 CONC 5 Jan 1383[254].  Dauphine de Clermont 1400'''.  The testament of "Johanna de Bourbonio comitissa Forensis, filiaque…domini Ludovici ducis Borbonii, comitis Claromontis et Marchie, et domine Marie Heynaut, coniugem, relicta…domini
2 CONC  Guidonis comitis Forensis quondam", dated 13 Jun 1400, bequeathed property to "dominum ducem Bourboni, comitem Claromontensem et Forensem, et Annam Dalphinam, duchissam Bourbonii, nepotem et filiam meos", and founded an anniversa
2 CONC ry for "domine Margarite de Sabbadia…sororgie mee, quondam consortis…fratris mei domini Reynaudi de Foresio"[255].  '''The testament of "Anne Dauphine duchesse douairière de Bourbonnais", dated 19 Sep 1416, appointed “son fils Jea
2 CONC n duc de Bourbon” as her heir[256].  Louis & his wife had four children:''' 
2 CONT a)         JEAN de Bourbon (Mar 1381-in prison London 5 Jan 1434, bur Priory of Souvigny).  The testament of "Louis duc de Bourbonnais comte de Clermont et de Forez", dated to [Apr 1390], appoints “son fils Jean” as his heir “sous
2 CONC  la tutelle de sa femme, et à défaut de celle-ci sous la tutelle du duc de Bourgogne, en considération du mariage projeté entre sondit fils et la fille du duc de Bourgogne”[257].  Comte de Clermont [Jul 1399].  Chamberlain of Fran
2 CONC ce 18 Mar 1408.  He succeeded his father in 1410 as JEAN I Duc de Bourbon.   
2 CONT -        see below. 
2 CONT b)         ISABELLE de Bourbon (-after 1451).  The testament of "Louis duc de Bourbon", dated 24 Jan 1409 (N.S.), provided dowry for “sa fille Isabelle”[258].  She became a nun at the Priory of Poissy.   Betrothed (1400) to ERIK V
2 CONC II King of Denmark and Norway, son of WARTISLAW VII Duke of Pomerania in Hinterpommern & his wife Marie von Mecklenburg-Schwerin ([1381]-Rügenwalde 1459 [after 4 Apr], bur Rügenwalde, Marienkirche). 
2 CONT c)         CATHERINE de Bourbon (-young).  La Mure names “la cadette...Catherine de Bourbon, elle mourut en jeunesse” but does not cite the source on which this information is based[259].  Père Anselme lists her as the older daugh
2 CONC ter[260]. 
2 CONT d)         LOUIS de Bourbon ([1387]-Paris, Hôtel de Bourbon 12 Sep 1404, bur Paris, église des Jacobins).  The chapter of Notre-Dame de Moulins agreed 22 Jun 1409 to celebrate "un obit pour le repos de l’âme de Louis fils du duc d
2 CONC e Bourbon, décédé le 12 septembre"[261]. 
2 CONT Louis had [three] illegitimate children by unknown mistresses: 
2 CONT e)         HECTOR bâtard de Bourbon ([1390?]-Soissons 11 May 1414).  According to Père Anselme, Hector was born “d’une fille de qualité”[262].  Fieyre suggests his birth “v. 1390?” (no source cited)[263].  "Jean duc de Bourbonnais
2 CONC  comte de Clermont" granted a pension to “Hector bâtard de Bourbon”, in exchange for “des terres de Chaveroche en Bourbonnais et de la Hérelle en Beauvoisis” granted to him by “le feu duc leur père commun”, by charter dated [befor
2 CONC e 21] Aug 1413[264].  Seigneur de Rochefort et de Dampierre-en-Champagne.  He died from wounds received at the siege of Soissons[265]. 
2 CONT f)           PERCEVAL bâtard de Bourbon (-after 6 Sep 1415).   Père Anselme says that “Perceval de Bourbon qualifié chevalier le 6 septembre 1415 pouvoit être bâtard du duc Louis II”[266], implying uncertainty about his parentage.
2 CONC   Fieyre indicates his “illégiitimité avérée ; filiation déduite…Par les armoiries et l’emblématique du sceau”[267].  The Chronique de Jean le Févre Seigneur de Saint-Remy records, in 1414, that “l’un des bastart de Bourbon, après
2 CONC  la mort de son frère messire Hector” was called to the siege of Arras, a later passage recording that “le bastard de Bourbon, joane enfant” was appointed by “le duc de Bourbon…chief des quatre Franchois” and recounting his milita
2 CONC rry exploits[268].  Fieyre suggests, in relation to these passages, that “Il est possible que la chronique de Jean Le Fèvre par[le] de lui dès 1414”[269]. 
2 CONT g)         [PIERRE bâtard de Bourbon .  Van Kerrebrouck records his parentage[270].  He cites no source, but presumably his report is based on a comment by Dussieux that “Le P. Labbé cite trois autres bâtards de Louis II, savoir :
2 CONC  Jacques de Bourbon, seigneur de Thury en 1419; Pierre de Bourbon, chevalier; Frère Jacques de Bourbon, de l’ordre des Célestins, en 1422”[271].  It seems likely that, in the case of “Jacques de Bourbon, seigneur de Thury en 1419…
2 CONC [et] Frère Jacques de Bourbon, de l’ordre des Célestins, en 1422””, they refer to the same person whom Labbé confused with Jacques de Bourbon, Seigneur d’Argies et de Préaux, Baron de Thury (son of Jacques de Clermont Comte de la 
2 CONC Marche et de Ponthieu, see above), who, according to Père Anselme, after his wife’s death “prit l’habit religieux au monastere des Celestins d’Ambert dans la forêt d'Orléans”[272].  Presumably some confusion is also possible in th
2 CONC e case of Pierre.  Père Anselme does not name Pierre[273].  It is suggested that his existence be treated with caution.] 
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BOURBON.htm#PierreIDucdied1356B
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BOURBON.htm#LouisIIDucdied1410
