1 NOTE Following the battle near Bretigny in April, the English took four hostages, which included Enguerrand Lord de Coucy, two if King Jean's sons, Louis and Jean, the King's brother, duc d'Orleans, and the Charles the Dauphin's brothe
2 CONC r in law, Louis II duc d.Bourbon, as well as The Count d'Artois, Count d.Eu, Count de OLongueville, Count d'Alencon, Count de Blois, Count de St. Pol, Count d Harcourt, Count de Graandpre, Count de Braisne, and other grands seigne
2 CONC urs include Matthieu de Roye, de Coucy's former guardian.  April and May 1360. They were to be held ransom and only released upon payment of the ransom to King Edward III.
