1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John VI of Harcourt
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT John VI of Harcourt or John of Vaudémont (1 December 1342 - 28 February 1389) was a count of Harcourt. He was son of John V of Harcourt and Blanche of Aumale.
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to his father's counties of Aumale and Harcourt and barony of Elbeuf on his execution in 1356
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1359 John married Catharina (1342-1427), daughter of Peter I, Duke of Bourbon. They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles (1366-1384)
2 CONT
2 CONT John VII (1370-1452)
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis (1382-1422), viscount of Châtellerault and lord of Aarschot in Mézières, archbishop of Rouen
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche (-1431), abbess of Fontevraut
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella (1371-1443), in 1383 married Humbert VI of Thoire en Villars
2 CONT
2 CONT Johanna (1372-1456), wife of Montaigle, in 1393 married William II of Namur
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria,in 1405 married Renaud IV of Gueldre (-1423) and in 1416 married Robert (-1431), son of Adolf of Gulik-Berg
2 CONT
2 CONT Catharina, non
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaretha (1378-), wife of Longueville and of Plaines, married John II lord of Estouteville,
2 CONT
2 CONT Johanna, non.
