2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda of Brabant
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT MahautBrabant.jpg
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda of Brabant (1224 – September 29, 1288) was the eldest daughter of Henry II, Duke of Brabant and his first wife Marie of Hohenstaufen.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Marriages and children
2 CONT
2 CONT On 14 June 1237, Matilda married her first husband Robert I of Artois. The bride was about thirteen years old and the groom twenty-one. Robert was the fifth son of Louis VIII of France and Blanche of Castile. They had two children
2 CONC :
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Blanche of Artois (1248 – 2 May 1302). Married first Henry I of Navarre and secondly Edmund Crouchback, 1st Earl of Lancaster.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Robert II of Artois (1250 – 11 July 1302).
2 CONT
2 CONT On 8 February 1250, Robert I was killed while participating in the Seventh Crusade. Sometime between 1250 and 1254, Matilda married her second husband Guy III, Count of Saint-Pol. He was a younger son of consorts and co-rulers Hug
2 CONC h I, Count of Blois and Mary, Countess of Blois. They had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Hugh II of Châtillon (died 1307), Count of Saint Pol and later Count of Blois
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Guy III of Châtillon (died 1317), Count of Saint Pol
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Jacques I of Leuze-Châtillon (died 1302, Battle of the Golden Spurs), first of the lords of Leuze, married Catherine de Condé and had issue; his descendants brought Condé, Carency, etc. into the House of Bourbon.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Beatrix (died 1304), married John I of Brienne, Count of Eu
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Jeanne, married Guillaume III de Chauvigny, Lord of Châteauroux
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Gertrude, married Florent, Lord of Mechelen (French: Malines).
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] External links
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Her profile, along with her father, in "Medieval Lands" by Charles Cawley
2 CONT
2 CONT This page was last modified on 18 July 2010 at 01:34.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda was 13 when she married Robert (who was 21). She became a widow in 1250, when Robert was killed on a crusade in Egypt. Sometime between 1250 and 1254, Matilda married her second husband Guy III, Count of Saint-Pol. 
2 CONT
2 CONT See http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matilda_of_Brabant for more information.
2 CONT
