1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Isabella van Venne (also known as Ermengarde van Vilvoorde) was the 2nd of 5 known mistresses of JEAN III “le Triomphant” Duke of Brabant, and Limburg.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT BRABANT & LOUVAIN  v5.0 Updated 22 January 2025
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRABANT,%20LOUVAIN.htm#_Toc62125578
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean III had four illegitimate children by Mistress (2):  
2 CONT
2 CONT 9.          JOANNA (-after 1351).  "Ioannes…Lotharingiæ, Brabantiæ et Limburgi dux" granted "villam de Houthain quondam Gosuini de Houtheyn" to "Ioannæ filiæ nostræ…naturali ex Isabella de Vene dicta Ermengarde de Volvorden procre
2 CONC ata", referring to rights for life of “domini Ioannis de Cosselaer militis nostri fratris naturalis nec non dominæ Katharinæ ipsius domini Iohannis uxoris”, by charter dated 8 Apr 1345[457].  Dame de Houtain.  Knetsch records her 
2 CONC marriage and says that she “lebt noch 1351” (no sources cited)[458].  m COSTIJN van Raenst Heer van Eegem, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 10.       JAN van Veen (-after 1 Sep 1354, bur Villers).  His father granted him revenue “assignés sur le chasteau de Rode”, confirmed by Emperor Karl IV by charter dated 1 Sep 1354[459].  An epitaph at Villers records the burial 
2 CONC of “de Vena Ioannes de Brabantia Bastardus is Ducis unus”[460].  Butkens says that “il est toutefois certain qu’il laissa quelque postérité laquelle est estaincte quant à la ligne masculine environ l’an 1460”, commenting that he k
2 CONC new no details[461]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 11.       JEANNETTE .  Butkens records her parentage and marriage, noting that her father granted revenue to her by charter dated 5 Apr 1353, confirmed by Emperor Karl IV by charter dated 1 Sep 1354, and noting the couple’s six ch
2 CONC ildren and descendants[462].  m GODFRIED Heer van der Dilft, Borchvliet en Hoogerheide, son of ---.
2 CONT
2 CONT 12.       MARIE van Veen (-1394).  Butkens records her parentage and date of death, suggesting that she was the beneficary of a grant from her father which was confirmed in the 1 Sep 1354 charter of Emperor Karl IV[463].  Nun at B
2 CONC russels.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT JEAN de Brabant, son of JEAN II "der Friedfertige" Duke of Brabant & his wife Margaret of England (1300-Brussels 5 Dec 1355, bur Villers-la-Ville, Brabant).  The Genealogia Ducum Brabantiæ Ampliata names "Iohannem ducem…tercium" a
2 CONC s the son of "Iohannes…dux" and his wife Margaret[424].  He succeeded his father in 1312 as JEAN III “le Triomphant” Duke of Brabant, and Limburg.  Gilles de Roye’s Annales Belgici record the death in 1355 of “Ioannes dux Brabanti
2 CONC æ” and the succession of “filia eius senior Ioanna, qui tunc Wenceslao fratris regis Boemiæ nupta fuit”[425]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([19 Jul] 1311) MARIE d'Evreux, daughter of LOUIS de France Comte d'Evreux [Capet] & his wife Marguerite d'Artois [Capet] (1303-31 Oct 1335, bur Brussels, Franciscan Church).  The Genealogia Ducum Brabantiæ Ampliata names "Maria
2 CONC m filiam domini Ludovici fratris Regis Francie" as the wife of "Iohannem ducem…tercium"[426].  The Oude Kronik van Brabant records that "Johannes tertius" married "Mariam filiam Ludowici comitis Eboracensis"[427]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mistress (1): [--- Brant, daughter of ---.  Butkens records “Jean Bastard de Brabant surnommé Brant (pour estre né d’une fille de cette maison)” (no source cited)[428].  The accuracy of the information concerning Jean Brant’s moth
2 CONC er is unknown.]  . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mistress (2): ISABELLA van Vene [Ermengarde van Vilvoorde], daughter of ---.  "Ioannes…Lotharingiæ, Brabantiæ et Limburgi dux" granted "villam de Houthain quondam Gosuini de Houtheyn" to "Ioannæ filiæ nostræ…naturali ex Isabella d
2 CONC e Vene dicta Ermengarde de Vilvorden procreata", referring to rights for life of “domini Ioannis de Cosselaer militis nostri fratris naturalis nec non dominæ Katharinæ ipsius domini Iohannis uxoris”, by charter dated 8 Apr 1345[42
2 CONC 9]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mistress (3): [--- van Erpe, wife of --- [Hacke?], daughter of ---.  Butkens records “Willaume Bastard de Brabant surnommé d’Erpe (apparamment pour estre né d’une fille de cette maison)”[430].  The accuracy of the information conc
2 CONC erning Willem van Erpe’s mother is unknown.  Her marriage is indicated by the 1368 document cited below under her son.]  . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mistress (4): [---.  Butkens records “Arnou Bastard de Brabant dict van der Hulpen (né d’une fille de ce surnom)” (no source cited)[431].  The accuracy of the information concerning the mother of the children shown below is unknow
2 CONC n.]  . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mistress (5): [--- van Ophem, daughter of ---.  Butkens records the parentage of “Barbara bastarde de Brabant dicte van Ophem (procréé d’une fille de cette maison)”[432].  The accuracy of the information concerning Barbe’s mother 
2 CONC is unknown.]  .  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_III,_Duke_of_Brabant
2 CONT
2 CONT John III (Dutch: Jan; 1300 – 5 December 1355) was Duke of Brabant, Lothier (1312–1355) and Limburg (1312–1347 then 1349–1355), the last Brabant male to rule them.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT John was the son of John II, Duke of Brabant, and Margaret of England.[1] In 1312, he succeeded his father as the duke of Brabant, in no small part due to his father's Charter of Kortenberg.[2] In an attempt to improve relations w
2 CONC ith France, John married Marie of Evreux.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1311, as his father's gesture of rapprochement with France, John married Marie of Évreux (1303–1335),[3] the daughter of Prince Louis, Count of Évreux and Margaret of Artois. They had: 
2 CONT
2 CONT #     Joanna, Duchess of Brabant (24 June 1322 – 1406), married first to William IV, Count of Holland and second to Wenceslaus I, Duke of Luxembourg.[8]
2 CONT #     Margaret of Brabant (9 February 1323 – 1368), married at Saint-Quentin on 6 June 1347 Louis II, Count of Flanders,[9] she is the ancestor of later dukes
2 CONT #     Marie of Brabant (1325 – 1 March 1399), Lady of Turnhout, married at Tervuren on 1 July 1347 to Reginald III of Guelders[10]
2 CONT #     John of Brabant (1327–1335/36), married Marie of France (1326–1333), daughter of King Philip VI of France,[a] but died soon after with no issue, buried in Tervueren.
2 CONT #     Henri of Brabant (d. 29 October 1349), Duke of Limburg and Lord of Mechelen in 1347. Died young and buried in Tervuren in 1349.
2 CONT #     Godfrey of Brabant (d. aft. 3 February 1352), Lord of Aarschot in 1346. Also died young and buried in Tervuren.
2 CONT
2 CONT John also had a son born from Elisabeth Maria of Huldenberg (d. 1365), who founded the House of Brant: John I Brant, 1st Lord of Ayseau.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1355, after all of his three legitimate sons had died, John was forced to declare his eldest daughter Joanna his heiress,[8] which provoked a succession crisis after his death. John III was buried in the Cistercian Abbey of Vil
2 CONC lers, Belgium. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He also left many illegitimate children, including Jean Brant of Brabant and Jean van Veen. 
2 CONT See [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat%C3%A9gorie:Enfant_naturel_du_duc_de_Brabant category: Natural children of the Duke of Brabant]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Hendrik ll van Berthout van Ranst was the son of Costin van Ranst and Johanna van Daer Achter. The latter was a natural daughter of Duke John III of Brabant and Ermengarde van den Veene. Van Daer Achter was a fief at Vilvoorde. Co
2 CONC stin was Lord of Mortsel and Edegem.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Hendrik-II-van-Berthout-van-Ranst/6000000019996372291 Hij was de zoon]  van Costin van Ranst en [https://www.geni.com/people/Joanna-van-daer-Achter-Bastaerde-van-Brabant/6000000000032976586 Johanna van
2 CONC  Daer Achter]. De laatste was een natuurlijke dochter van Hertog Jan III van Brabant en '''Ermengarde van den Veene'''. Van Daer Achter was een leengoed bij Vilvoorde. Costin was Heer van Mortsel en Edegem.
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hendrik_van_Ranst_%281400-%29
2 CONT
