2 CONT >2. [https://www.geni.com/people/Louis/6000000205440539873 LOUIS "le Haeze"] (-killed in battle Nicopolis 28 Sep 1396). Espinoy records his parentage, noting that his father granted him “tous les biens de Messire Geeraert de Moor 
2 CONC chevalier”, from whom they had been confiscated for murdering “Messire Jean Tant chevalier”, by charter dated 1 Apr 1370 (no source citations)[820]. m --- de Landas, daughter of ---. The primary source which confirms her marriage 
2 CONC has not been identified. Louis [& his wife] had two children:
2 CONT >3. [https://www.geni.com/people/LOUIS/6000000205440789821 LOUIS "Friese"] (-killed in battle Nicopolis 28 Sep 1396). His mother is referred to in the following source: Vredius quotes a manuscript which records “messire Loys de Fr
2 CONC ise fils bastard de...Loys de Male conte de Flandre, lequel il eut d’une fille de Monsieur de Borre”[822].
2 CONT >4. [https://www.geni.com/people/Jean/6000000205440702826 JEAN "Sans Terre"] (-killed in battle Nicopolis 28 Sep 1396). Espinoy names “Jean de Flandres...le cinquiesme fils bastard du... [Comte Louys dit de Maele]...surnommé sans 
2 CONC terre”, to whom his father granted “le chastel et maison de Drincam”, which has been confiscated from “Jean de Scheuruelde...proche heritier de Jacques de Drincham dernier possesseur”, confirmed by charter dated 21 Nov 1383 (no so
2 CONC urce citation)[823].
2 CONT >5. [https://www.geni.com/people/Pierre/6000000205440587914 PIERRE] (-[3 Mar 1376]). A list of knights in Flanders dated [1384-86] names “mer Pieter de Bastaerd”[824]. Buylaert records that an epitaph at Gent Dominican church reco
2 CONC rds the burial of “Pieter van Vlaanderen bastaard van Lodewijk van Male” who died 3 Mar 1376 (O.S.?)[825]. It is unclear whether these two entries relate to the same person, but if so the epitaph must be misdated.
