1 NOTE {geni:about_me}      Otton Herzog von Österreich was born in 1301.1 He was the son of Albrecht I von Habsburg, Holy Roman Emperor and Elisabeth von Kärnten.1 He married, firstly, Elisabeth von Wittelsbach, daughter of Stefan I Her
2 CONC zog von Niederbayern, in 1325.1 He married, secondly, Anna de Luxembourg, daughter of Jean de Luxembourg, King of Bohemia, in 1335. He died in 1339.1
2 CONT      He was a member of the House of Habsburg.2 He succeeded to the title of Herzog von Österreich in 1330.2 Children of Otton Herzog von Österreich and Elisabeth von Wittelsbach
2 CONT
2 CONT Friedrich II von Habsburg1 b. 1327, d. 1344 Leopold II von Habsburg1 b. 1328, d. 1344 Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT  Louda and Michael MacLagan, Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe, 2nd edition (London, U.K.: Little, Brown and Company, 1999), table 78. Hereinafter cited as Lines of Succession.
2 CONT
2 CONT  John Morby, Dynasties of the World: a chronological and genealogical handbook (Oxford, Oxfordshire, U.K.: Oxford University Press, 1989), page 130. Hereinafter cited as Dynasties of the World. Anna de Luxembourg
2 CONT
2 CONT , b. 1323, d. 1338
2 CONT
2 CONT      Anna de Luxembourg was born in 1323.1 She was the daughter of Jean de Luxembourg, King of Bohemia.1 She married Otton Herzog von Österreich, son of Albrecht I von Habsburg, Holy Roman Emperor and Elisabeth von Kärnten, in 133
2 CONC 5. She died in 1338.1
2 CONT      She was also known as Anne of Bohemia.1 Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT Jirí Louda and Michael MacLagan, Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe, 2nd edition (London, U.K.: Little, Brown and Company, 1999), table 78. Hereinafter cited as Lines of Succession.
