2 CONT Conrad IV Hohenstaufen, King of Sicily ▼1
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #114033, b. 1228, d. 1254
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=6 Mar 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT Consanguinity Index=0.0%
2 CONT
2 CONT      Conrad IV Hohenstaufen, King of Sicily was born in 1228.1 He was the son of Friedrich II Hohenstaufen, Holy Roman Emperor and Isabel de Brienne, Queen of Jerusalem. ▼1 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elisabeth von Wittelsbach, daughter of Otto II Herzog von Bayern and Agnes von Braunschweig, in 1246. ▼1 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1254. ▼1
2 CONT
2 CONT      Conrad IV Hohenstaufen, King of Sicily succeeded to the title of King Conrad II of Jerusalem in 1228. ▼2 He succeeded to the title of King Conrad of Sicily in 1250. ▼1 He succeeded to the title of King Conrad IV of the Romans
2 CONC  in 1250. ▼1
2 CONT
