1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT '''Matilda I''', Countess of Nevers or Mathilde de Courtenay, or Mahaut de Courtenay, (1188–1257), was a ruling countess of Nevers, Auxerre and Tonnerre. She was the only daughter of Peter II of Courtenay and of Agnes of Nevers, b
2 CONC orn from the Capetian House of Courtenay, she was married to Hervé IV of Donzy and then to Guigues IV of Forez.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on July 29, 1257[6] at the castle of Coulanges-sur-Yonne, and was buried in the abbey Notre-Dame of the Reconfort of Saizy. Her great-granddaughter Matilda II succeeded her as Countess of Nevers, Auxerre and Tonnerre.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matilda_I_of_Nevers
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From her first marriage with Hervé of Donzy:
2 CONT
2 CONT # William, died between 1207 and 1214, engaged to Beatrice of Viennois
2 CONT # Agnes of Donzy (1205–1225), married in 1217 Philip, eldest son of the future King Louis VIII of France.[7] Philip died the following year. Agnes then married in 1221 Guy of Châtillon (died 1226),[8] and had the daughter Yolande 
2 CONC of Châtillon,[5] who married Archambaud IX of Bourbon.[9]
2 CONT
2 CONT From her second marriage with Guigues IV of Forez:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Artaude, married to Artaud IV of Roussillon, widower of Marie of Geneva, lord of Roussillon and other places.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LATIN%20EMPERORS.htm#PierreIEmpdied1219B Medlands] > CONSTANTINOPLE, LATIN EMPIRE  v5.0 Updated 02 February 2025 >  Chapter 2.    LATIN EMPERORS of CONSTANTINOPLE 1216-1261 (SEIGNEURS de COURTENAY
2 CONC ) MATHILDE de Courtenay ([1188]-29 Jul 1257, bur Abbaye de Réconfort, near Monceaux-le-Comte).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Mathildem" as only daughter of "comitis Petris" & his first wife, specifying that s
2 CONC he married firstly "Herveio Gaufridi filio de Giam et de Dunzeio" and secondly "comiti Gugoni Forensi"[45].  She succeeded her mother in 1193 as Ctss de Nevers, Ctss d'Auxerre, Ctss de Tonnerre, under the guardianship of her fathe
2 CONC r.  …
