1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guigues_III_de_Forez
2 CONT
2 CONT Foreig Guigues III Earl of Forez 1199 - 1204 Predecessor	Foreig Guigues II Successor	Foreig Guigues IV Personal information Birth	approx. 1160 Death	November 28 , 1204 Family Dynasty	Albon Father	Foreig Guigues II Mother	Beaujeu E
2 CONC rmengarda Spouse	Ascura Alix de Sully
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://translate.google.com/translate?hl=en&sl=fr&u=https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guigues_III_de_Forez&prev=search
2 CONT
2 CONT Guigues III (1160 - † November 28, 1204 ) says Branda or Overseas is Earl of Forez from 1198 to 1203 . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Summary  Biography  He succeeds his father Guigues II who abdicates in his favor. During his reign he regularly fights the house of Beaujeu who has many inclinations on the Forez [ 1 ] . He died in the Holy Land during a battle in
2 CONC  Saint-Jean d'Acre [ 2 ] . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and genealogy  Married to Alix / Adela of Sully , the daughter of Gilon III (rather qu'Archambaud IV Sully lord ) and Luce de Charenton (unlike Jean-Marie de La Mure [3] , the site Medlands [4] does not necessarily connecte
2 CONC d Alix / Alasia / Adèle / Sully Adelasia); they had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Guigues IV , who succeeded him.  Marquise de Forez , † about 1237/1239, married to Guy VII, viscount of Thiers , son of Guy VI of Thiers and Clémence de Courtenay [ 5 ] , [ a ] .  Guigonne de Forez, Countess of Vienna by her secon
2 CONC d marriage, married or betrothed to Archambaud VIII of Bourbon around 1205/1206; repudiated she remarries around 1211 with Géraud II de Mâcon , count of Mâcon and Vienne  she gave up her rights on Forez in 1230 to her nephew Guigu
2 CONC es .  Eleanor of Forez, born around 1190 (for the site MedLands , she is not the daughter of Alix / Adelasia, but of a 1st woman of Guigues III, Ascuraa), married to William III or II the Old of Baffie hence: William III or IV of 
2 CONC Baffie; Eleanor of Baffie (x c. 1245 Robert V Count of Auvergne ); Beatrix (x Agnon VI of Auvergne de Meymont d'Oliergues , Philippie / Philippa (x 1 ° Guillaume VIII-II Dauphin as his 3rd wife, then 2 ° in 1241 Robert II, lord of
2 CONC  Courcelles du Breuil ).  another Eleonore, according to the website MedLands , who was betrothed around 1210 to William X Count of Auvergne .  possibly another girl, according to the site MedLands , who would have been the 1st wi
2 CONC fe of William II Count of Geneva , from where a girl who would be the wife of Artaud IV of Roussillon .  Renaud de Forez, canon of the Lyon church.  Notes and references  Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT The different sources [Which?] Give for different people different numbering. The sources of the nineteenth century , here with the case of Jean de La Mure, indeed give Guy sixth name. But recent research shifts the numbering one 
2 CONC step further. Currently, the designated Guy VI of historiography becomes Guy VII while Guy V is an old denomination to designate Guy VI of Thiers .  References 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierre-Yves Laffont The armorial William Revel: castles, towns and villages of the drill in the fifteenth century, vol. 35, Lyon , Liaison Association for Heritage and Archeology in Rhône-Alpes and Auvergne, coll. "Archeology docu
2 CONC ments in Rhône-Alpes and Auvergne", 2011 , 502 p. ( ISBN 9782916125053 , read online ) , "Néronde: the city and chatiau of Neronde (Clément Mottin and Pierre-Yves Laffont)", p. 154-163 
2 CONT
2 CONT Édouard Perroy , " The castles of Roannais from the eleventh to the thirteenth century ", Cahiers of medieval civilization , No. 33, 1966 , p. 13-27 ( ISSN 0007-9731 , read online ) 
2 CONT
2 CONT " Guy III de Forez, p. 182-203 " , on History of the Dukes of Bourbon and the Counts of Forez, by Jean-Marie de La Mure, book I, chap. X to XIV, 1675 and 1809 
2 CONT
2 CONT " Counts of Lyon and Forez " , on MedLands  Jean-Luc Fray, " Auvergne, Velay and Kingdom of Arles: elements for a revision of the relational geography Auvergne in the Middle Ages ", Centuries, review of the Center of History Space
2 CONC s and Cultures , Clermont-Ferrand, House of Sciences of Man, Blaise-Pascal University , vol. 15 2002 ( read online )  Bibliography  Document utilisé pour la rédaction de l’article
2 CONT
2 CONT Memoirs to serve the history of Dombes, Volume I. on Google Books , page 446.  Jean Marie de la Mure, History of the Dukes of Bourbon and the Counts of Forez, Volume I on Google Books , 1809 , pages 156-174; 188; 199-203. 
