1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gebeurtenisse:
2 CONT
2 CONT a.	Jacques de Montmorency was knighted by Charles VI, after the ceremonies of his coronation in 1380. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b.	He participated with the King at the Battle of Rosbecque .
2 CONT c.	 In 1391, it is held for its own account, in the right to take on passing tide in Saint-Brice fish that was to his liking, yet paying according to its value.
2 CONT
2 CONT d.	 In 1392, he erected in the castle of Hunting park, a hotel for his mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT e.	In 1399, King Charles VI named the Chamberlain and the Duke of Burgundy, Philip the Bold does the same.
2 CONT
2 CONT f.	 Around 1400, he was confirmed in his first title of Baron of France, having proved that he is the oldest Baron of the royal domain, the Ile-de-France.-Ds. MG Müller
2 CONT
2 CONT g.	 In 1411, he built the walls around the city of Mourning. h.	Philipotte of Melun, Lady Croisilles and Courrières, descendant of Louis VII France, ca 1355-1421)
2 CONT
