1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Theobald I of Bar From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Jean (Thibaut) Theobald I of Bar (c.1158 - 13 February 1214) was count of Bar from 1190 until his death, and a count of Luxemburg from 1197 until his death. H
2 CONC e was the son of Reginald II of Bar and his wife Agnès de Champagne. He accompanied his elder brother Henry I on the Third Crusade, and succeed as count when Henry was killed in the Siege of Acre. [edit]Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald I was married three times; to Ermesinde (Isabella) of Bar-sur-Seine, Adelheid von Loos (Looz) & Ermesinde (Ermesinda) de Namur and was succeeded as count by his eldest son Henry II, by his first marriage. His eldest daugh
2 CONC ter Agnes, by his second marriage, married Frederick II, Duke of Lorraine. His lands in Luxembourg reverted to Waleran IV of Limburg, who married Theobald's widow Ermesinde I of Luxemburg. [edit]External Link/Source
2 CONT
2 CONT Foundation for Medieval Genealogy on Jean (Thibaut/Theobald I), Comte de Bar http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~jamesdow/s060/f012348.htm
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Jean (Thibaut) Theobald I of Bar (c.1158 - 13 February 1214) was count of Bar from 1290 until his death, and a count of Luxemburg from 1197 until his death. He was the son of Reginald II of Bar and his wife Agnès de Champagne. He 
2 CONC accompanied his elder brother Henry I on the Third Crusade, and succeed as count when Henry was killed in the Siege of Acre.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family Theobald I married three times and was succeeded as count by his eldest son Henry II. His eldest daughter Agnes married Frederick II, Duke of Lorraine. His lands in Luxembourg reverted to Waleran IV of Limburg, who m
2 CONC arried Theobald's widow Ermesinde I of Luxemburg.
