1 OCCU Conde de Luxemburgo e Namur, Comte, de Namur, de Luxembourg, Count of Luxembourg, Count of Namur, 
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''HENRI de Namur (1111-14 Aug 1196, bur Abbaye de Floreffe). HENRI Comte de Luxembourg Henri I "l'Aveugle" [The Blind] Comte de Namur.''' 
2 CONT s/o Comte Godefroi ERMESINDE de Luxembourg
2 CONT x ([1152/59], divorced 1163)  LAURETTA de Flandre  ([1120]-Abbaye de Voorst, near Brussels 1170)
2 CONT xx (1168) AGNES van Gelre (-24 Jan -, bur Echternach).Comte Henri & his second wife had one child:
2 CONT *ERMESINDE de Namur (Jul 1186-12 Feb 1247, bur Clairefontaine, near Arlon). 
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NAMUR.htm#Godefroidied1139
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Comte Godefroi & his second wife ERMESINDE de Luxembourg, had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT >4.HENRI de Namur (1111-14 Aug 1196, bur Abbaye de Floreffe).  The Chronicon Hanoniense names "Henricum…et Albertum qui iuvenis decessit" as the two sons of "Godefridus comes Namurcensi" & his second wife[119].  "Godefridus comes 
2 CONC Namurcensis et Ermensendis comitissa" founded the abbey of Floreffe, with the consent of "Adelberto, Henrico, Clementia, Beatrice, Adelaide", by charter dated 27 Nov 1121[120].  "Godefridus comes Namucensis et Ermensindis comitiss
2 CONC a" donated property to the abbey of Floreffe with the consent of "filiis suis Alberto et Heinrico…" by charter dated 7 Jan 1125[121].  "Ducem Godefridum seniorem eiusque filium…Godefridum iuniorem" donated property "in parochia Br
2 CONC aniensi…Dudinsart" to Gembloux by charter dated 1131, witnessed by "Godefridus comes Namucensis eiusque filius Henricus, Henricus minor filius ipsius ducis, Wilhelmus advocatus de Namuco eiusque frater Anselmus…"[122].  He succeed
2 CONC ed his first cousin (on his mother's side) in 1136 as HENRI Comte de Luxembourg.  He succeeded his father in 1139 as HENRI I "l'Aveugle" Comte de Namur.  He marched against Adalberon Archbishop of Trier in 1141, was excommunicated
2 CONC  and lost Luxembourg territory when the archbishop counter-attacked, although peace was finally signed in Speyer in 1146[123].  He also challenged the authority of the Bishop of Liège, attacking the château de Bouillon which the b
2 CONC ishop claimed from the counts of Bar, but was defeated in 1151 at Andenne by the forces of Bishop Henri de Leyon[124].  He named his brother-in-law Baudouin IV Comte de Hainaut as his heir in Namur and Luxembourg, the latter's son
2 CONC  Baudouin V assuming the position of designated successor after his father's death[125].  Comte Henri lost his sight in 1182[126].  After the unexpected birth of his daughter in 1186, Comte Henri revoked his assurance to Baudouin 
2 CONC V Comte de Hainaut concerning the succession and betrothed the infant to Henri II Comte de Champagne.  In 1188, Comte Henri was obliged to reinstate Baudouin as his heir after a verdict in the latter's favour from Heinrich VI King
2 CONC  of Germany.  Comte Baudouin attacked Namur, captured Comte Henri and obtained a confirmation of his position from Emperor Friedrich I who also secretly created him Marquis de Namur.  Under a compromise reached in 1190, Baudouin r
2 CONC eceived Namur immediately, with the expectation of La Roche and Durbuy after the death of Henri who received the revenues of these two counties for life; the fate of Luxembourg was not mentioned.  The creation of the Marquisate of
2 CONC  Namur was announced at Worms in 1190, at which time Comte Henri retired to Luxembourg where he continued to rule as count[127].  He made a last attempt to recover Namur in 1194 but was defeated at Noville-sur-Mehaigne[128].  The 
2 CONC necrology of Floreffe records the death "III Non Feb" of "Henrici comitis fundator ecclesie Sennensis"[129].  m firstly ([1152/59], divorced 1163) as her fourth husband, LAURETTA de Flandre, widow firstly of IWAN Graaf van Aalst, 
2 CONC secondly of HENDRIK II Duke of Limburg, and thirdly of RAOUL I "le Vaillant" Comte de Vermandois, daughter of THIERRY Count of Flanders & his first wife Swanhilde --- ([1120]-Abbaye de Voorst, near Brussels 1170).  The Cartulaire 
2 CONC de Saint-Bertin records that Count Thierry "ex priori uxore unicam tantum filiam habuit quam Ivanus de Alosto postea sortitus est in conjugium" but does not give her name[130].  The Flandria Generosa names "Laurentiam" as the only
2 CONC  daughter of "comitissa etiam Suanildis", specifying that her marriage with "dux de Lemburg" was terminated on grounds of consanguinity, that she subsequently married "Iwanus de Alst", and after the latter's death "Rodulfo comiti 
2 CONC Peronensi" and "comiti de Namur", although this switches her first and second husbands[131].  She left her fourth husband before [1163] and refused to return to him despite being excommunicated by the bishop of Cambrai.  She becam
2 CONC e a nun at Voorst.  m secondly (1168) AGNES van Gelre, daughter of HENDRIK Graaf van Gelre & his wife Agnes von Arnstein (-24 Jan -, bur Echternach).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines in 1193 records the marriage of "He
2 CONC nrici comitis ceci" and "Agnate sorore comitis de Gelre"[132].  In a later passage, the same source names "Agneta…comitissa de Luscelenborch" as sister of "soror comitis de Gelderland", who was the mother of "domnus Engelbertus fi
2 CONC lius comitis Engelberti de Monte Veteri frater comitis Adolfi", specifying that she was mother of "Ermensindis relicta comitis Barri uxor Waleranni"[133].  The Chronicon Hanoniense names "Agnetam filiam Henrici…comitis de Ghelre" 
2 CONC as wife of "Henricus comes Namurci et Luscelenborch"[134].  She left her husband, entered a convent and refused to return to him despite his appeal to Pope Alexander III[135].  A reconciliation was negotiated in 1185 by the Archbi
2 CONC shop of Köln, Philippe Count of Flanders and Godefroi Duke of Brabant, anxious to ensure that Namur and Luxembourg was not inherited by Baudouin V Comte de Hainaut (the nominated successor of Comte Henri)[136].  The necrology of F
2 CONC loreffe records the death "IX Kal Feb" of "Agnetis comitisse de Gelra"[137].  Comte Henri & his second wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT >>a)         ERMESINDE de Namur (Jul 1186-12 Feb 1247, bur Clairefontaine, near Arlon[138]).  The Chronicon Hanoniense records the birth in Jul 1186 of "Ermensendem" daughter of "comes Namurcensis Henricus" and his wife Agnes[139]
2 CONC .  The Chronicon Hanoniense records the betrothal in 1187 of "Ermensendis" and "comiti Campanensi Henrico"[140].  Her first betrothal was arranged by Comte Henri in order to guarantee a suitably strong protector for his daughter i
2 CONC n light of his dispute with Baudouin V Comte de Hainaut regarding the eventual succession to his counties but the arrangement was discontinued after the 1190 imperial decision in favour of Comte Baudouin[141].  The Chronicle of Al
2 CONC beric de Trois-Fontaines in 1193 records the marriage of "Theobaldus comes Barrensis" and "filiam Henrici comitis ceci…Ermensendem"[142].  She succeeded her father in 1196 as ERMESINDE Ctss de Luxembourg.  Her first husband bought
2 CONC  the counties of Luxembourg, Durbuy and La Roche, with the approval of Philipp King of Germany, and besieged Philippe Marquis de Namur in his castle at Namur, which forced the negotiation of the 1199 treaty of Dinant[143].  Under 
2 CONC the treaty, signed 26 Jul 1199, Baudouin IX Count of Flanders and Hainaut inherited Namur, while Ermesinde retained Luxembourg, Durbuy, La Roche and that part of Namur which lay on the right bank of the river Meuse[144].  The Chro
2 CONC nicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "seniori Walerano filio Henrici" as second husband of "Ermensende filia Henrici ceci comitis Namucensis"[145].  She received Arlon as her jointure on her second marriage[146].  Betrothed (
2 CONC 1187) to HENRI II Comte de Champagne, son of HENRI I "le Libéral" Comte de Champagne & his wife Marie de France (29 Jul 1166-Acre 10 Sep 1197).  m firstly (1197) as his third wife, THIBAUT I Comte de Bar, son of RENAUD II Comte de
2 CONC  Bar & his wife Agnes de Blois ([1160]-12/13 Feb 1214, bur Saint-Mihiel).  m secondly ([Feb/May] 1214) as his second wife, WALERAN de Limbourg Seigneur de Montjoie, son of HENDRIK III Duke of Limburg & his wife Sophie von Saarbrüc
2 CONC ken (-Cremona 2 Jul 1226, bur Rode Abbey).  He succeeded in 1221 as WALERAN IV Duke of Limburg. https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NAMUR.htm#Godefroidied1139
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hendrik_I_van_Namen
2 CONT
2 CONT Ermesinda would have been 50 years old when he was born. She was detached as his mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry IV (c.1112 – 14 August 1196), called the Blind (l'Aveugle or der Blinde), was count of Luxembourg from 1136 and count of Namur from 1139 until his abdication in 1189. He was the son of Godfrey I of Namur and Ermesinda, daugh
2 CONC ter of Conrad I of Luxembourg.
2 CONT
2 CONT He inherited the counties of La Roche and Durbuy from cousins Henry II of Durbuy and Henry of Laroche. When his cousin Conrad II of Luxembourg died, he was granted that county by the Emperor Lothair II, who thus prevented its pass
2 CONC ing to the French count of Grandpré. Three years later, he inherited Namur from his father. He inherited the advocacy of the abbeys of Saint-Maximin at Trier and Saint-Willibrod at Echternach. This was the cause of many conflicts 
2 CONC with the archbishop of Trier.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1141, he helped Alberon II, Bishop of Liège take Bouillon with Renaut I of Bar. In 1147, he gave up Saint-Maximin, but he regained it on the death of the Archbishop Albero de Montreuil in 1152. The new archbishop, Hillin von Fa
2 CONC llemanien, exchanged the rights over the abbeys with the town of Grevenmacher in 1155. In 1157, he married Laurette (d.1175), daughter of Thierry of Alsace, Count of Flanders, and Margaret of Clermont. They separated in 1163. Left
2 CONC  without child, he designated his brother-in-law Baldwin IV of Hainault, husband of his sister Alice of Namur, as his heir. When Baldwin died in 1171, he designated Baldwin V. Baldwin V and Henry carried out two wars, in 1170 and 
2 CONC 1172, with Henry III of Limburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1171, Henry married a second time, this time to Agnes, daughter of Henry of Guelders and Agnes of Arnstein. Heirless still, he repudiated her in 1184, but fell seriously ill and rejoined her. In September 1186, a girl, Ermesind
2 CONC e, was born to them. This birth called into question the plan of succession, as Henry considered his promise to Baldwin null. Henry, then 76 years old, pledged his daughter in marriage to Henry II of Champagne. Baldwin still claim
2 CONC ed his inheritance. It was then decided that Baldwin would inherit Namur, Ermesinde Durbuy and La Roche, and Luxembourg (fief masculin) would revert to the Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT The fiefs were dispensed in 1189 and after the planned marriage between Ermesinde and the count of Champagne was cancelled Henry bethrothed her instead to Theobald I of Bar. He entered into a war with Henry of Limburg and was defe
2 CONC ated on 1 August 1194 at Neuville on Mehaigne. He died two years later in Echternach.
2 CONT
2 CONT source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_IV_of_Luxembourg
2 CONT
