1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marguerite de Bar le Duc
2 CONT
2 CONT  d. 23 November 1275
2 CONT
2 CONT      Marguerite de Bar le Duc was the daughter of Henri II de Bar le Duc, Comte de Bar le Duc and Philippe de Dreux. She married Henri V, Comte de Luxembourg, son of Walram III, Duc de Limbourg and Ermisende II, Comtesse de Luxemb
2 CONC ourg, circa 1240. She died on 23 November 1275.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Marguerite de Bar le Duc and Henri V, Comte de Luxembourg:
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippa de Luxembourg+ d. 6 Apr 1311
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel de Luxembourg+ d. c 1330
2 CONT
2 CONT Henri VI, Comte de Luxembourg+ b. c 1240, d. 5 Jun 1288
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p365.htm#i3650
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of Bar (1220-1275)[1] was a daughter of Henry II of Bar and his wife Philippa of Dreux. She was Countess of Luxembourg by her marriage to Henry V of Luxembourg. She is also known as Marguerite of Bar.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents [hide]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Family
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Ancestors
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 References
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret's maternal grandparents were Robert II of Dreux and his second wife Yolanda de Coucy. Her paternal grandparents were Theobald I of Bar and his second wife Ermesinde of Brienne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret was the eldest of seven children born to her parents. Her brother was Theobald II of Bar. Margaret's sister, Jeanne married Frédéric de Blamont. The rest of her siblings died young or unmarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1240, Margaret married Henry V of Luxembourg [2]. Margaret was twenty years old, and Henry was twenty-four.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret brought Henry Ligny-en-Barrois as her dowry, however, by a clause in the marriage contract, it remained under the feudal suzerainty of the county of Bar. In contempt of this, Henry paid homage in 1256 to Theobald II of Na
2 CONC varre, in his capacity as Count of Champagne. Margaret's brother, Theobald II of Bar, took advantage of the conflict then raging between Frederick III of Lorraine (their cousin) and the bishops of Metz. Henry V was a partisan of t
2 CONC he duke and so Theobald took the side of the bishop. Henry was captured in battle at Prény on 14 September 1266. On 8 September 1268, King Louis IX arbitrated between the two counts and Henry was freed and repossessed of Ligny, bu
2 CONC t under the suzerainty of the Barrois.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret and Henry had seven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry VI, (d. 1288) Count of Luxembourg
2 CONT
2 CONT Waleran I (d. 1288), Count of Ligny & Roussy
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabelle (1247-1298), married Guy of Dampierre
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippa (1252-1311), married John II, Count of Holland
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret
2 CONT
2 CONT Felicitas
2 CONT
2 CONT Joanna (d. 1310), Abbess of Clairefontaine
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret and Henry made peace with Guy of Dampierre by marrying him to their daughter, Isabelle. Their other daughter, Philippa married John II, Count of Holland and became grandparents to Philippa, Queen of England and Margaret I
2 CONC I, Countess of Hainault.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret died in 1275, six years before her husband's death.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Ancestors
2 CONT
2 CONT   Reginald II, Count of Bar 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Theobald I of Bar   
2 CONT
2 CONT   Agnes of Champagne 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Henry II of Bar   
2 CONT
2 CONT   Guy of Brienne 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Ermesinde of Brienne   
2 CONT
2 CONT   Pétronille Elisabeth de Chacenay 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Margaret of Bar   
2 CONT
2 CONT   Robert I of Dreux 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Robert II of Dreux   
2 CONT
2 CONT   Agnes de Baudemont 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Philippa of Dreux   
2 CONT
2 CONT   Raoul de Coucy 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Yolanda of Coucy   
2 CONT
2 CONT   Agnes of Hainaut 
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] References
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.^ Marguerite de Bar
2 CONT
