1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - https://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hendrik_VI_van_Luxemburg
2 CONT - https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enrico_VI_di_Lussemburgo
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry VI (ca. 1240 – 5 June 1288) was count of Luxembourg and Arlon from the death of his father, Henry V the Blond in 1281 until his own death, seven years later, when he was succeeded by his son, Henry VII.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry was the son of Henry V the Blond and Marguerite of Bar. His father took part in Saint Louis's crusade against Tunis and he continued this war, being killed alongside three of his brothers at the Battle of Worringen by a knig
2 CONC ht of John I, Duke of Brabant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry married Beatrice d'Avesnes (d. 1 March 1321, daughter of Baldwin and granddaughter of Bouchard IV of Avesnes) around 1260–1 and they had three sons, two of whom attained the highest honours and excellence:
2 CONT
2 CONT Baldwin, afterwards Archbishop-Elector of Trier, and
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry, who would become King of the Romans in 1308 and Holy Roman Emperor (as Henry VII) in 1309, being crowned as such by Pope Clement V in 1312.
2 CONT
2 CONT Walram, died at the siege of Brescia in 1311
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]References
2 CONT
2 CONT This article incorporates text from the public-domain Catholic Encyclopedia of 1913.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henri VI, Comte de Luxembourg, thePeerage.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrix d'Avesnes, thePeerage.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Baudoin d'Avesnes, thePeerage.com
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Henry VI (ca. 1240 – 5 June 1288) was count of Luxembourg and Arlon from the death of his father, Henry V the Blond in 1281 until his own death, seven years later, when he was succeeded by his son, Henry VII.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry was the son of Henry V the Blond and Margaret of Bar. His father took part in Saint Louis's crusade against Tunis and he continued this war, being killed alongside three of his brothers at the Battle of Worringen by a knight
2 CONC  of John I, Duke of Brabant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry married Beatrice d'Avesnes (d. 1 March 1321, daughter of Baldwin and granddaughter of Bouchard IV of Avesnes) around 1260–1 and they had three sons, two of whom attained the highest honours and excellence:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Baldwin, afterwards Archbishop-Elector of Trier, and
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Henry, who would become King of the Romans in 1308 and Holy Roman Emperor (as Henry VII) in 1309, being crowned as such by Pope Clement V in 1312.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Walram, died at the siege of Brescia in 1311
