1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Ferry I de Lorraine''', né vers 1143 mort 7 avril 1206, fut '''seigneur de Bitche''' de 1176 à 1206 et se proclama '''duc de Lorraine''' de 1205 à 1206. Il était le second fils du duc Mathieu Ier et de Judith de
2 CONC  Hohenstaufen (1123-1195), aussi appelée Berthe. Il fut aussi le premier prince de la maison de Lorraine à porter l'écu aux alérions. http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferry_Ier_de_Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick I, Duke of Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick I (French: Ferry or Ferri) (ca. 1143 – 7 April 1206) was the duke of Lorraine from 1205 to his death. He was the second son of Matthias I and Judith, daughter of Frederick II, Duke of Swabia. He succeeded his brother, Si
2 CONC mon II, who had already given him the county of Bitche in 1176 and had recognised him over the northern, germanophone half of Lorraine by the Treaty of Ribemont of 1179. Judith had wanted him to succeed to all their father's inher
2 CONC itance, but a three-year civil war only secured him Bitche and a half-portion.
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon abdicated to a monastery in 1205, recognising Frederick's son Frederick as heir. Frederick inherited it all nevertheless, but died a year later and it went to his son by Ludmilla (1150-1223), daughter of Mieszko III the Old,
2 CONC  duke of Greater Poland and high duke of all Poland, and Elisabeth, daughter of Prince Álmos. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick, his successor in Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT Thierry the Devil (le Diable), lord of Autigny
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry the Lombard, who built the castle of Bayon
