1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Theobald I of Bar
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald I was married three times; to Ermesinde (Isabella) of Bar-sur-Seine, Adelheid von Loos (Looz) & Ermesinde (Ermesinda) de Namur and was succeeded as count by his eldest son Henry II, by his first marriage. His eldest daugh
2 CONC ter Agnes, by his second marriage, married Frederick II, Duke of Lorraine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick II, Duke of Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT By his marriage to the daughter of the count of Bar and Laurette de Looz, he had:
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald (d.1220), his successor in Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthias (d.1251), his brother, successor in Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT Reginald (d.1274), count of Blieskastel
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice, countess of Ormes, married firstly Werner (d.1228), count of Kirbourg, and secondly, in 1229, Walter, lord of Vignory
2 CONT
2 CONT Lauretta, married Simon III, Count of Saarbrücken, in 1226
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob (d.1260), bishop of Metz
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald I of Bar
