1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''John II, Marquis of Namur'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John II (1311 – 2 April 1335) was Marquis of Namur from 1330 to 1335.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the eldest son of John I, Marquis of Namur, and Mary of Artois.
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded his father on 26 January 1330. He joined an alliance against John III, Duke of Brabant, but by the intervention of King Philip VI of France, a conflict was averted.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died unmarried, but had an illegitimate son Philip, who was killed in 1380, while defending Dendermonde.
2 CONT He was succeeded by his brother Guy.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_II,_Marquis_of_Namur
