1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guy_II,_Marquis_of_Namur
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy II of Namur, (1312 – March 12, 1336), was Count of Namur from 1335 to 1336.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the second son of John I, Marquis of Namur, and Mary of Artois.
2 CONT
2 CONT He participated in 1332 on the side of the Count of Flandres against the Duke of Brabant, in the war over Mechelen. He succeeded his brother John II as Count of Namur on April 2, 1335. Under influence of his younger brother Robert
2 CONC  of Namur, he recognized King Edward III of England as his Lord, in exchange for a pension.
2 CONT
2 CONT He also participated in the War against Scotland with 300 men, but was surprised by a larger Scottish force under John Randolph, 3rd Earl of Moray in the Battle of Boroughmuir. Guy was taken prisoner, but released for ransom.  htt
2 CONC p://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Boroughmuir
2 CONT
2 CONT After his return to Namur, he participated in a tournament in Flanders, where he was mortally wounded.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his younger brother Philip.
