2 CONT Also called Geoffrey de Geneville, Lord of Trim.2 Lord of Trim at Ireland in 1234.2 Geoffroy de Joinville, seigneur de Vaucouleurs was born circa 1235. He was the son of Simon, sire de Joinville and Blanche (?).1 Arms: Azure three
2 CONC  horse braies fesswise in pale or a chief ermine a lion rampant issuant gules.3 Geoffroy de Joinville, seigneur de Vaucouleurs married Maud de Lacy, daughter of Gilbert de Lacy and Isabel le Bigod.4,2 Geoffroy de Joinville, seigne
2 CONC ur de Vaucouleurs was the successor of James de Aldithley, Justiciar of Ireland; Justiciar of Ireland.5 Geoffroy de Joinville, seigneur de Vaucouleurs was the successor of Maurice fitz Maurice, Lord Justice of Ireland; Justiciar o
2 CONC f Ireland.5 Justiciar of Ireland in 1273.6,5 Annals of Monte Fernando 1273: "Item dominus Galfridus de Genevile venit usque Hiberniam, de terra sancta, parum ante festum beati Francisci, et factus est justiciarius Hibernie, post o
2 CONC ctavas beati Francisci."7 Geoffroy de Joinville, seigneur de Vaucouleurs was the predecessor of Robert de Ufford, Justice of Ireland; Justice of Ireland.8,9 Arms: Azure, three horsebrays or, on a chief ermine a demi-lion rampant g
2 CONC ules.10 Geoffroy de Joinville, seigneur de Vaucouleurs bought the marriage of his daughter from William de Valence, Earl of Pembroke, for £200 in December 1283.6 He died in 1314.10  Family	Maud de Lacy b. before 1230, d. 11 April 
