1 NOTE In the 38th year of the reign of King Henry III, he had livery of the castle of Trim in Ireland. Four years afterwards he received military summons to march against the Welsh. In the 44th year of the reign of Henry III, being one 
2 CONC of the marchers, he was commanded to repair the Castle of Wales and to reside there. He was summoned to Parliament as a baron on 6 Feb 1299 to 3 Nov 1306 as a reward for his services during the wars in Gascony. He died on an exped
2 CONC ition against the Weslsh during the reign of King Edward I.
