2 CONT j)          AGNES (-after 15 May 1326).  Dame d’Aubonne.  The marriage contract between “Guillaume Allemand fils de Guigues seigneur de Valbonnais” and “Agnès de Villard”, the father granting “à son fils la terre de Claix”, is dat
2 CONC ed 6 Mar 1314[512].  Her marriage is confirmed by the charter dated 20 Aug 1370 under which her son’s son-in-law "Rodulphus comes Gruerie" sold the succession in the seigneuries d’Aubonne et de Coppet, inherited from "dne Agnetis 
2 CONC de Villar, quondam dne Albone, et dni Humberti Alamandi, eius filii"[513].  She succeeded her brother Amédée as dame d’Aubonne[514].  “Guillerme Allamandi et Agnès du Villar sa femme” issued a charter dated 7 Aug 1322 relating to 
2 CONC a property transaction[515].  The testament of “Guillaume Allemand chevalier seigneur de Valbonnais”, dated 27 Apr 1332, named “sa [première] femme Agnès de Villars...sa seconde femme Sibylle de la Palud”[516].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (contract 6 Mar 1314) as his first wife, GUILLAUME Alamandi, son of GUIGUES Alamandi Seigneur de Valbonnais & his second wife Eléonore de Roussillon (-[27 Apr 1332/4 Aug 1333]).  
