2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         MARGUERITE de Vergy (-1 Nov 1398, bur Theulay).  “Marguerite de Vergy Dame de Pesmes mere de noble damoisel Jean de Grandson, Jehanne de Vergy Dame d’Authon et Henrie de Vergy Dame de Fontaines [...auctorisée de son sei
2 CONC gneur et mary...Jehan de Vienne Seigneur de Pagny] seurs” shared property of “feu...leur...nepueu Pierre de Bar jadis escuyer trespassé sans hoirs de son corps...en la terre de Pusoye” by charter dated 9 Dec 1386[454].  A parliame
2 CONC ntary registry dated 19 Feb 1389 records a claim by “ducem Barensem marquesiam Pontis” against “Ioannam de Vergeyo dominam d’Authon et Margaretam de Vergeyo dominam de Pesmes et...Ioannem de Vienna dominum de Paigny militem et Hen
2 CONC rietam de Vergeyo eius uxorem”, naming “Henricus, Ioannes, Erardus et Petrus” as sons of Thibaut II Comte de Bar, “Henricum” as the son of Pierre and “Ysabelli de Vergeyo” as his wife, specifying that “Guillelmus de Vergeyo dominu
2 CONC s de Mirabel miles” had “tres filias...Ysabellim, Joannam et Margaretam” by his first marriage[455].  This document indicates that these three daughters of Guillaume de Vergy were born from the same marriage, specified in the docu
2 CONC ment as his first.  The date of death of Jeanne suggests that she must have been born from her father’s second marriage.  If that is correct, Marguerite as youngest of the three was also the daughter of Guillaume’s second wife.  T
2 CONC he document specifies that Guillaume’s daughter Marguerite married “defuncto Iacobo de Grançon domino de Pesmes [miles]”.  The testament of “Margareta de Vergeyo domina de Pesmis”, dated 10 Jun 1396 published mid-Nov 1398, chose b
2 CONC urial “in parrochiali ecclesia de Pesmis” between the bodies of “quondam bone memorie...Jacobi de Grandissono domini de Pesmis...mariti mei et...quondam...Guillelmi filii mei de Grandissono”, bequeathed property to “filie mee Alid
2 CONC i de Grandissono domine de Talemey...filie mee Hugonete de Grandissono domine de Poppeto...”, and appointed “filium meum Johannem de Grandissono” as her heir[456].  An epitaph at Theulay records the burial of “Marguerite de Vergy 
2 CONC Dame de Pesmes qui fut femme de...Iean de Gransson chevalier et seigneur dudit lieu” who died “le jour...de Toussaints” 138--[457].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (Dijon before 1346) JACQUES de Grandson Seigneur de Pesmes, son of OTHON Seigneur de Grandson & his wife Jeanne de Pesmes (-[Jun/19 Dec] 1381, bur Pesmes Saint-Hilaire).  
