2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/GERMANY,%20Kings.htm#ElenaMGuelfoGherardescadied1295
2 CONT
2 CONT    Enzio & his [first/second] wife had [two] children:
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         '''ELENA''' (-[before 16 Mar 1272]).  The testament of “Henricus...rex Sardinie”, dated 16 Mar 1272, appointed “Henrico et Ugolino nepotibus...ex...filia nostra Helena et viro...Guelfo de Donoratico genero nostro natos”
2 CONC  as his heirs, specifically in “regno nostro Sardinie”[731].  The appointment of her sons as heirs to Sardinia suggests that their mother must have been the testator´s daughter by his first marriage.  However, Fara (writing in 157
2 CONC 9) states that Adelasia di Torres died childless and bequeathed Torres to Pope Gregory IX by her testament[732].  <br/>
2 CONT '''m''' GUELFO Gherardesca Conte di Donoratico, son of UGOLINO Conte di Donoratico & his wife --- (-1295). 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Enzio had [one illegitimate child by FRASCA, daughter of ---]:
2 CONT
2 CONT c)          ['''ELENA''' .  The testament of “Henricus...rex Sardinie”, dated 16 Mar 1272, bequeathed property to “Helenam filiam Frescam” and requesting “Henrico et Ugoilino nostris heredibus” to make the payment[733].  The docum
2 CONC ent does not specify that Elena was the testator´s daughter.  Assuming that she was Enzio´s daughter, the testament suggests that she was not the same daughter Elena who was the mother of his heirs Enzio and Ugolino.]   
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
