2 CONT c)         GASPARD Grimaldi (-[29 Oct 1414/8 Jul 1417]).  The testament of “dominus Raynerius de Grimaldis...dominus Mentoni necnon dominus Rochebrune”, dated 8 Jun 1407, bequeathed property to “...eius filium Ambrosinum...Anthoni
2 CONC um eius natum...Gasparum eius natum...Joannem eius natum...”[231].  Louis II d’Anjou King of Sicily confirmed a pension to “Ambrosius, Anthonius, Gaspar et Johannes de Grimaldis fratres, filii quondam...militis Raynerii de Grimald
2 CONC is” by charter dated 29 Oct 1414[232].  He is named as deceased in his mother’s 8 Jul 1417 testament.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' [JANQUINA, daughter of ---.  The testament of “Isabella de Grimaldis quondam felicis memorie...domini Raynerii de Grimaldis relicta”, dated 8 Jul 1417, bequeathed property for masses for “dominabus Luquine et Janquine de G
2 CONC rimaldis nurum suarum”[233].  The order of their names suggests that Janquina was the wife of one of the testator’s younger sons, possibly the widow of Gaspard.  Another possibility is that Janquina was the supposed first wife of 
2 CONC Antoine Grimaldi (see above).] 
2 CONT
