1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://www.euganeinews.it/AlberiGen/CARR.php (1143-1191) 
2 CONT #Speronella di Dalesmano Dalesmanini e di Mabilia
2 CONT # Maria di Albertino da Baone
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Da_Carrara
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT   PLZ source for /!\ (1155-1180) /!\ 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacopino_da_Carrara__(podestà_di_Treviso)
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Marsilius (?-1163) and Galearch[1] and was loyal to the imperial side. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT In about 1163 she had married Speronella Dalesmanni, a noble and rich feudal lord of the bishop of Padua when the imperial vicar of Padua, Count Pagano della Torre fell in love with her and kidnapped her, taking her to the Rocca P
2 CONC endice[1] of Teolo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Speronella's brother, Dalesmanino, swore revenge[1] and organized the siege with the nobles of Padua, which led, on June 23, 1164, to the defeat of the representative of Emperor Frederick Barbarossa, thus declaring the birth of th
2 CONC e free municipality of Padua. From here began the Italian war against the emperors, which ended in 1183 with the Peace of Constance. [1] Count Pagano withdrew from Padua and Jacopino, despite the outrage he received, remained fait
2 CONC hful to the emperor. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1174 he was appointed podestà of Treviso. [1] He died in about 1190. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lineage
2 CONT Jacopino married first Speronella Dalesmanni, from whom he divorced and married second Maria di Albertino da Baone (?-after 1215). [1] He had seven children:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marseille (?-1210)
2 CONT Albertino
2 CONT Anna
2 CONT Jacopino (?-1262 ca.), politician
2 CONT India
2 CONT Uguccione
2 CONT Pierconte, politician.
