1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Eudes II, Duke of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Eudes II of Burgundy (1118 – June 27 or September 27, 1162) was Duke of Burgundy between 1143 and 1162. Eudes was the eldest son of duke Hugh II and Matilda De Turenne. He married Marie de Champagne, daughter of Theobald II, Count
2 CONC  of Champagne and Matilda of Carinthia. They had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Alix (1146 - 1192), married in 1164 to Archambaud VII (d.1169), Lord of Bourbon
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh III (1148 - 1192), his successor in the duchy
2 CONT
2 CONT Mahaut (d.1202), married Robert IV, Count of Auvergne
