1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Eudes II of Burgundy''' (1118 – June 27 or September 27, 1162) was Duke of Burgundy between 1143 and 1162. Eudes was the eldest son of duke Hugh II and Felicia-Matilda of Mayenne, daughter of Gauthier, Count of 
2 CONC Mayenne and Adelina de Presles. He married Marie de Champagne, daughter of Theobald II, Count of Champagne and Matilda of Carinthia. They had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Alix (1146–1192), married in 1164 to Archambaud (died 1169), son of Archambaud VII (died 1171), Lord of Bourbon[1]
2 CONT *Hugh III (1148–1192), his successor in the duchy[1]
2 CONT *Mahaut (died 1202), married Robert IV, Count of Auvergne
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odo_II,_Duke_of_Burgundy
