2 CONT GUILLAUME [VIII] "le Vieux" d'Auvergne, son of GUILLAUME [VI] Comte d'Auvergne & his wife Emma of Sicily (-[1182]).  "Poncius…Cluniacensis ecclesiæ…abbas" recommended "amitam suam domnam Judit Arvernorum comitissam" to donate prop
2 CONC erty to Cluny, noting the later donation by "eidem comitissæ et filio eius domno Willelmo Arvernorum comiti…et filios eius Robertum…et Willelmum et eius filiam Judith", by undated charter[229].  He succeeded as Comte d'Auvergne.  
2 CONC A letter from the canons of Clermont to Louis VII King of France complained of the activities of “Willelmi maioris natu comitis atque filii eius Roberti”, undated[230]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ANNE de Nevers, daughter of GUILLAUME II Comte de Nevers & his wife Adelais ---.  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "comitissa Anna…soror comitis Renaldi Nivernensis" as mother of "Robertus [comes Alvernie]
2 CONC "[231]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Guillaume [VIII] & his wife had four children: 
