2 CONT Wikipedia contributors, 'Henry II of Rodez', Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia, 4 December 2010, 06:27 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Henry_II_of_Rodez&oldid=400446768> [accessed 15 March 2011] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry II of Rodez
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry II (Occitan: Enric II de Rodés) (c. 1236 – 1304), of the House of Millau, was the Count of Rodez and Viscount of Carlat from 1274 until his death. He was the son of Hugh IV of Rodez and Isabeau de Roquefeuil.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry II was a troubadour and patron of troubadours (his Occitan name was Enric II de Rodes). He composed six poems that survive: four tensos and two partimens (alternatively five torneyamens). His short vida records an exchange o
2 CONC f couplets between lo coms de Rodes (the count of Rhodes) and Uc de Saint Circ. The count claims to have got Uc back on his feet through his generous patronage. Among the other troubadours who were supported at Henry's court were 
2 CONC Guiraut Riquier, Folquet de Lunel, Cerverí de Girona, and Bertran Carbonel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages and children Henry II married three times. His first wife, married in 1256, was Marquise, daughter of Barral des Baux. They had one daughter named Isabeau who inherited the viscounty of Carlat and married the troubadour 
2 CONC Geoffrey, lord of Pons. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Though Marquise died in 1276, she was repudiated sometime before that in favour of Mascarosse, daughter of Bernard IV of Comminges. The latter bore Henry four children: Hugh Cecilia (1275–1313), successor, married (1298) Bernard V
2 CONC I of Armagnac Beatrix, lady of Scorailles and Saint-Christophe, married (1295) Bernard III (died 1325), lord of La Tour Valpurge, viscountess of Creyssel and lady of Roquefeuil, married (1298) Gaston d'Armagnac (died 1326), viscou
2 CONC nt of Fézenzaguet
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry was widowered in 1292 and remarried for the last time in 1302 to Anne (died 1351), daughter of Aymar III of Valentinois. The couple had no children and the widowed Anne remarried to John I, Dauphin of Auvergne.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://gw.geneanet.org/chatelaine87?lang=en&pz=clara&nz=adobati&p=henri+ii&n=de+rodez Geneanet Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 29 2024, 9:54:43 UTC''
