1 NOTE {geni:about_me} - https://www.comune.modena.it/salastampa/archivio-comunicati-stampa/2017/5/san-contardo-d2019este-un-videodocumentario-lo-racconta
2 CONT
2 CONT Contardo, figlio di Aldobrandino I d’Este signore di Ferrara, crebbe orfano del padre sotto la protezione dello zio https://www.geni.com/people/Azzo-VII-d-Este-Marquis-of-Ferrara/6000000003827400343 alla corte estense di Ferrara
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT - https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contardo_d%27Este
2 CONT
2 CONT Saint Contardo of Este was the posthumous son of Aldobrandino of Este, marquis of Ferrara. He was born in 1216 in Ferrara.
2 CONT
2 CONT He renounced to his wealth and position of crown prince of Ferrara to become a simple "God's man" and started on a pilgrimage to Santiago de Compostela.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fell ill in Broni (Province of Pavia, Lombardy, Italy) and died there. His body was first buried on the hill where he died. Miracles were reported on his grave : severely sick people were cured.[1][2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT The body was later transferred to the Saint Peter parish church (which later became a Minor basilica) in Broni. Two relics are in "Saint Biagio church (Saint Blaise) in Modena.
2 CONT
2 CONT His cult was approved in 1609 by Pope Paul V (papacy 1605-1621) on the request of Claudio Rangoni (it), bishop of Piacenza (1596-1619[4]), native of Modena,[5] and indulgences were linked to it by Pope Urban VIII (papacy 1623-1644
2 CONC ) [2][6] https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Contardo_of_Este
