2 CONT
2 CONT Ben M. Angel notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT The Italian Wikipedia page on Bonifacio del Vasto lumps all of Bonifacio's children as having Agnes as a mother, and doesn't acknowledge the existence of Alix of Savoy (possibly the author sides with Szabolcs de Vajay on her being
2 CONC  a fabrication, compelling evidence to the contrary notwithstanding). The page also brings up a couple points worth noting:
2 CONT
2 CONT - Bonifacio never went by "del Vasto" as this was a name given to his territory long after his death - apparently during his time it went by Montenotte, and included the high hinterlands of Savonna.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Adelasia del Vasto, wife firstly to Roger I of Sicily and secondly to Baldwin I of Jerusalem, is apparently now thought to have been Bonifacio's daughter, rather than his niece. If Alix of Savoy exists, it is uncertain whether A
2 CONC delasia would have been born by her, or second wife Agnes of Vermandois.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference: http://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonifacio_del_Vasto
2 CONT
