2 CONT * According to the [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MONFERRATO,%20SALUZZO,%20SAVONA.htm#BonifazioSaluzzodied11251135 FMG Medieval Lands database]:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BONIFAZIO''', son of ODDONE Marchese della Liguria Occidentale & his wife Berta di Susa ([1060]-[1127/35]).  "Berta comitissa filia quondam Maginfredi et item Maginfredus et Anselmus, Bonifacius, Oto clericus germani et filii q
2 CONC uondam Toto itemque marchionis, mater et filii" donated property to the monastery of San Silo near Genoa by charter dated 31 Aug 1064[430].  "Berta comitissa et Manfredus, Bonifacius et Anselmus marchioness et Henricus et Oto germ
2 CONC ani, mater et filii" donated property to the church of Santa Maria "de episcopatu Astensi" by charter dated 22 Apr 1065[431].  Marchese del Vasto.  "Bonifacius marchio filius quondam Othonis" donated property to the church of Acqu
2 CONC i by charter dated 22 Jul 1090 "in castro de Ceva"[432].  "Bonifacius marchio filius quondam Teutonis…marchio et Henrico nepos suus" donated property to the canons of the church "in valle Burmia in loco…Ferranica" by charter dated
2 CONC  1097[433].  "Bonifacius marchio filius Teutonis…marchio…cum Alice cometissa filia qd. d. Petri marchio atque Theotone, Petro, Magnifredo, Hugone et Willielmo filiis eorum" donated property to "monasterio sancti Petri…in…villa Sav
2 CONC iliani" by charter dated 21 Dec 1099[434].  "Bonifacius marchio cum filiis suis Manfredo atque Ugone" donated property to "ecclesie S. Donati de Monte" by charter dated 1121[435].  "Bonifacius marchio" appointed "filiis suos Magin
2 CONC fredum et Wilielmum adque Ugonem necnon Anselmum…et Anricum et Bonefacium minorem atque Odonem" as his heirs and provided dowries for "filiabus…Sibilie et Adalaxia et alie filie si ex hac uxore nata fuit", but disinherited "Bonifa
2 CONC cium…incixie nominatum", by charter dated 1125[436].  "Bonifatius marchio…Agnes comitissa uxor ipsius marchionis…filii eius Mainfredus et Ugo" donated "domum sancti Laurentii" to Lérins by charter dated 1127[437]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[m''' firstly ALIX de Savoie, daughter of PIERRE I Comte de Savoie & his wife Agnès de Poitou.  "Bonifacius marchio filius Teutonis…marchio…cum Alice cometissa filia qd. d. Petri marchio atque Theotone, Petro, Magnifredo, Hugon
2 CONC e et Willielmo filiis eorum" donated property to "monasterio sancti Petri…in…villa Saviliani" by charter dated 21 Dec 1099[438].  Szabolcs de Vajay dismisses this individual as an imaginary person designed to explain the claims of
2 CONC  Marchese Bonifazio to Turin, which he in fact inherited through his mother who was the younger sister of Adelaida di Susa, mother of Comte Pierre[439].  It is uncertain whether he was aware of the charter quoted above when he mad
2 CONC e this suggestion.  Even if the charter in question was spurious, it is unclear what purpose would have been served by fabricating the ancestry of Marchese Bonifazio´s wife.  It should be noted that Bonifazio´s [second] wife Agnes
2 CONC  de Vermandois was considerably younger than her husband.  An earlier marriage would therefore be likely.''']'''   
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' [secondly] AGNES de Vermandois, daughter of HUGUES de France Comte de Vermandois et de Valois [Capet] & his wife Adelais Ctss de Vermandois [Carolingian] ([1085]-after 1127).  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis refers 
2 CONC to (but does not name) the first of the daughters of "Hugonem Magnum [et] Adelaide comitissa Veromandensium" as wife of "Bonefacius marchio", parents of "Bonefacium archidiaconum Noviomensem et filios et filias, quarum una nupsit 
2 CONC Guilelmo de Monte-pessulano"[440].  "Bonifatius marchio…Agnes comitissa uxor ipsius marchionis…filii eius Mainfredus et Ugo" donated "domum sancti Laurentii" to Lérins by charter dated 1127[441]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Marchese Bonifazio & his [first] wife had five children: 
