2 CONT 10.    '''  BONIFAZIO "minor" ''' (-[1188/26 May 1190]).  "Bonifacius marchio" appointed "filiis suos Maginfredum et Wilielmum adque Ugonem necnon Anselmum…et Anricum et Bonefacium minorem atque Odonem" as his heirs but disinherit
2 CONC ed "Bonifacium…incixie nominatum" by charter dated 1125[468].  This document shows that Marchese Bonifazio had two sons named Bonifazio.  Archdeacon of Noyon.  The Genealogiæ Scriptoris Fusniacensis refers to (but does not name) t
2 CONC he first of the daughters of "Hugonem Magnum [et] Adelaide comitissa Veromandensium" as wife of "Bonefacius marchio", parents of "Bonefacium archidiaconum Noviomensem et filios et filias, quarum una nupsit Guilelmo de Monte-pessul
2 CONC ano"[469].  A manuscript entitled Genealogia regum Francorum tertiæ stirpis names "Bonefacium archidiaconum Noviomensem" as one of the sons of "Bonefacius Marchio" and his wife "Hugo…frater Philippi Regis Francorum…filias…una"[470
2 CONC ].  Bishop of Alba.  Marchese di Curtemilia.  "Dominus Bonifacius Marchio de Curtemilia" confirmed the donation of "medietas castri, villæ…et comitatus Laureti", made by "Otto Marchio qui fuit frater eius", to the consuls of Asti 
2 CONC by charter dated 1188[471].  "Dominus Guilielmus Marchio de Ceva" donated "hæreditate Domini Bonifacii Marchionis de Curtemilia" to the consuls of Asti by charter dated 26 May 1190[472].  This latter charter shows that Bonifazio d
2 CONC ied without children, his property being inherited by his nephew Guglielmo Marchese di Ceva. 
