2 CONT
2 CONT c)         HENRI de Milly "Bubalus" (-after 16 Jul 1164).  The Lignages d'Outremer name "mesire Phelippe de Naples…Henri le Bufle, et…Gui" as the three sons of "Gui le Franceis" and his wife "Estefenie"[663].  In another passage, 
2 CONC the Lignages d'Outremer record that "Henri le Bufle" was "seignor dou Bouquiau et de tote la terre dou Ssaor"[664].  "Philippus Neapolitanus et Henricus frater eius…" subscribed the charter dated 1155 under which "Melisendis…Ihero
2 CONC solimorum regina" confirmed the donation of "Hugonis de Hibeline…et Balduini fratri sui" to the church of the Holy Sepulchre, Jerusalem[665].  "Philippi…Neapolitani, Guidonis Francigene, Henrici Bubali" are referred to as "avuncul
2 CONC orum" of "Hugo de Hybelino et…fratris sui Balduini…" in a charter dated 14 Jan 1155[666].  “Amalricus...comes Ascalonitanus” confirmed the donation of “casal Zaythar” to the lepers of St Lazarus at Jerusalem made by “Philippus Nea
2 CONC politanus”, with the consent of “Ysabel uxore sua et domina Stephania matre sua, et Rainerio filio suo, Helena etiam et Stephania filiabus suis...et Guidone Francigena et Henrico Bubalo fratribus suis”, by charter dated 3 Jul 1155
2 CONC [667].  A charter dated 1180 records earlier donations by "Guidonem de Miliaco…dominus Philippus Neapolitanus dominusque Guido Francigena et dominus Henricus Bubalus, predicti Guidonis filii" and the present donation by "Reginaldu
2 CONC s quondam princeps Anthiochensis…Montisregalis et Hebron dominus" of property to the abbey of Notre-Dame de Josaphat with the consent of "uxor mea Stephania"[668].  "…Henricus Bubalus…" subscribed the charter dated 16 Jul 1164 und
2 CONC er which "Amalricus…in sancta civitate Ierusalem Latinorum rex quintus" granted privileges to the church of the Holy Sepulchre, Jerusalem[669].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' AGNES Garnier of Sidon, daughter of [EUSTACHE [II] Garnier Lord of Sidon & his wife Papia ---].  The Lignages d'Outremer record that the wife of "Henri le Bufle" was "la suer de Renaut seigneur de Seete"[670], although thi
2 CONC s appears unlikely to be correct assuming the estimated marriage date in [1138] of Renaud's supposed parents.  Another manuscript of the Lignages names "Girart et Gautier, et Agnes qui espousa Henri le Bufle" as the three children
2 CONC  of "Huistace Garnier…sire de Cesaire" and his wife "Heimeline, la niesse dou patriarche Ernoul de Jerusalem"[671], referring from the context to Eustache [I].  However, this is clearly improbable from a chronological point of vie
2 CONC w.  The most probable solution is that Agnes was the daughter of Eustache [II], the Lignages confusing the father with the son.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Henri & his wife had four children:  
