2 CONC married "''Heinricus purcravius Ratisponensis''"[183]. The'' Notæ Genealogicæ Bavaricæ'' record the marriage of "''purcravius''" and "''sororem ducis Heinrici'' [''de Austria'']"[184]. "''Ratisbonensis Comes Heinricus et uxor eius
2 CONC  Pertha''" donated property to St Nikolas by charter dated to [1145][185]. The necrology of Kloster Neuburg records the death "''V Id Apr''" of "''Berhta filia Liupoldi marchionis Austrie''"[186]. The necrology of the Obermünster,
2 CONC  Regensburg records the death "''V Id Apr''" of "Berhta com"[187]. The necrology of Admunt records the death "''V Id Apr''" of "Berhta com"[188].  
