2 CONT Manfred II (1140 – 1215) was the second margrave of Saluzzo from his father's death in 1175 to his own. He was the son of Manfred I and Eleanor. He placed the capital of the margravate definitively in Saluzzo.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Azalaïs of Montferrat before 1182, forming an alliance with one of the most powerful dynasties in northern Italy. He had at least five children with her:
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes, married Comita III of Torres
2 CONT
2 CONT Boniface (the heir, who predeceased his father), married Maria, daughter of aforementioned Comita
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret, married Geoffrey de Salvaing
2 CONT
2 CONT (unnamed daughter), married Marquis William II of Ceva
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas
2 CONT
2 CONT He also fathered an illegitimate son, Bastardino.
2 CONT
2 CONT He expanded the march and fought against the expansionism of the neighbouring counts of Savoy. After several minor skirmishes, the two principalities came to terms in 1213 and peace was established for the final two years of his l
2 CONC ife. Since his eldest son Boniface had predeceased him in 1212, he was succeeded by his grandson, Manfred III, under the regency of Azalaïs. She had to pay tribute on behalf of young Manfred, and for the next century, Saluzzo was 
2 CONC a vassal of Savoy.
2 CONT --------------------
