1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Tower of Raimondello Orsini in Taranto, c. 1880.Roberto (1295–1345), Gentile II's elder son, married to Sibilla del Balzo, daughter of the Great Senechal of the Kingdom of Naples. Among his sons, Giacomo (died 
2 CONC 1379) was created cardinal by Gregory XI in 1371, while Nicola (August 27, 1331 – February 14, 1399) obtained the counties of Ariano and Celano. The latter was also Senator of Rome and enlarged the family territories in Lazio and 
2 CONC Tuscany. His second son, Raimondello Orsini del Balzo, supported Charles III' coup d'état in Naples against Queen Joan II. Under king Ladislas he was among the few Neapolitan feudataries who were able to maintain their territorial
2 CONC  power afther the royal war against them. However, at his death in 1406 the southern Orsini fiefs were confiscated. Relationships with the royal family remained cold under Joan II; however, when Raimondello's son Giannantonio (138
2 CONC 6–1453) sent his troops to help her against the usurpation attempt of James of Bourbon, he received in exchange the Principality of Taranto.
2 CONT * see: Wikipedia, '''marriage & issue '''[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anastasia_de_Montfort,_Countess_of_Nola '''Anastasia de Montfort, Countess of Nola''']
2 CONT
2 CONT On 8 June 1293[1] Anastasia '''married''' Roman senator, '''Romano Orsini''' (1268–1327), the son of Gentile II Orsini, Senator of Rome, and Claricia de Ruffo. The marriage had been arranged by Cardinal Napoleon Orsini, who was he
2 CONC r mother's guardian. Anastasia, being Margherita's eldest daughter and heiress, eventually brought the rich Aldobrandeschi and Sovana inheritances into the Orsini family.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Together '''Romano''' and '''Anastasia''' had at least three children:
2 CONT # '''Roberto Orsini, Count of Nola (1295 - 15 January 1345)''', married '''Sueva del Balzo''', the daughter of Hugues del Balzo, Count of Soleto and Seneschal of Naples, and Jacopa della Marra, by whom he had issue. Elizabeth Wood
2 CONC ville, Queen consort of Edward IV of England was a descendant of Roberto and Sueva.[1]
2 CONT # Guido Orsini, Count of Pitigliano (died after 1348), married Agostina della Gherardesca, by whom he had issue.
2 CONT # Giovanna Orsini, married in 1334 Nicolo Caetani by whom she had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anastasia died on an unknown date, which occurred sometime before her eldest son, Romano's death on 15 January 1345 as he had succeeded her as Count of Nola. Her husband Romano died in 1327.
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CENTRAL%20ITALY.htm#RobertoOrsinidied1345B
