1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====FMG: France [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/CAPET.htm#MarieValoisdied1331 Capetian Kings]
2 CONT
2 CONT * 11. MARIE de Valois (-28 Oct 1331, bur Naples, Santa Chiara). The Annales Ludovici di Raimo record the death "in San Nicola di Bari" in 1331 of "la duchessa di Calabria suore del Re di Francia" and her burial 21 Aug in "Santa Ch
2 CONC iara di Napoli"[909]. '''m''' (Paris 4 Oct 1323, in person May 1324) as his second wife, '''CHARLES of Sicily''', son of ROBERT King of Sicily and Jerusalem [Anjou-Capet] & his first Infanta doña Violanta de Aragón ([28 May] 1298-
2 CONC Naples 10 Nov 1328, bur Naples, Santa Chiara). He was installed as Duca di Calabria in 1325, Viceroy of Sicily.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====FMG: [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SICILY.htm#Charlesdied1328 Sicily]
2 CONT * 1. CHARLES of Sicily ([28 May] 1298-Naples 9 Nov 1328, bur Naples Santa Chiara)....'''m''' firstly (23 Jun 1316/end 1316)''' KATHARINA von Habsburg''', daughter of ALBRECHT I King of Germany, Duke of Austria & his wife Elisabeth
2 CONC  von Görz-Tirol (Oct 1295-Naples 18 Jan 1323, bur Naples San Lorenzo Maggiore)....'''m''' secondly (contract Paris 4 Oct 1323, by proxy Paris 11 Jan 1323/4 in person May 1324) '''MARIE de Valois''', daughter of CHARLES de France C
2 CONC omte de Valois & his third wife Mahaut de Châtillon (-Bari 28 Oct 1331, bur Naples Santa Chiara). '''Charles of Sicily & his second wife had five children:'''
2 CONT ** a) ELOISA di Calabria ([Jan/Feb] 1325-27 Dec 1325). [No citation]
2 CONT ** b) MARIA di Calabria ([Apr] 1326-1328, bur Naples Santa Chiara). [No citation]
2 CONT ** c) CHARLES MARTEL di Calabria (Florence 13 Apr 1327-Florence 21 Apr 1327, bur Florence Santa Croce). [No citation]
2 CONT ** d) JEANNE di Calabria (Naples [1328]-strangled Castello San Fele/Muro, Basilicate 22 May 1382, bur Naples Santa Chiara).
2 CONT ** e) MARIE di Calabria (posthumously Naples [mid-May] 1329-Naples 20 May 1366, bur Naples Santa Chiara)....
2 CONT <nowiki>————————————————————————————————————————————</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles, Duke of Calabria
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1316, he married Catherine of Habsburg (1295–1323), daughter of Albert I of Germany. After her death, he married Marie of Valois (1309–1332), daughter of Charles of Valois. They had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Eloisa (d. December 1325)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie (1326–1328)
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Martel (Florence, April 13, 1327 – April 21, 1327, Florence)
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan I of Naples (1328–1382)
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria of Calabria (1329–1366), Countess of Alba. Married Charles, Duke of Durazzo.
