1 NOTE Charles, Duke of Durazzo born 1345, great-grandson of Charles II King of Naples.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles, Duke of Durazzo, was adopted by Queen Joanna I of Naples, but was abandoned in favor of Louis I Duke of Anjou.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles, Duke of Durazzo, having helped depose Joanna of Naples, and then having her murdered, took over her throne as King of Naples in 1382.
2 CONT
2 CONT As heir to the throne of Hungary through his mother, Marie of Hungary, Charles of Durazzo, came to rule Hungary  in 1385.  He ruled to 1386 when there was a revolt and uprising and he was poisoned.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Charles was crowned King of Hungary in 1385, he was captured and imprisoned as a result of a revolt, and poisoned.
