0 @N6000000002187747971@ NOTE Beatrice of Savoy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Beatrice of Savoy (1198 – 1266), was the daughter of Thomas I of Savoy and Marguerite of Geneva. Beatrice married on (5 June 1219) Ramon Berenguer IV, Count of Provence. She was a shrewd and politically astute woman, whose beauty 
1 CONC was likened to that of a second Niobe by Matthew Paris. After two stillborn sons, Ramon and Beatrice of Savoy had four daughters, who all married kings.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marguerite of Provence (1221-1295), wife of Louis IX of France 
1 CONT Eleanor of Provence (1223-1291), wife of Henry III of England 
1 CONT Sanchia of Provence (1228-1261), wife of Richard, Earl of Cornwall 
1 CONT Beatrice of Provence (1231-1267), wife of Charles I of Sicily 
