1 CONT even had he not been the sovereign of the land of song, his own verses would
1 CONT have entitled him to a distinguised rank among the Troubadour poets.
1 CONT He was relatively impoverished count who could provide little dowry for his
1 CONT daughters.
0 @N6000000003051138490@ NOTE Berenger was the last and most illustrious of the Royal Provenal Counts; and, even had he not been the sovereign of the land of song, his own verses would have entitled him to a distinguised rank among the Troubadour poets. He was
