0 @N6000000002188017642@ NOTE Manfred III of Saluzzo
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Manfred III (d.1244) was the third margrave of Saluzzo from 1215 to his death. He was the son and heir of Manfred II and Alaisia of Montferrat, who was his regent during his minority until 1218. During that period, his mother paid
1 CONC  tribute to Count Thomas I of Savoy.
1 CONT
1 CONT Manfred fought the expansionistic policies of Thomas, as had his father, and he defended the borders of his march with care. He died in 1244 and was succeeded by his son Thomas.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Manfred II Margrave of Saluzzo
1 CONT 1215 – 1244 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Thomas I 
