0 @N6000000002240774863@ NOTE Louis, an outstanding monarch of medevial times, was canonized in 1297 as
1 CONT Saint Louis, with his feast day August 25th. Saintly, but he had his faults.
1 CONT Quick-tempered and sometimes violent, he had to struggle with his gluttony.
1 CONT High-spirited, he made his decisions alone, but knew how to choose wise
1 CONT counsellors. His sincere piety did not prevent him from curbing the abuses of
1 CONT the clergy, at times brutally. The saintly Louis enjoyed immense prestigue
1 CONT throughout western Christendom as the most popular of the Capetian monarchs.
