1 CONT
1 CONT      Henry III (1207-1272) was the eldest son of King John, and a grandson of Henry II.  He came to the throne in 1216 when he was only 9 years old, but did not rule until he came of age in 1227.
1 CONT Henry was a fickle tyrant who surrounded himself with favorites from other countries.  The English nobles revolted against his rule and the foreign influences in his court.  They forced Henry to grant the Provisions of Oxford, whi
1 CONC ch transferred governing powers to a committee of barons.  Later, Henry broke the agreement and raised an army.  But he was defeated and captured at the battle of Lewes in 1264.
1 CONT      Simon de Montfort, leader of the reform party, then governed England until he was killed at the batttle of Evesham in 1265 by Henry's son, Edward.  Edward ruled the country during the rest of Henry's lifetime.
