0 @N6000000001956369765@ NOTE
1 CONT Edmund 'Crouchback' Plantagenet, Earl of Leicester was born on 16 January 1245 in London, England.2 He was the son of Henry III, King of England and Eleanor of Provence. He married, firstly, Aveline de Forz, Countess of Holderness
1 CONC , daughter of William de Forz, Count of Aumale and Isabel de Reviers, on 8 April 1269 in Westminster Abbey, Westminster, London, England.2 He married Blanche d'Artois, daughter of Robert I de France, Comte d'Artois and Matilde de 
1 CONC Brabant, before 3 February 1276 in Paris, France.2 He died on 5 June 1296 at age 51 in Bayonne, Bearn, France.2 He was buried on 15 July 1296 in Westminster Abbey, Westminster, London.1 
1 CONT Edmund 'Crouchback' Plantagenet, Earl of Leicester gained the title of King Edmund of Sicily on 7 January 1254.2 He abdicated as King of Sicily in 1263.2 He gained the title of Earl of Leicester on 26 October 1265.2 He gained the 
1 CONC title of 1st Earl of Lancaster on 30 June 1267.2 Through his marriage, Edmund 'Crouchback' Plantagenet, Earl of Leicester was styled as Comte de Brie in 1276. Through his marriage, Edmund 'Crouchback' Plantagenet, Earl of Leiceste
1 CONC r was styled as Comte de Champagne in 1276.2
