0 @N6000000005076803119@ NOTE Earl of Leicester
1 CONT
1 CONT from thePeerage.com:
1 CONT
1 CONT Edmund 'Crouchback' Plantagenet, Earl of Leicester was born on 16 January 1245 at London, England.2 He was the son of Henry III, King of England and Eleanor of Provence. He married, firstly, Aveline de Forz, Countess of Holderness
1 CONC , daughter of William de Forz, Count of Aumale and Isabel de Reviers, on 8 April 1269 at Westminster Abbey, Westminster, London, England.2 He married, secondly, Blanche d'Artois, daughter of Robert I de France, Comte d'Artois and 
1 CONC Matilde de Brabant, before 3 February 1276 at Paris, France.2 He died on 5 June 1296 at age 51 at Bayonne, Bearn, France.2 He was buried on 15 July 1296 at Westminster Abbey, Westminster, London, England.1
1 CONT      Edmund 'Crouchback' Plantagenet, Earl of Leicester gained the title of King Edmund of Sicily on 7 January 1254.2 He abdicated as King of Sicily in 1263.2 He gained the title of Earl of Leicester on 26 October 1265.2 He gained
1 CONC  the title of 1st Earl of Lancaster on 30 June 1267.2 As a result of his marriage, Edmund 'Crouchback' Plantagenet, Earl of Leicester was styled as Comte de Brie in 1276. As a result of his marriage, Edmund 'Crouchback' Plantagene
1 CONC t, Earl of Leicester was styled as Comte de Champagne in 1276.2
1 CONT Children of Edmund 'Crouchback' Plantagenet, Earl of Leicester and Blanche d'Artois
1 CONT Thomas Plantagenet, 2nd Earl of Lancaster b. bt 1277 - 1280, d. 22 Mar 1322
1 CONT Henry Plantagenet, 3rd Earl of Lancaster+ b. c 1281, d. 22 Sep 1345
1 CONT John of Beaufort, Lord of Beaufort b. b May 1286, d. c 13271
1 CONT Mary Plantagenet b. b 12961
