0 @N6000000004303404286@ NOTE FROM CURT HOFEMAN:
1 CONT
1 CONT Luisa (Aluigia) del Vasto de Ceva 
1 CONT
1 CONT Note: SGM names her Ceva while Ancestral Roots names her Cave. (There are towns known by both names in Italy). I will go with SGM. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Aluigia del Vasto of Ceva [Ref: Richard Borthwick, 26 Jan 1999] 
1 CONT ********** 
1 CONT It would appear that even though Weis for 28:31 cited CP I:241-242 as a source of his data, he apparently transposed the toponym CEVA in CP to CAVE in AR7 & his editors missed it. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Name: Luisa, daughter of Giorgio, Marquis of Ceva [Ref: CP I:240] 
1 CONT Name: Luigia de CEVA [Ref: Turton p97 citing: Guichenon, S., _Hist. de Savoie_, 1660] 
1 CONT Name: Luisa di Ceva [Ref: Moriarty Plantagenet] 
1 CONT Name: Louisa di Giorgia, Marquess of Ceva [Ref: Ronny Bodine 18 Feb 1997 citing: volume 11 of Pompeo Litta's Famiglie celebri italiani (Milan: Paolo Emilio Giusti, 1819-1871), 1st series] 
1 CONT
1 CONT Note that in 3 of his msgs to SGM, Richard Borthwick cited the same source, 
1 CONT *Genealogie medioevali di Sardegna* eds. L L Brook, F C Casula, M M Costa, A M Oliva, R Pavoni & M Tangheroni (Publicazione della Deputazione di Storia Patria per la Sardegna, 1983), pp 109 (tav. XVIII), 131 (tav.XXIX) 
1 CONT
1 CONT but gave 3 versions of the same name: 
1 CONT
1 CONT Aluigia di Ceva [Ref: Richard Borthwick 10 Dec 1998] 
1 CONT Aluigia del VASTO (dau of Giorgio I del VASTO, M of Ceva) [Ref: Richard Borthwick 26 Jan 1999] 
1 CONT Aluiga di Ceva [Ref: Richard Borthwick 12 Aug 1999] 
1 CONT
1 CONT I am a bit curious at the use of "del Vasto" for numerous generations of this line. AFAIK, it means "the Fat" or "the Huge". In a time period where there were no surnames, why would an epithet for one person, be also used for his 
1 CONC descendants for a number of generations? Richard Borthwick is deservedly well known for his scholarship in genealogy & I know very little about Italian genealogy & naming patterns so it is likely that I'm misunderstanding this.
0 @N6000000000337389323@ NOTE Weis, p. 30
1 CONT
1 CONT Source #2:  Douglas Richardson, "Plantagenet Ancestry:  A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families" (Baltimore, Maryland:  Genealogical Publishing Company, Inc., 2004), p. 315
