0 @N6000000003051292588@ NOTE [Wikipedia, "Joan of Valois (1294-1352)", retrieved 23 Dec 07]
1 CONT Jeanne of Valois (c. 1294 Longpont, Aisne, France - 7 March 1342, Fontenelle, Yonne, France) was the daughter of Prince Charles of Valois and Marguerite of Anjou and Maine (1274?1299) and the sister of king Philip VI of France.
1 CONT
1 CONT Her paternal grandparents were Philip III of France and Isabella of Aragon. Her maternal grandparents were Charles II of Naples and Maria Arpad of Hungary.
1 CONT
1 CONT Jeanne married William III, Count of Holland and Hainaut in 1305 and had the following children:
1 CONT - William IV of Hainaut (1307-1345)
1 CONT - John (died 1316)
1 CONT - Margaret II, Countess of Hainaut (1311-1356), married Louis IV Wittelsbach, Holy Roman Emperor
1 CONT - Philippa of Hainault (1311-1369), married king Edward III of England
1 CONT - Agnes (died 1327)
1 CONT - Joanna of Hainaut (1315-1374), married William V, Duke of Jülich
1 CONT - Isabelle of Hainaut (1323-1361), married Robert of Namur
1 CONT - Louis (1325-1328)
