1 CONT John and William de Braose were close friends but eventually broke apa rt, and in 1207, John led troops into the Welsh Marches so as to siez e the properties of William such as castle Bramber as well as other Ma rche castles belon
1 CONC ging to William.  William waited for the King at Her eford and begged for terms.  William agreed to the Kings terms that in cluded payment for the royal lands in Leinster as well as the castles of Radnor, Hoy and Brecon.  In Augus
1 CONC t of 1207, John issued letters of patent giving Liverpool the status of a free borough and invited his s ubjects to settle there with guaranteed trading rights in hope of fost ering development of a harbor along the Mersey river. 
