1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Children of Queen Eleanor and King Edward I
1 CONT
1 CONT The Northampton CrossDaughter, stillborn in May 1255 in Bordeaux, Franc
1 CONT Katherine, living June 17, 1264, died September 5, 1264 and buried at Westminster Abbey. 
1 CONT Joan, born January 1265, buried at Westminster Abbey before September 7, 1265. 
1 CONT John, born July 13, 1266, died August 3, 1271 at Wallingford, in the custody of his granduncle, Richard, Earl of Cornwall. Buried at Westminster Abbey. 
1 CONT Henry, born before May 6, 1268, died October 16, 1274. 
1 CONT Eleanor, born ca. 18 June 1269 and died 29 August 1298. She was long betrothed to Alfonso III of Aragon, who died in 1291 before the marriage could take place, and in 1293 she married Count Henry III of Bar. 
1 CONT Daughter, born after May 1271 in Palestine and died before September 1272. 
1 CONT Joan of Acre. born at Acre 1272 and died April 7, 1307. She married (1) Gilbert de Clare, 7th Earl of Hertford, (2) Ralph Morthermer, 1st Baron Monthermer. 
1 CONT Alphonso, Earl of Chester, born 24 November 1273, died 19 August 1284, buried in Westminster Abbey. 
1 CONT Margaret, born March 15, 1275 and died after 1333. She married John II of Brabant. 
1 CONT Berengaria, born 1 May 1276 and died before June 27, 1278, buried in Westminster Abbey. 
1 CONT Daughter, died shortly after birth, January 1278. 
1 CONT Mary, born 11 March 1279 and died 29 May 1332, a nun in Amesbury, Wiltshire (England). 
1 CONT A son, born in 1280 or 1281, who died very shortly after birth. 
1 CONT Elizabeth of Rhuddlan, born August 1281 at Rhuddlan, died 5 May 1316. She married (1) John I, Count of Holland, (2) Humphrey de Bohun, 4th Earl of Hereford & 3rd Earl of Essex. 
1 CONT Edward II of England, also known as Edward of Caernarvon, born 25 April 1284 at Caernarvon, died 21 September 1327. He married Isabella of France. 
1 CONT [edit]
