0 @N6000000005076973058@ NOTE from thePeerage.com:
1 CONT
1 CONT Blanche d'Artois was born between 1245 and 1250.2 She was the daughter of Robert I de France, Comte d'Artois and Matilde de Brabant.2 She married, firstly, Enrique I (III), Rey de Navarre, son of Thibaut I (IV), Rey de Navarre and
1 CONC  Marguerite de Bourbon, in 1269.2 She married, secondly, Edmund 'Crouchback' Plantagenet, Earl of Leicester, son of Henry III, King of England and Eleanor of Provence, before 3 February 1276 at Paris, France.3 She died on 2 May 13
1 CONC 02 at Paris, France.2 She was buried at Minoresses' Convent, Aldgate, London, England.2
1 CONT Children of Blanche d'Artois and Enrique I (III), Rey de Navarre
1 CONT Thibaut de Navarre d. 12732
1 CONT Jeanne I, Reina de Navarre+ b. c 1271, d. 2 Apr 13052
1 CONT Children of Blanche d'Artois and Edmund 'Crouchback' Plantagenet, Earl of Leicester
1 CONT Thomas Plantagenet, 2nd Earl of Lancaster b. bt 1277 - 1280, d. 22 Mar 1322
1 CONT Henry Plantagenet, 3rd Earl of Lancaster+ b. c 1281, d. 22 Sep 1345
1 CONT John of Beaufort, Lord of Beaufort b. b May 1286, d. c 13271
1 CONT Mary Plantagenet b. b 12961
0 @N6000000005598847794@ NOTE At least one souce indicates that Blanche was actually the daughter o f Mechtild of Hainault, daughter of John, 2nd Count of Hainault (?).Th is needs additional investigation.  After her marriage to Edmund, Blan che and Edmund wer
1 CONC e to administer Campagne until Blanches daughter Joa n from her first marriage came of age or married.  On 17 May 1284, Bla nche and Edmund relinquished their guardianship and received 60,000 li vres tournois in compensation.
