0 @N6000000006296743001@ NOTE Blanche of Artois (1248 - 2 May 1302) was the queen regent of Navarre </wiki/Navarre> from 1274 to 1284, and later became Countess of Lancaster </wiki/Earl_of_Lancaster> by marrying into the English royal family. She was the daugh
1 CONC ter of Count Robert I </wiki/Robert_I_of_Artois> of Artois </wiki/Artois> and Matilda of Brabant </wiki/Matilda_of_Brabant>. From 1274 to 1284 she ruled Navarre and the counties of Brie </wiki/Brie>, Champagne </wiki/Champagne_(pr
1 CONC ovince)>, Troyes </wiki/Troyes> et Meaux </wiki/Meaux> for her daughter, Joan I </wiki/Jeanne_of_Navarre> of Navarre (ruled 1274 to 1305).
1 CONT Her paternal grandparents were Louis VIII of France </wiki/Louis_VIII_of_France> and Blanche of Castile </wiki/Blanche_of_Castile>. Her maternal grandparents were Henry II, Duke of Brabant </wiki/Henry_II,_Duke_of_Brabant> and Mar
1 CONC ie of Hohenstaufen </wiki/Marie_of_Hohenstaufen>, daughter of Philip of Swabia </wiki/Philip_of_Swabia>.
1 CONT Blanche married Henry I </wiki/Henry_I_of_Navarre> of Navarre (ruled 1270-1274) who died in 1274. They had two children:
1 CONT Theobald - d. 1270 fell from a battlement at the castle of Estella
1 CONT Joan I of Navarre </wiki/Joan_I_of_Navarre>, who became Queen regnant </wiki/Queen_regnant> of Navarre and Queen consort </wiki/Queen_consort> of France
1 CONT After Henry's death, Blanche married Edmund Crouchback </wiki/Edmund_Crouchback,_1st_Earl_of_Lancaster> (1245-1296), in 1276, an English prince who was a younger son of Henry III </wiki/Henry_III_of_England> and Eleanor of Provenc
1 CONC e </wiki/Eleanor_of_Provence>. Edmund was also a widower, his young wife having died the same year as Blanche's husband.
1 CONT Edmund and Blanche had four children:
1 CONT Thomas Plantagenet, 2nd Earl of Lancaster </wiki/Thomas_Plantagenet,_2nd_Earl_of_Lancaster> (b. 1278)
1 CONT Henry Plantagenet, 3rd Earl of Lancaster </wiki/Henry,_3rd_Earl_of_Lancaster> (b. 1281)
1 CONT John Plantagenet, Lord of Beaufort (c. 1282 - 1327)
1 CONT Mary Plantagenet (c. 1284 - c. 1289)
