0 @N6000000000437167263@ NOTE Name Suffix:<NSFX> Of Gloucester
0 @N6000000003658774316@ NOTE From Magna Carta Ancestry:
1 CONT
1 CONT MARGARET DE CLARE, born in 1250.  She married at Ruislip, Middlesex 6 (or 7) Oct. 1272 EDMUND OF CORNWALL, Knt. (usually styled EDMUND OF ALMAIN), Earl of Cornwall, Baron of Wallingford, Berkshire, Launceston and Trematon, Cornwal
1 CONC l, Bradninch, Devon, and Berkhampstead, Hertfordshire, Joint and Sole Guardian of the Realm, Sheriff of Cornwall and of Rutland, Councillor to the Prince of Wales, born about 1 Jan. 1250.  They had no issue.  They separated about 
1 CONC 14 Feb. 1293/4, she desiring "to live in chastity."  SIR EDMUND OF ALMAIN, Earl of Cornwall, died at Ashridge Abbey, Buckinghamshire on or before 25 Sept. 1300, and was buried at Hailes Abbey, Gloucestershire.  His wife, Margaret,
1 CONC  died in 1312.
