0 @N6000000002187840330@ NOTE Eudes of Burgundy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT Eudes of Burgundy (1230-1266) was count of Nevers and Auxerre and the heir of Hugh IV, Duke of Burgundy.
1 CONT
1 CONT He never inherited the duchy, due to his death before his father; Burgundy was thereafter ruled by Eudes' brother Robert. Eudes married Maud of Dampierre and had three daughters:
1 CONT
1 CONT Yolande (1247-1280), married Jean-Tristan, prince of France and count of Valois (son of Louis IX of France) 
1 CONT Marguerite (1250-1308), married king Charles I of Naples 
1 CONT Joanna (1253-1271) 
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT See also
1 CONT Dukes of Burgundy family tree 
