0 @N6000000002187840088@ NOTE Bonne of Luxembourg
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Bonne of Luxemburg (also Bona) (May 20, 1315 - September 11, 1349), was the daughter of John the Blind of Luxemburg, king of Bohemia and his first wife Elizabeth of Bohemia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Bonne was married to the future John II of France on July 28, 1332. She was 17 years old, and the future king was 13.
1 CONT
1 CONT Their children were:
1 CONT
1 CONT 1) Charles V le Sage (January 21, 1338 - September 16, 1380) 
1 CONT 2) Louis (July 23, 1339 - September 20, 1384) 
1 CONT 3) Jean de Berry (November 30, 1340 - June 15, 1416) 
1 CONT 4) Philippe (January 17, 1342 - April 27, 1404) 
1 CONT 5) Jeanne (June 24, 1343 - November 3, 1373) 
1 CONT 6) Marie (September 12, 1344 - October, 1404) 
1 CONT 7) Agnès (1345 - 1349) 
1 CONT 8) Marguerite (1347 - 1352) 
1 CONT 9) Isabelle (October 1, 1348 - September 11, 1372) 
