0 @N6000000002322305105@ NOTE Charles was a leading figure of the Hungarian branch of the Angevin dynasty;
1 CONT an astute politician who won both of his thrones by triumphing over rival
1 CONT claimants. Educated in the court of Louis I of Hungary, he married his cousin
1 CONT Margaret, the daughter of Charles of Durrazo and Mary of Naples, thus
1 CONT becoming an heir to the Neopolitan throne. Later, with the death of Louis I
1 CONT of Hungary, Charles claimed the throne, and was crowned King of Hungary in
1 CONT 1385. Elizabeth, widowed queen of Louis, ordered the death of Charles in 1386.
